{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_33", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\n?? cores/bench/test/test_div_restore_step.py\n# Borrow-lookahead carry-select restoring divider\n\nImplemented the hypothesis in `rtl/div_unit.sv`. The five restoring cells\ninstantiate an acyclic `div_restore_step` helper in the same source file.\nEach cell has four independent nine-bit byte subtractions, equality borrow\npropagates, balanced (1:0)/(3:2) prefix groups, and three independent eight-bit\nincoming-borrow-one alternatives computed as `X_byte + ~D_byte`. No full-width\nsubtraction remains inside a restoring cell. The true borrow is explicitly\n`!shifted[32] && borrow_in[4]`; accepted low differences and restored shifted\nremainders feed the original recurrence.\n\nThe registers, launch magnitude conversion, six five-step groups, final\ntwo-step group, terminal sign restoration, seven RUN clocks, handshake,\nreset behavior, DONE retention and ALTOPS expressions are unchanged. Terminal\nresults still use `quotient_step[2]` and `remainder_step[2]`.\n\n`test/test_div_unit.py` adds byte-boundary, equal-byte propagation,\ngenerate/kill, near-power-of-256 and signed corner vectors while retaining\nall arithmetic, latency, capture, reset, rejected-start, consume/start and\nDONE-hold tests in real and ALTOPS builds. The added\n`test/test_div_restore_step.py` directly compares the cell against independent\nPython 33-bit arithmetic, including every combination of four local\ngenerate/propagate/kill byte classes, both shifted bit-32 values and 2,000\nrandom vectors. A direct cell test is needed because normal 32-bit division\nfrom a zero remainder does not reach shifted bit 32 during its valid steps.\n\nDeviation: the helper and its direct test are added to expose/test the\ncombinational arithmetic independently; the architecture is unchanged.\nPrimary concerns remain duplicated byte arithmetic, prefix routing and\nanother core path becoming the frequency limit.\n\nLocal validation:\n- Required full RTL Verilator lint: PASS, no warnings in real or ALTOPS mode.\n- Arithmetic, divider/ALTOPS, direct restoring-cell and EX divider tests:\n  PASS (`pytest`, five runner cases).\n- Pipeline and decoder suites: PASS (`pytest`, two runner cases), including\n  stalled memory and retirement assertions.\n- Formal: PASS on the first invocation, 53 passed / 0 failed, with automatic\n  nret=1 wrapper/config selection. No counterexample or fix attempts.\n- Cosim: initial bare make invocation used the harness default NRET=2;\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` then PASS for both ELFs, including exact\n  selftest retirement comparison with/without random stalls and stalled\n  CoreMark CRC/UART/memory-bounds checks. No harness changes.\n- Canonical CoreMark markers: PASS; 3,829,487 bracketed cycles, 10 iterations,\n  exactly matching the baseline.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`: placement option 0 reports 31.169 MHz,\n  3,944 logic cells and 904 registers. The worst path remains inside the\n  five-cell divider cascade, divisor_q[12] to quotient_q[0], 53 cells and\n  37.378 ns data arrival. Its data path has 12.647 ns cell delay and 19.170 ns\n  routing delay, so shorter native carry chains did not improve this result.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench`: PASS correctness and place-and-route;\n  placement Fmax values are 31.169, 31.920 and 31.920 MHz. Median Fmax is\n  31.920 MHz, fitness is 83.35 iterations/second, and canonical bracketed\n  cycles remain 3,829,487. This is a measured timing regression against\n  the 51.54 MHz / 134.59 iterations/second champion.\n\nThe hypothesis FAILS its performance acceptance threshold: median Gowin\nFmax is below 53.91084 MHz and fitness is below 140.78114 iterations/second.\nThe faithful arithmetic implementation is retained for the orchestrator to\nevaluate; no recurrence, latency or unrelated CPU-path changes were used to\nmask the regression. Fast formal uses ALTOPS as required; full-core deep\nformal without ALTOPS was not run. Real arithmetic was checked by directed\nand randomized divider/cell tests and stalled cosimulation.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
