{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\nImplemented the radix-4 then radix-8 divider hypothesis in rtl/div_unit.sv.\nSix normal RUN groups consume five bits each using parallel unsigned trials,\ndisjoint masked-OR remainder selection, and the specified quotient encodings.\nLaunch captures independent, explicitly widened 35-bit 3D, 5D, and 7D;\n2D, 4D, and 6D are wiring shifts of captured values. The terminal group has\nits own two restoring cells driven directly by quotient_q/remainder_q and\nretains fused sign restoration. Handshake, operand capture, seven RUN clocks,\nheld DONE, reset, and exact ALTOPS expressions are unchanged. No CPU pipeline\nor top-level interface files were changed.\n\nTests retain all existing arithmetic and protocol assertions and add an\nindependent Python integer oracle at reachable radix-4/radix-8 thresholds\n(below/equal/above), five-bit boundaries, every digit, terminal bit patterns,\nmaximum unsigned divisor multiples, both operand signs, and zero divisors.\nCaptured odd multiples are also checked against full-width Python integers.\n\nNo architectural deviations. Concern: parallel trials increase LUT usage\nand divisor fanout; launch magnitude/multiple generation and other CPU paths\nmay limit Fmax. Timing and acceptance must be measured, not inferred.\n\nLocal validation so far:\n- Full-core Verilator lint passed without warnings in real and ALTOPS builds.\n- Entire existing cocotb suite passed: 10 pytest runners, including real and\n  ALTOPS divider tests and the nine-cycle consecutive-divide / ten-cycle\n  redirect-to-divide retirement checks.\n- NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench passed: selftest RVFI versus the Python ISS\n  with and without random stalls, plus stalled CoreMark CRC/UART validation.\n- CoreMark marker start=14,091, stop=3,843,578, giving 3,829,487 bracketed\n  cycles for 10 iterations, unchanged from the champion. No out-of-bounds\n  access; seedcrc=e9f5, crclist=e714, crcmatrix=1fd7, crcstate=8e3a,\n  crcfinal=fcaf, and the required validation literal is present.\n- Vendor Gowin placements 0/1/2 measured 50.022 / 49.187 / 49.187 MHz;\n  median 49.187 MHz, 4,058 LUTs and 1,004 FFs (8 LUT-RAM, 6 BSRAM, 6 DSP).\n  Fitness is 128.442791 iter/sec, below 134.59 champion and 140.78114\n  acceptance threshold. This implementation does not meet the acceptance\n  margin, and did not reproduce the preliminary probe's 53.299 MHz median.\n  Worst option-0 path is register-file -> ID -> EX -> ALU -> memory address\n  at 25.286 ns / 13 cells; option-1/2 worst paths cross live memory, integer\n  forwarding and ALU at 25.625 ns / 18 cells. The separate terminal divider\n  path also appears at option-0 rank 17 (25.079 ns / 67 cells).\n  Reviewed all 25 reported setup paths for each placement: no launch path\n  to a captured 3D/5D/7D register appears among them. The forwarded launch\n  magnitude/multiple generation is therefore not the reported worst path;\n  the default vendor report does not expose its separate endpoint delay.\n- Local formal PASS on the first run: 53 passed, 0 failed using the\n  auto-detected nret=1 wrapper_si.sv/checks_si.cfg and ALTOPS mode. No RTL fix\n  attempts or counterexamples. This gate does not prove real arithmetic;\n  that is checked here by the independent integer-oracle divider tests and\n  real-arithmetic cosimulation. Formal-deep was not run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
