{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check; git status --short; git -C formal/riscv-formal status --short; sed -n '1,95p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\n# Implementation notes\n\nImplemented the two radix-4 body digits with narrow divider bootstrap hypothesis.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `rtl/div_unit.sv`: replaced four dependent full-width radix-2 restoring\n  cells with two radix-4 cells. Each uses parallel 35-bit trials against\n  explicitly widened D, 2D and the existing registered 34-bit 3D. Borrow\n  predicates encode the digit and disjoint masked OR terms select the\n  restored remainder.\n- Added an independent first-group bootstrap with six-bit remainders and\n  divisors, seven-bit restoring trials, and the D >= 64 bypass. The launch\n  remainder is at most three, so this first four-bit window is at most 63.\n  Bootstrap/body selection occurs only at the existing state-register inputs.\n- Retained two launch bits, seven RUN edges, first-RUN preparation of 3D,\n  the independent final two-bit/sign-restoration path, held READY behavior,\n  consume/relaunch, rejected-start behavior, reset cancellation and every\n  ALTOPS formula. EX, forwarding, pipeline control and top-level IO were\n  unchanged; no state registers or instruction latency were added.\n- `test/test_div_unit.py`: added every six-bit dividend prefix, divisors\n  around 63/64 and 0..4, signed divisor magnitudes, every radix-4 quotient\n  digit at each body position, widened multiple boundaries and signed\n  extrema. Retained random operands and all protocol tests. An independent\n  integer divmod oracle checks launch and every RUN/held-READY state,\n  captured divisor, group count and registered 3D. Verilator must expose\n  the registers for these assertions; other simulators may skip internal\n  checks when their handles are unavailable.\n\n## Deviations\n\nNo architectural deviations. The notes are in `cores/bench/` to respect the\ntarget-only edit scope. The two body cells declare their trial arrays within\ntheir generate scopes rather than adding helper modules.\n\n## Local validation\n\n- Full-core Verilator lint with the requested flags: passed without warnings\n  in both real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS builds.\n- Divider suite in real and ALTOPS modes plus existing EX divider integration\n  suite: passed (three pytest runner cases, thirteen cocotb tests). The real\n  divider suite also passed after enforcing public state-oracle visibility.\n- Formal: PASS on the first attempt, 53 passed and 0 failed, using\n  `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`.\n  Automatic nret=1 selection used the existing single-channel wrapper and\n  ALTOPS configuration. No fixes or retries were needed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: passed, two ELFs tested. Selftest matched\n  the ISS both with and without random memory stalls, and stalled CoreMark\n  passed canonical CRC/UART validation with no out-of-bounds access.\n- CoreMark start marker: cycle 14,584; stop marker: cycle 4,039,157.\n  Canonical bracket: 4,024,573 cycles for ten iterations, unchanged.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` and the same vendor flow with `--all-options`:\n  placement options 0/1/2 measured 61.966/64.558/64.558 MHz. Median Fmax is\n  64.558 MHz, with 4,476 LUT4s and 963 registers (8 LUT-RAMs, 6 BSRAMs,\n  6 DSPs). This is a 9.294% clock gain over 59.068 MHz.\n- Median Fmax times canonical iterations/cycle gives 160.4096 iterations/s,\n  above the requested 61.785128 MHz and 153.52142 iterations/s thresholds.\n- `git diff --check`: passed; tracked changes are limited to the divider\n  RTL and its allowed Python unit-test file.\n\n## Concerns and limits\n\nThe parallel subtractors increase combinational area. The median placement's\nworst reported paths now involve EX multiplication/result forwarding into OF,\ncompleted divide forwarding, and live-load forwarding into early divider\nlaunch, so those paths can constrain subsequent clock improvements. Full\nreal-arithmetic `formal-deep` was not run; the local formal gate uses ALTOPS,\nwhile exact arithmetic and recurrence were checked by the real divider\nsuite and cosimulation. The orchestrator's independent fitness evaluation\nremains authoritative.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
