{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check\ngit status --short\ncat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_ex_divider.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Implementation\n\nImplemented the hypothesis in `rtl/div_unit.sv` without changing the EX\nintegration or core IO. The accepted launch computes the unsigned leading\nnibble directly from raw `a`, including carry from zero low 28 bits for a\nnegative signed dividend. It derives the small-divisor predicate and nibble\ndirectly from raw `b`, independent of the full divisor magnitude. Four narrow\nrestoring cells seed the existing quotient/remainder bank after four bits.\nExactly four full-width restoring cells are shared across seven RUN edges;\nthe final group's completed outputs feed parallel sign restoration and DONE.\nThe single bank, zero-divisor sign rules, IDLE/RUN/DONE handshake and all four\ncaptured ALTOPS subtraction/XOR expressions are preserved.\n\nNo architectural deviations. Tests now exhaust every raw leading nibble\nagainst divisor magnitudes 0 through 17 and negative encodings, zero/nonzero\nlow-28 carry boundaries, signed extrema and all final-nibble patterns using\nindependent arithmetic oracles. Real and ALTOPS tests retain seven-edge\nlatency, changing inputs/rejected starts, held DONE, consume/relaunch and\nreset cancellation for all operations. EX tests cover forwarded ALU/load\noperands and captured RVFI payloads through completion backpressure. Pipeline\ntests cover dependent chains, x0 destinations, held WB forwarding, independent\nbus stalls, branch/JALR divide targets, memory effects and nine/ten-cycle bounds.\n\n# Local validation\n\n- Required Verilator lint: pass, no warnings in real or ALTOPS builds.\n- Divider real/ALTOPS, EX and pipeline tests: pass (4 pytest runners).\n  Reset coverage was subsequently extended to all four operations; the final\n  divider/EX rerun also passed (3 pytest runners).\n- Standalone ALU and decoder tests: pass (24 and 30 cocotb tests).\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed and 0 failed on the first attempt; no counterexample\n  or RTL fix attempts. Used unchanged `formal/run_all.sh`, auto-selected\n  `wrapper_si.sv` and `checks_si.cfg` for nret=1.\n- Cosim: pass for selftest with and without memory stalls, and CoreMark CRC\n  validation. Invoked `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: plain `make cosim`\n  initially defaults the harness build to NRET=2 and cannot compile against\n  the core's existing NRET=1 ports. No contract files were changed.\n- CoreMark: 3,829,487 marker-bracketed cycles (14,091 to 3,843,578), ten\n  iterations, ebreak reached, `oob=false`. UART reports canonical CRCs\n  e9f5/e714/1fd7/8e3a/fcaf and `Correct operation validated.`\n- Gowin EDA all placements: 41.473 / 42.831 / 42.831 MHz; median 42.831 MHz.\n  Logic 3,494, registers 904, LUT-RAM 8, BSRAM 6, DSP 6.\n\n# Concerns\n\nThis implementation does not meet the acceptance margin. CoreMark cycles\nare unchanged, but median timing is below the champion's 51.54 MHz and the\nrequired approximately 53.914 MHz. The worst path is registered remainder\nthrough the final four restoring cells and sign correction to result bits\n28-30. A forwarded load-to-launch-prefix path is also among the worst paths\nfor placements 1 and 2. The measured median implies approximately 111.85\niterations/sec, below 140.78114. The hypothesis is left implemented for the\norchestrator's unchanged gates; no improvement is claimed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
