{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_117", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --stat; git status --short; git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " cores/bench/rtl/core.sv              |  32 ++++++++-\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv          |  39 +++++++++--\n cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv       |  10 +--\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv          |  31 +++++----\n cores/bench/test/test_ex_divider.py  |  93 +++++++++++++++++++++++--\n cores/bench/test/test_fetch_queue.py |  72 +++++++++++++++----\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py    | 130 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\n cores/bench/test/test_predictor.py   |  48 +++++++++++++\n 8 files changed, 401 insertions(+), 54 deletions(-)\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_ex_divider.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_fetch_queue.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_predictor.py\n# Registered predictor squash\n\nImplemented one synchronous `squash_q` flop in `core.sv`, capturing the accepted EX correction on every non-reset edge. Correction installs the full recovery PC immediately. IF retains both queue payloads and occupancy on that edge; the next cycle ignores stale entries and rebuilds the queue from the corrected-PC bus word. PC control and queue control use separate register blocks. An unavailable target clears stale occupancy and leaves the corrected PC for retry; an unconsumed available target is retained exactly once.\n\nHazards consume registered squash. ID/OF accepts a fresh target during squash, OF/EX validity is flushed, and operand acceptance is suppressed. EX captures its ordinary wide payload with validity killed, disables ordinary and early forwarding producers, load producers, training and correction, and prevents early/fallback divider launches and divide waiting. The existing exclusion of early divider launch behind valid EX branches or jumps remains. Divider arithmetic, latency, consume/publication behavior, predictor counters, training boundary, raw predecode, retirement, top-level ports and nret=1 are unchanged.\n\nAdded executable RTL assertions for recovery ownership, the\n…[2527 of 5599 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e126288dc12cca31]…\n7 MHz, and fitness 163.018536 is below the required 169.0336. Correctness and cycle-count reproduction pass, but this implementation does not establish the requested fitness gain. Equivalent fetch-control formulations were measured at median 61.851, 65.608 and 59.947 MHz; the best verified implementation is retained. Remaining critical paths include multiplier operand/result forwarding and divider launch/operand paths. Divider arithmetic or pipeline latency was not altered to pursue additional timing changes.\n\nThe only implementation restructuring beyond adding squash is splitting IF's PC and queue state into separate sequential blocks. The immediate correction still freezes stale queue state until squash, all reset/recovery priorities are preserved, and no target register or output-address mux was added. No wrappers, formal definitions/depths, evaluation tools or other cores were modified. The formal framework and unchanged runner were copied under `$TMPDIR` to avoid writing to the shared upstream checkout.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
