{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"agent_message","text":"The local launch-control prototype preserved correctness but still missed the timing target. The next test removes `start` from the divider’s wide register-enable path: operand registers can refresh while idle, while `start` still controls request acceptance and the existing seven-clock schedule. Completed results remain held until consumption."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r10s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r10s0',\n'title':'Remove late divider-start control from wide operand register enables',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''LESSONS.md is absent. The champion scores 161.60 iter/sec at 65.036 MHz median Gowin Fmax with 4,024,573 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path begins at an OF/EX PC flop, crosses the ALU and OF hazard logic, then reaches divider remainder state through div_start. Detailed vendor timing confirms that late start/acceptance logic gates the wide divider launch register bank. The successful radix-4 body and terminal retiming has made this launch-enable path competitive with the recurrence. Prior micro_opt divider rewrites and forwarding-match predecode did not address this particular control fanout. Removing start from the wide datapath enables can shorten the observed path while retaining the same pipeline, arithmetic and acceptance schedule.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Separate divider request-state transitions from speculative operand-register refresh. Keep the existing state/group FSM exactly: start accepts only in IDLE or in READY with consume, enters RUN at group zero, executes seven RUN edges, enters held READY, and consumes normally. Keep busy/result_valid definitions and the original accepted-start predicate. Do not alter EX integration, early/fallback launch, payload capture, divider arithmetic, grouping, result publication or instruction latency.\n\nIn a separate sequential datapath block, capture the existing launch seed, divisor magnitude, quotient/remainder signs and operation selection whenever the PRE-EDGE state is IDLE, regardless of start. Also capture those same input-derived fields on any READY-and-consume edge, regardless of whether a replacement start is asserted. Use precisely state_q == IDLE || (state_q == READY && consume) as this wide capture condition: never retain a start term in this enable or its data mux. The actual accepted-launch edge is always included, so that edge still captures its current a/b/op exactly; an earlier idle refresh must never substitute for current launch operands. Refreshing invalid idle state produces no valid result, retirement or architectural side effect. This is local enable refactoring within existing registers, with no added preparation stage or state bank.\n\nOn every RUN edge preserve the existing bootstrap or two-cell radix-4 updates verbatim, including L+1 preparation of widened 3D. Do not refresh any launch operand or sign in RUN, even if start or consume is spuriously asserted. When READY and consume is low, hold every datapath field and the complete terminal result, including when rejected starts and changing live inputs occur. At READY with consume and start, capture new operands and restart on that same edge exactly as before. At READY with consume and no start, state becomes IDLE and the now-invalid datapath may refresh safely. Reset overrides all conditions and clears both blocks as before. Do not clear triple_divisor_q during idle refresh; its existing reset and group-zero update remain sufficient.\n\nApply the same refresh enable to ALTOPS operand-expression capture, retaining each exact subtraction/XOR formula and the identical seven-RUN/result-valid timing. Real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU results, zero-divisor handling, signed extrema, INT_MIN/-1, held completion, rejected starts, reset cancellation and consume/relaunch remain exact. EX must continue to capture metadata only on an accepted div_start and publish exactly once. Preserve nine-cycle divide spacing, ten-cycle redirect-to-divide assertions, load interlocks, dmem stalls, wrong-path suppression, held-WB forwarding, decoder default-illegal rules, nret=1 IO and strictly increasing RVFI order.\n\nThe intended gain is removing the late start/acceptance cone from the high-fanout launch-data enable and replacing it with direct registered-state decode. The state FSM still times start into its few state/control flops; launch magnitude, feedback, terminal forwarding and placement may become limits. Extra idle switching is the main cost. The eight-percent forecast is provisional pending candidate measurements. Require unchanged real/ALTOPS divider and pipeline tests, formal and stalled full-RVFI cosim, canonical CoreMark CRCs/UART/address bounds and marker-bracketed cycles. Acceptance requires measured fitness above 169.0336 iter/sec; at unchanged cycles median Gowin Fmax must exceed approximately 68.028 MHz.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Split state/group updates from datapath updates. Preserve accepted-start state transitions, but refresh existing operand/sign/operation registers on IDLE or READY-and-consume without a start-dependent wide enable. Retain all RUN arithmetic, widened multiple preparation, READY holds, reset values and real/ALTOPS schedules.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Retain exact arithmetic, seven-clock completion, held result, rejected-start, reset and consume/relaunch assertions in both arithmetic modes. Add multiple idle edges with changing a/b/op before a distinct actual launch, consumption without replacement followed by a distinct launch, and changing inputs during RUN/held READY. Use an independent RV32M oracle to ensure only actual accepted-launch operands determine valid results.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'''Verify idle operand refresh cannot issue or publish an instruction, capture wrong RVFI metadata, or alter accepted early/fallback launch timing. Exercise changing forwarding data before acceptance, reset in every phase, held READY and one-time publication under memory backpressure; preserve all existing assertions.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Exercise unrelated ALU/load instructions while divider state is idle, then DIV/REM from fresh forwarded operands, consecutive dependent divides, wrong-path divides and reset/stall transitions. Retain exact source/result/PC/order, side-effect and nine/ten-cycle progress checks.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r10s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r10s0',\n'title':'Remove late divider-start control from wide operand register enables',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''LESSONS.md is absent. The champion scores 161.60 iter/sec at 65.036 MHz median Gowin Fmax with 4,024,573 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path begins at an OF/EX PC flop, crosses the ALU and OF hazard logic, then reaches divider remainder state through div_start. Detailed vendor timing confirms that late start/acceptance logic gates the wide divider launch register bank. The successful radix-4 body and terminal retiming has made this launch-enable path competitive with the recurrence. Prior micro_opt divider rewrites and forwarding-match predecode did not address this particular control fanout. Removing start from the wide datapath enables can shorten the observed path while retaining the same pipeline, arithmetic and acceptance schedule.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Separate divider request-state transitions from speculative operand-register refresh. Keep the existing state/group FSM exactly: start accepts only in IDLE or in READY with consume, enters RUN at group zero, executes seven RUN edges, enters held READY, and consumes normally. Keep busy/result_valid definitions and the original accepted-start predicate. Do not alter EX integration, early/fallback launch, payload capture, divider arithmetic, grouping, result publication or instruction latency.\n\nIn a separate sequential datapath block, capture the existing launch seed, divisor magnitude, quotient/remainder signs and operation selection whenever the PRE-EDGE state is IDLE, regardless of start. Also capture those same input-derived fields on any READY-and-consume edge, regardless of whether a replacement start is asserted. Use precisely state_q == IDLE || (state_q == READY && consume) as this wide capture condition: never retain a start term in this enable or its data mux. The actual accepted-launch edge is always included, so that edge still captures its current a/b/op exactly; an earlier idle refresh must never substitute for current launch operands. Refreshing invalid idle state produces no valid result, retirement or architectural side effect. This is local enable refactoring within existing registers, with no added preparation stage or state bank.\n\nOn every RUN edge preserve the existing bootstrap or two-cell radix-4 updates verbatim, including L+1 preparation of widened 3D. Do not refresh any launch operand or sign in RUN, even if start or consume is spuriously asserted. When READY and consume is low, hold every datapath field and the complete terminal result, including when rejected starts and changing live inputs occur. At READY with consume and start, capture new operands and restart on that same edge exactly as before. At READY with consume and no start, state becomes IDLE and the now-invalid datapath may refresh safely. Reset overrides all conditions and clears both blocks as before. Do not clear triple_divisor_q during idle refresh; its existing reset and group-zero update remain sufficient.\n\nApply the same refresh enable to ALTOPS operand-expression capture, retaining each exact subtraction/XOR formula and the identical seven-RUN/result-valid timing. Real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU results, zero-divisor handling, signed extrema, INT_MIN/-1, held completion, rejected starts, reset cancellation and consume/relaunch remain exact. EX must continue to capture metadata only on an accepted div_start and publish exactly once. Preserve nine-cycle divide spacing, ten-cycle redirect-to-divide assertions, load interlocks, dmem stalls, wrong-path suppression, held-WB forwarding, decoder default-illegal rules, nret=1 IO and strictly increasing RVFI order.\n\nThe intended gain is removing the late start/acceptance cone from the high-fanout launch-data enable and replacing it with direct registered-state decode. The state FSM still times start into its few state/control flops; launch magnitude, feedback, terminal forwarding and placement may become limits. Extra idle switching is the main cost. The eight-percent forecast is provisional pending candidate measurements. Require unchanged real/ALTOPS divider and pipeline tests, formal and stalled full-RVFI cosim, canonical CoreMark CRCs/UART/address bounds and marker-bracketed cycles. Acceptance requires measured fitness above 169.0336 iter/sec; at unchanged cycles median Gowin Fmax must exceed approximately 68.028 MHz.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Split state/group updates from datapath updates. Preserve accepted-start state transitions, but refresh existing operand/sign/operation registers on IDLE or READY-and-consume without a start-dependent wide enable. Retain all RUN arithmetic, widened multiple preparation, READY holds, reset values and real/ALTOPS schedules.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Retain exact arithmetic, seven-clock completion, held result, rejected-start, reset and consume/relaunch assertions in both arithmetic modes. Add multiple idle edges with changing a/b/op before a distinct actual launch, consumption without replacement followed by a distinct launch, and changing inputs during RUN/held READY. Use an independent RV32M oracle to ensure only actual accepted-launch operands determine valid results.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'''Verify idle operand refresh cannot issue or publish an instruction, capture wrong RVFI metadata, or alter accepted early/fallback launch timing. Exercise changing forwarding data before acceptance, reset in every phase, held READY and one-time publication under memory backpressure; preserve all existing assertions.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Exercise unrelated ALU/load instructions while divider state is idle, then DIV/REM from fresh forwarded operands, consecutive dependent divides, wrong-path divides and reset/stall transitions. Retain exact source/result/PC/order, side-effect and nine/ten-cycle progress checks.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated and schema-valid: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r10s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
