{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_69", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r10s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r10s0',\n'title':'Select OF forwarding sources directly with disjoint one-hot masks',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''LESSONS.md is absent. The champion measures 161.60 iter/sec at 65.036 MHz median Gowin Fmax and 4,024,573 bracketed CoreMark cycles. The latest critical path crosses EX/ALU, OF and early divider launch, rather than only the divider feedback cells. Prior micro_opt forwarding-match predecode regressed on the older pipeline, and prior merged EX/ALU mux experiments also regressed. The current six-stage operand-register boundary provides a different target: both OF forwarding networks still encode youngest-writer priority into two-bit selectors and then decode those selectors into wide data muxes. Direct source masks can remove this encoding/decoding round trip while preserving every existing register and acceptance edge.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only the forwarding selection representation inside operand_stage with direct disjoint source masks. Preserve the same source comparisons and youngest-writer priority, but do not form a two-bit fwd selector and compare or decode it again for data selection. For each nonzero source address compute E = ex_w_en && ex_rd \"'!= 0 && ex_rd == source, M = mem_w_en && mem_rd != 0 && mem_rd == source, and W = wb_w_en && wb_rd != 0 && wb_rd == source. For source x0 force E/M/W false and retain the existing explicit zero at capture. Select normal EX using E && ex_normal_w_en, completed DIV using E && !ex_normal_w_en, MEM using !E && M, WB using !E && !M && W, and RF using !E && !M && !W. Form the resolved word as the OR of these five individually masked values. Derive masks in parallel from address hits; avoid an encoded priority mux followed by another decoder.\n\nFor the independent early-divider network, compute its own E from ex_early_w_en and select normal EX, MEM, WB and RF with E, !E && M, !E && !M && W and !E && !M && !W. Express this four-source data selection as masked OR too, replacing its case on an encoded selector. Keep the completed-divider result physically absent from this early mux. Do not change ex_early_w_en, producer qualification, alignment checks, the normal_result/producer_result separation, memory-load formatting, WB data selection or RF write-first behavior. A valid younger producer must retain priority during every hold; invalid/trapping producers and rd=x0 must never become sources. Recompute masks while OF is held, and sample data only at the original accepting edge.\n\nKeep the separate normal and early masks for both architectural sources, existing raw RVFI operands, load-use interlock, early_payload, OF/EX register layout, payload capture enable and validity-only flush behavior. Leave forward_unit available for standalone clients; operand_stage can implement direct masks locally rather than extending unrelated interfaces. This is one local forwarding mux optimization with no new stage, register bank, speculative state, cache, predictor or arithmetic rewrite.\n\nPreserve exact real and ALTOPS division behavior and seven-RUN schedule, accepted early/fallback launch, held READY, single publication, nine-cycle divide spacing, ten-cycle redirect-to-divide checks, all memory stalls, wrong-path suppression, held-WB provenance, decoder default-illegal rules, alignment traps, nret=1 IO and +1 RVFI retirement order. No existing correctness or progress assertion may be relaxed.\n\nA scratch implementation of these direct masks passes the existing operand-stage, EX-divider and pipeline pytest runners. Full-RVFI selftest cosim passes both without stalls and with independent instruction/data stalls. Its canonical -O3, 2K, ten-iteration stalled CoreMark run passes all five CRCs, the validation literal, clean EBREAK termination and address bounds; start/stop markers differ by exactly 4,024,573 cycles, equal to the champion. These are local correctness/cycle checks; full formal remains required and FPGA timing is not yet a measured improvement. The forecast is six percent with low confidence because synthesis may already simplify some selector logic, mask fanout can increase, and other launch/recurrence paths may limit Fmax. Require the final implementation'\"'s unchanged formal, unit and stalled cosim gates and median Gowin timing across all placement options. At unchanged cycles acceptance requires Fmax above approximately 68.028 MHz and fitness above 169.0336 iter/sec.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'''Replace the encoded-selector instances and normal/early selector decoding with explicit youngest-writer-qualified disjoint masks and parallel masked-OR data selection for both sources. Preserve all ports, register fields, independent early-divider isolation, x0 handling, producer priority, load-use controls and acceptance/hold/flush behavior.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'''Retain existing forwarding/interlock checks and add exhaustive source-presence combinations, simultaneous matching producers, different source addresses, x0, invalid/trapping qualifications and completed-DIV isolation. Assert the selected value is the independently modeled youngest eligible writer through holds and subsequent acceptance.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Exercise dependent ALU/MUL/DIV/load chains with both sources matching, younger MEM over held WB, load-use bubbles, branch flushes and independent bus stalls. Retain all exact RVFI source/result/PC/order, memory-side-effect and nine/ten-cycle progress assertions.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
