{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_58", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r11s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Share one explicitly signed 33-bit multiplier across RV32M products\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz with\n  4,024,573 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its latest worst Gowin\n  path starts at an OF/EX operand and traverses EX/OF, with the endpoint\n  named u_alu/mul_uu_63_s0. The ALU expresses three separate products\n  for signed/signed, unsigned/unsigned and signed/unsigned operands,\n  and the timed design uses six DSP resources. Divider retiming has\n  already removed the early-launch arithmetic chain; another forwarding\n  mask rewrite is unpromising because r10s0 regressed 3.76 percent.\n  LESSONS.md is absent, and the micro_opt history contains no shared\n  multiplier attempt. A local multiplier rewrite can reduce product\n  selection and physical congestion without adding CoreMark cycles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only the real multiplication datapath in alu.sv with one\n  shared signed 33-by-33 product. Let A and B be the existing product_a\n  and product_b, retaining SEPARATE_MUL_OPERANDS and its isolation from\n  live memory load forwarding. Set sign_a when op is ALU_MULH or\n  ALU_MULHSU, and sign_b only when op is ALU_MULH. Declare signed\n  33-bit operands ax={sign_a && A[31], A} and\n  bx={sign_b && B[31], B}, and a signed 66-bit product p=ax*bx.\n  Use p[31:0] for ALU_MUL and p[63:32] for ALU_MULH, ALU_MULHU and\n  ALU_MULHSU. Explicit signed declarations and widths are essential:\n  0-prefixed operands must stay positive even when their bit 31 is one.\n  Bits 65:64 are unused extension bits and must not enter selection.\n  A 33-bit signed representation covers both all RV32 unsigned values\n  and every signed RV32 value exactly, so the selected product bits\n  implement the four RV32M multiplication operations without magnitude\n  preprocessing, post-product subtraction or additional carry chains.\n\n  Delete the three independent real product expressions. Group the\n  three high-half op cases around the same product slice, lea\n…[1615 of 4687 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fd95e99ccef18895]…\n three real signedness-specific products with one\n      explicitly signed 33-by-33, 66-bit product, sign-prefix operands\n      according to MULH/MULHSU, and share its high-half result cases.\n      Preserve separate multiply operands, ALTOPS and every other ALU\n      operation and interface.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Add independent integer-reference directed and randomized checks\n      for all four multiply operations and sign/high-half boundaries.\n      Exercise default and SEPARATE_MUL_OPERANDS elaborations, unrelated\n      nonmultiply operands, and consecutive changes of signedness.\n      Retain all existing arithmetic assertions and ALTOPS formulas.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Verify adjacent dependent low/high multiply chains, both matching\n      source operands, signedness changes, load-to-multiply interlocks,\n      held-WB forwarding and memory stalls against exact RVFI results,\n      operands and order without changing instruction latency checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
