{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_80", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r11s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Remove branch comparison from OF operand capture controls\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz and 4,024,573\n  bracketed CoreMark cycles. A local vendor retest reproduces its\n  placement-0 Fmax of 69.480 MHz. The full timing report reveals that\n  the worst path runs from an OF/EX source through the 32-bit branch\n  comparison, branch recovery/producer controls, and OF operand\n  selection to a multiplier input register absorbed into a DSP.\n  The multiplier is an endpoint rather than the arithmetic bottleneck\n  on that path. LESSONS.md is absent; previous direct forwarding masks\n  regressed, while predictor squash changes also failed acceptance.\n  Shortening the existing operand capture controls is a local micro_opt\n  opportunity that does not need a prediction or pipeline change.\nhypothesis: |\n  Remove the current branch comparator's two unnecessary dependencies\n  from OF operand capture. First, in operand_stage retain reset, all\n  forwarding selection, x0 handling and the validity process, but use\n  only in.valid && !stall to enable the wide payload capture, instead\n  of accept && in.valid && !stall && !flush. An accepted redirect still\n  clears OF/EX.valid with the current priority on that same edge;\n  accept still qualifies newly valid instructions. A younger payload\n  may be sampled on a redirect, but its valid bit is zero and no EX,\n  divider, memory, register-write or retirement action may use it.\n  Keeping in.valid on payload capture avoids making OF's wide enable\n  identical to ID's, which can change vendor register/RAM inference.\n  Keep every payload field held when stall is asserted, including\n  simultaneous stall/flush; never change the validity-only load bubble.\n\n  Second, compute normal_w_en directly from ex_accept,\n  in.ctrl.reg_write, !in.ctrl.is_illegal, !in.ctrl.mem_read and\n  !misalign_jump. Stop routing it through ctrl_with_trap, whose\n  misalign_branch term depends on the late branch comparison. Every\n  legal br\n…[2385 of 5457 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:195571f64029eabb]…\n    description: |\n      Derive normal EX writer eligibility from original decoded writer\n      controls and misalign_jump, excluding the nonwriting branch's\n      misalignment comparison from this forwarding-control cone.\n      Preserve full branch/jump trap correction in EX/MEM and RVFI.\n  - file: test/test_operand_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Retain all producer priority, x0, accepted source and payload-hold\n      assertions. Cover flush with and without stall, rejected validity\n      and recovery followed by a fresh accepted payload; enforce zero\n      validity after kills and exact stall-held payload behavior.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise misaligned taken branches and misaligned JAL/JALR with\n      dependent target operands and consumers, occupied fetch queues,\n      wrong-path stores/divides and independent bus stalls. Preserve\n      exact traps, RVFI sources/results/PC/order, memory-side-effect\n      checks, load-use schedules and the ten-cycle progress bound.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
