m_0_0_0_s -> dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_mem > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex\n  path 3: 26.409 ns, 16 cells, dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s -> dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\n          through: clock_ibuf > cpu/u_mem > cpu/u_ex > cpu/u_ex/u_alu > cpu/u_ex\n  full report: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_1-sol_xhigh-v2-nolessons-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261004-001-r3s0-hypgen/cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p2/impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\nscore Fmax (median): 47.35 MHz\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_67", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r3s0.yaml')\nx={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r3s0',\n'title':'Remove load-use bubbles with ready-qualified MEM-to-EX forwarding',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 108.26 at 48.625 MHz with 4,491,485 bracketed CoreMark cycles. The successful five-step divider leaves several competing arithmetic and control timing paths. Previous micro_opt radix-4 trials did not beat this champion, and local control-mux experiments failed to clear the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold. LESSONS.md is absent. A throughput improvement is therefore more promising than another small clock-only change. The current hazard unit always inserts a bubble behind a dependent load because EX/MEM forwarding exposes only the effective address. The memory interface actually supplies load data combinationally during MEM, and dmem backpressure already holds the dependent EX instruction until the load can complete.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add one local MEM-to-EX forwarding path for completed loads, preserving the pipeline stages and retirement schedule for all other instructions. Expose the existing mem_stage sign/zero-extended load_data as part of a forwarding value: select load_data for mem_to_reg, otherwise the existing EX/MEM alu_result. Route this value into EX's existing highest-priority EX/MEM forwarding input. The forwarding producer must be valid, have a nonzero matching destination, and retain reg_write after memory-alignment trap correction. Never forward the effective address as a load result or make a trapped/misaligned load a producer.\n\nRemove the unconditional ID/EX-load versus fetched-source bubble once the new bypass is connected. A load enters MEM while its immediately following consumer enters EX. When io_dmemReady is high, the formatted load result feeds the consumer before the same accepting edge that moves the load to MEM/WB and the consumer to EX/MEM. When it is low, the existing dStall mechanism holds PC, ID/EX and EX/MEM, clears only MEM/WB.valid, preserves WB forwarding provenance, and suppresses redirect and divider launch. The consumer must never advance or launch a divide from unaccepted data. Thus one producer can serve ALU, branch/JALR, store-address/store-data and divide consumers without a new stage, queue, speculative state or architectural latency change. Preserve younger EX/MEM priority over held WB, source x0, simultaneous rs1/rs2 matches and all RVFI source values.\n\nRetain the seven-clock real/ALTOPS divider, captured forwarded operands, held DONE behavior, all decoder legality rules, trap behavior, nret=1 IO, strictly increasing retirement order, and redirect-over-fetch-stall priority. No evaluation or formal configuration changes are permitted. The improvement must come from fewer genuine load-use and conservative source-index bubbles. The longer dmem-to-EX-to-branch/multiplier path is the principal risk: validate the final design with median vendor Fmax times marker-bracketed CoreMark iterations/cycle, rather than accepting an IPC gain alone. Run the existing formal, cosim and CRC gates, and preserve the ten-cycle zero-wait liveness bound.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':10,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Expose a combinational forwarding value using the existing formatted load_data for loads and alu_result otherwise, plus a producer-valid/write-enable qualified by in.valid and ctrl_with_trap.reg_write. Reuse the existing alignment and sign/zero extension logic. Preserve bus enables, MEM/WB holding and RVFI data.'''} ,\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire the MEM forwarding value to ex_stage.fwd_ex_mem and the trap-corrected producer qualification to forward_unit.ex_mem_w_en. Disable the old unconditional load-use bubble only after the bypass is connected. Keep all global memory/divider stalls, redirect gating, held-WB forwarding provenance and top-level ports.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'''Remove the mandatory one-cycle load-use bubble for dependencies covered by MEM forwarding; simplify only the resulting unused dependency-control cone. Preserve imem bubble behavior, dmem holds, divider holds, redirect priorities and WB valid-only clearing. No speculative consumption while dmem is unready.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Check immediate LW/LB/LBU/LH/LHU consumers with all offsets and sign cases, both operands matching the load destination, ALU/branch/JALR/store/divide consumers, and x0 destinations. On zero-wait loads assert adjacent load/consumer retirements where their own instruction latency permits, while maintaining exact PCs, source values, results, memory effects, traps and RVFI order. Exercise long and random dmem stalls, imem stalls on redirect, older WB forwarding with a held consumer, and trapped misaligned loads that must not forward or write a destination. Preserve the existing ten-cycle zero-wait progress bound.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'''Cover a divide/rem launch whose operand arrives through the new load forwarding input, with older-load dmem stalls before launch and input changes after accepted launch. Preserve exact seven-clock completion, single publication, RVFI operand capture and held-DONE assertions.'''}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=80))\nprint(p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_67", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r3s0.yaml')\nx={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r3s0',\n'title':'Remove load-use bubbles with ready-qualified MEM-to-EX forwarding',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 108.26 at 48.625 MHz with 4,491,485 bracketed CoreMark cycles. The successful five-step divider leaves several competing arithmetic and control timing paths. Previous micro_opt radix-4 trials did not beat this champion, and local control-mux experiments failed to clear the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold. LESSONS.md is absent. A throughput improvement is therefore more promising than another small clock-only change. The current hazard unit always inserts a bubble behind a dependent load because EX/MEM forwarding exposes only the effective address. The memory interface actually supplies load data combinationally during MEM, and dmem backpressure already holds the dependent EX instruction until the load can complete.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add one local MEM-to-EX forwarding path for completed loads, preserving the pipeline stages and retirement schedule for all other instructions. Expose the existing mem_stage sign/zero-extended load_data as part of a forwarding value: select load_data for mem_to_reg, otherwise the existing EX/MEM alu_result. Route this value into EX's existing highest-priority EX/MEM forwarding input. The forwarding producer must be valid, have a nonzero matching destination, and retain reg_write after memory-alignment trap correction. Never forward the effective address as a load result or make a trapped/misaligned load a producer.\n\nRemove the unconditional ID/EX-load versus fetched-source bubble once the new bypass is connected. A load enters MEM while its immediately following consumer enters EX. When io_dmemReady is high, the formatted load result feeds the consumer before the same accepting edge that moves the load to MEM/WB and the consumer to EX/MEM. When it is low, the existing dStall mechanism holds PC, ID/EX and EX/MEM, clears only MEM/WB.valid, preserves WB forwarding provenance, and suppresses redirect and divider launch. The consumer must never advance or launch a divide from unaccepted data. Thus one producer can serve ALU, branch/JALR, store-address/store-data and divide consumers without a new stage, queue, speculative state or architectural latency change. Preserve younger EX/MEM priority over held WB, source x0, simultaneous rs1/rs2 matches and all RVFI source values.\n\nRetain the seven-clock real/ALTOPS divider, captured forwarded operands, held DONE behavior, all decoder legality rules, trap behavior, nret=1 IO, strictly increasing retirement order, and redirect-over-fetch-stall priority. No evaluation or formal configuration changes are permitted. The improvement must come from fewer genuine load-use and conservative source-index bubbles. The longer dmem-to-EX-to-branch/multiplier path is the principal risk: validate the final design with median vendor Fmax times marker-bracketed CoreMark iterations/cycle, rather than accepting an IPC gain alone. Run the existing formal, cosim and CRC gates, and preserve the ten-cycle zero-wait liveness bound.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':10,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Expose a combinational forwarding value using the existing formatted load_data for loads and alu_result otherwise, plus a producer-valid/write-enable qualified by in.valid and ctrl_with_trap.reg_write. Reuse the existing alignment and sign/zero extension logic. Preserve bus enables, MEM/WB holding and RVFI data.'''} ,\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire the MEM forwarding value to ex_stage.fwd_ex_mem and the trap-corrected producer qualification to forward_unit.ex_mem_w_en. Disable the old unconditional load-use bubble only after the bypass is connected. Keep all global memory/divider stalls, redirect gating, held-WB forwarding provenance and top-level ports.'''},\n{'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'''Remove the mandatory one-cycle load-use bubble for dependencies covered by MEM forwarding; simplify only the resulting unused dependency-control cone. Preserve imem bubble behavior, dmem holds, divider holds, redirect priorities and WB valid-only clearing. No speculative consumption while dmem is unready.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Check immediate LW/LB/LBU/LH/LHU consumers with all offsets and sign cases, both operands matching the load destination, ALU/branch/JALR/store/divide consumers, and x0 destinations. On zero-wait loads assert adjacent load/consumer retirements where their own instruction latency permits, while maintaining exact PCs, source values, results, memory effects, traps and RVFI order. Exercise long and random dmem stalls, imem stalls on redirect, older WB forwarding with a held consumer, and trapped misaligned loads that must not forward or write a destination. Preserve the existing ten-cycle zero-wait progress bound.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'''Cover a divide/rem launch whose operand arrives through the new load forwarding input, with older-load dmem stalls before launch and input changes after accepted launch. Preserve exact seven-clock completion, single publication, RVFI operand capture and held-DONE assertions.'''}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(x,sort_keys=False,width=80))\nprint(p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r3s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
