{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='micro_opt' and d.get('id','').endswith(('r2s0','r3s0','r4s0')):\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-001-r2s0 Shorten the registered divider with four parallel-trial radix-4 steps\nReplace the eight radix-2 restoring steps in each div_unit RUN clock\nwith four radix-4 steps, each producing two quotient bits. Preserve the\nexisting launch, four RUN clocks, one SIGN clock, and held DONE result\nschedule exactly in both real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS builds. This is a\nlocal arithmetic rewrite: the pipeline and divider handshake keep their\ncurrent behavior, and CoreMark instruction throughput should stay the\nsame while the divider's register-to-register path becomes shorter.\n\nAt launch capture the unsigned divisor magnitude D and the widened\nmultiples 2D and 3D. All multiples must be 34 bits; form 3D with an\nexplicitly widened addition during launch rather than recomputing it\ninside the RUN recurrence. Each digit step forms the 34-bit trial\nT = {remainder[31:0], quotient[31:30]}. Compute T-D, T-2D, and T-3D in\nparallel as 35-bit zero-extended subtractions. Their bit 34 supplies\nborrow, so no separate compare followed by subtract is needed. With\nok1, ok2, and ok3 denoting no-borrow for D, 2D, and 3D respectively,\nappend the quotient digit {ok2, ok3 | (ok1 & !ok2)}. Select the low\n32 remainder bits using disjoint masks !ok1, ok1 & !ok2,\nok2 & !ok3, and ok3 on T and the three difference results. Express\nselection as parallel masked OR, avoiding a serial priority mux chain.\nShift the quotient left by two