{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r5s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-001-r5s0\ntitle: \"Parallel block-borrow lookahead in the existing restoring divider\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  No LESSONS.md exists. The current champion scores 126.34 iter/sec at\n  50.352 MHz with 3,985,515 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst\n  Gowin path is 25.608 ns across 164 cells, from quotient_q to quotient_q\n  inside div_unit. The same five-step restoring recurrence was the\n  critical path in r3s1. Earlier radix-4 and mixed-radix rewrites reached\n  51.856 and 52.657 MHz but enlarged the arithmetic and moved the limit\n  to integer/load forwarding. A different local approach is to shorten\n  each subtraction's borrow dependency while keeping the current radix,\n  registers, seven RUN clocks, and instruction throughput.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the five full-width ripple subtraction/borrow cones inside\n  div_unit with explicit parallel block subtraction and prefix borrow\n  lookahead. Keep the existing unsigned restoring radix-2 recurrence,\n  six groups of five bits and terminal group of two bits exactly. This\n  is one combinational arithmetic optimization within existing register\n  boundaries; no new pipeline stage, operation latency, predictor,\n  forwarding policy, divider algorithm or memory behavior is proposed.\n\n  For each bit step form the 33-bit unsigned trial\n  T={remainder_step,quotient_step[31]}. Partition T[31:0] and divisor_q\n  into four eight-bit blocks. In parallel for each block j compute the\n  explicitly widened nine-bit differences z0_j={0,T_j}-{0,D_j} and\n  z1_j={0,T_j}-{0,D_j}-9'd1. Express these as independent arithmetic\n  cones, rather than deriving z1 by decrementing z0. Define local borrow\n  generate G_j=z0_j[8] and propagate P_j=(T_j==D_j). Starting with B0=0,\n  derive B1=G0, B2=G1|(P1&G0),\n  B3=G2|(P2&G1)|(P2&P1&G0), and\n  B4=G3|(P3&G2)|(P3&P2&G1)|(P3&P2&P1&G0).\n  Write these as parallel prefix expressions, not a serial block-borrow\n  loop. Select each eight-bit difference from z0_j[7:0] or z1_j[7:0]\n  using its incoming B_j, and concatenate the four sel\n…[2238 of 5310 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b1a53712dc7ff5fe]…\ns:\n  - file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace only the real five restoring-step subtraction cones with\n      four parallel eight-bit candidate blocks, local borrow generate\n      and equality propagate, explicit prefix borrow equations and\n      selected difference blocks. Reuse the cells for terminal steps.\n      Keep all registers, radix-2 recurrence, sign handling, interface,\n      seven-clock real/ALTOPS schedule and DONE/consume behavior.\n  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n    description: |\n      Add independent arithmetic checks for cross-block borrow propagation\n      and termination, equal blocks, high trial bits, and boundary values\n      near 2^8, 2^16, 2^24 and 2^32. Exercise these patterns through all\n      four divide/remainder operations and both operand signs, including\n      zero divisors and INT_MIN/-1. Preserve the existing exact seven-clock\n      completion, operand capture, rejected starts, held result, reset\n      and simultaneous consume/relaunch assertions in both builds.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
