{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(l) for l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\nfor x in rows:\n print(x['id'], x.get('category'), x.get('outcome'), 'fitness',x.get('fitness'),'fmax',x.get('fmax_mhz'),'cycles',x.get('cycles'), 'title:',x.get('title'))\n if x.get('category')=='micro_opt' and 'r1s' not in x['id']:\n  h=x.get('hypothesis',{})\n  if isinstance(h,dict): print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis',''))\n  print('NOTES:',x.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-0e2f75b micro_opt improvement fitness 12.12 fmax 5.442 cycles 4491485 title: Baseline retest for cores/bench\nPROPOSAL: \nNOTES: \nhyp-20261004-001-r1s0 micro_opt regression fitness 13.32 fmax 5.984 cycles 4491485 title: Share a radix-4 combinational divider across RV32M divide and remainder\nhyp-20261004-002-r1s1 structural improvement fitness 71.55 fmax 32.136 cycles 4491485 title: Replace combinational division with a bounded multicycle EX divider\nhyp-20261004-003-r1s2 predictor regression fitness 12.59 fmax 5.292 cycles 4201766 title: Fetch-time bimodal prediction removes taken-branch bubbles\nhyp-20261004-001-r2s0 micro_opt regression fitness 94.28 fmax 42.346 cycles 4491485 title: Shorten the registered divider with four parallel-trial radix-4 steps\nPROPOSAL: Replace the eight radix-2 restoring steps in each div_unit RUN clock\nwith four radix-4 steps, each producing two quotient bits. Preserve the\nexisting launch, four RUN clocks, one SIGN clock, and held DONE result\nschedule exactly in both real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS builds. This is a\nlocal arithmetic rewrite: the pipeline and divider handshake keep their\ncurrent behavior, and CoreMark instruction throughput should stay the\nsame while the divider's register-to-register path becomes shorter.\n\nAt launch capture the unsigned divisor magnitude D and the widened\nmultiples 2D and 3D. All multiples must be 34 bits; form 3D with an\nexplicitly widened addition during launch rather than recomputing it\ninside the RUN recurrence. Each digit step forms the 34-bit trial\nT = {remainder[31:0], quotient[31:30]}. Compute T-D, T-2D, and T-3D in\nparallel as 35-bit zero-extended subtractions. Their bit 34 supplies\nborrow, so no separate compare followed by subtract is needed. With\nok1, ok2, and ok3 denoting no-borrow for D, 2D, and 3D respectively,\nappend the quotient digit {ok2, ok3 | (ok1 & !ok2)}. Select the low\n32 remainder bits using disjoint masks !ok1, ok1 & !ok2,\nok2 & !ok3, and ok3 on T and the three difference results. Express\nselection as parallel masked\n…[20542 of 23614 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3b7b6c7f4223c72a]…\nrement order, liveness, and all bus-stall behavior.\n\nThe intended gain is shorter borrow and difference propagation in\nevery dependent restoring step at unchanged CoreMark cycles. The\nmain risks are duplicated block arithmetic, prefix routing and the\nexisting integer/forwarding paths becoming the clock limit. The\nestimate is not a measured fitness result. Require unchanged formal,\narithmetic unit, stalled cosim, memory-bound, CRC and UART gates,\nwith canonical marker-bracketed cycles. At unchanged cycles the\nacceptance threshold is median Gowin Fmax greater than 53.91084 MHz,\nor fitness greater than 140.78114 iter/sec; small placement variation\nalone does not establish the hypothesis.\n\nNOTES: \nhyp-20261004-002-r6s1 structural regression fitness 132.61 fmax 50.784 cycles 3829487 title: Dedicated leading-byte divider stage enables a four-bit shared body\nhyp-20261004-003-r6s2 predictor regression fitness 131.57 fmax 50.384 cycles 3829487 title: One-bit registered predictor squash preserves immediate PC recovery\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
