{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"tail -35 cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\nrg -n 'def test.*runner' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\nls cores/bench/generated/hypgen_regforward\"","aggregated_output":"@cocotb.test()\nasync def rvfi_order_strictly_monotonic(dut):\n    \"\"\"A short stream must produce rvfi_order = 0,1,2,... with no gaps.\"\"\"\n    program = [\n        ADDI(1, 0, 1),\n        ADDI(2, 0, 2),\n        ADDI(3, 0, 3),\n        ADDI(4, 0, 4),\n        EBREAK(),\n    ]\n    rets, _ = await _run(dut, program)\n    orders = [r[\"order\"] for r in rets]\n    assert orders == list(range(len(orders))), f\"order not monotonic +1: {orders}\"\n\n\ndef test_pipeline_runner():\n    runner = get_runner(os.environ.get(\"SIM\", \"verilator\"))\n    build_dir = SIM_BUILD / \"core\"\n    runner.build(\n        hdl_toplevel=\"core\",\n        sources=[str(RTL / source) for source in [\n            \"core_pkg.sv\",\n            \"alu.sv\", \"div_unit.sv\", \"decoder.sv\", \"imm_gen.sv\", \"reg_file.sv\",\n            \"if_stage.sv\", \"id_stage.sv\", \"ex_stage.sv\",\n            \"mem_stage.sv\", \"wb_stage.sv\",\n            \"hazard_unit.sv\", \"forward_unit.sv\",\n            \"core.sv\",\n        ]],\n        build_dir=str(build_dir), always=True,\n        build_args=[\"-Wall\", \"-Wno-fatal\", \"-Wno-style\", \"--public-flat-rw\", f\"+incdir+{RTL}\"],\n    )\n    runner.test(\n        hdl_toplevel=\"core\", test_module=\"test_pipeline\",\n        test_dir=str(TEST_DIR), build_dir=str(build_dir),\n    )\n1090:def test_pipeline_runner():\ngowin_p0\nresult0.json\nrtl\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r7s0.yaml')\nh={'id':'hyp-20261004-001-r7s0','title':'Precompute forwarding register matches at decode to shorten EX bypass control','category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''LESSONS.md is absent. The champion scores 134.59 at 51.54 MHz with\n3,829,487 timed CoreMark cycles. Recent divider and predictor changes\nfailed to clear acceptance, and vendor reports show competing paths\nfrom EX/MEM destination bits through forwarding selection, multiplier,\nand result arbitration. The core repeats five-bit source/destination\ncomparisons on the EX critical path, although the register identities\nare already available one clock earlier in ID. Registering only those\nmatches can remove comparator delay before both integer and isolated\nmultiplier bypass muxes without adding a CPU stage or a stall.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Precompute and register four address-match bits alongside each ordinary\nID/EX payload transfer. Compare the offered decoded rs1/rs2 addresses\nagainst the current ID/EX rd for that instruction's future MEM producer,\nand against the current EX/MEM rd for its future WB producer. Require\nnonzero producer rd in every comparison. Use the same \"'!stall_id payload\ncapture enable as id_stage, reset all matches to zero, and hold them\nthrough backend stalls and load-to-MUL bubbles. A redirect may capture\nmatches for an invalid payload exactly as the current ID stage captures\nits other fields; validity still suppresses its side effects.\n\nIn EX replace the duplicated live five-bit comparator instances with\nsmall priority selection from these registered address matches. Retain\nlive producer eligibility exactly: integer MEM forwarding requires\nex_mem.valid, reg_write and either a non-load or an asserted io_dmemREn;\nmultiply MEM forwarding additionally excludes every load. WB eligibility\nremains wb_fwd_valid_q && mem_wb.ctrl.reg_write, retaining the existing\nforwarding provenance after retirement during dmem holds. Give an\neligible younger MEM producer priority over WB for each source. When\nneither eligible registered match applies, select the ID/EX value.\nDo not pre-register producer validity, reg_write, alignment correction\nor load acceptance: those can change between stages and must qualify\nthe matches at their actual consumption boundary. Keep the standalone\nforward_unit module available for any existing standalone use/tests.\n\nNo new forwarding data path is added. Retain the current live integer\nload extraction, separate registered-source MUL operand muxes, selective\nload-to-MUL interlock, regfile write-first bypass and all RVFI source\nvalues. A dmem hold preserves the MEM producer and retained WB payload,\nso its registered identity matches remain applicable. During a held\nDIV, operands have already been captured by the divider; when DIV is\nconsumed and decode resumes, recompute matches against the outgoing\nDIV destination so the next instruction forwards its published result.\nKeep the existing pipeline/divider/fetch schedules and top-level IO.\n\nThis is one local forwarding control timing optimization. The gain is\nremoving destination comparison and its fanout from EX bypass selection\nwhile keeping the same cycles and architectural behavior. Four extra\nmatch flops replace the repeated live comparators. The unchanged divider\nand live-load recovery cone may cap Fmax; estimates are provisional.\nDo not combine this proposal with divider arithmetic, multiplier sharing,\none-hot ALU result encoding or predictor changes.\n\nPreserve nret=1, +1 retirement order, decoder legality, all traps and\nmemory bounds, seven-clock real/ALTOPS divider and exact arithmetic,\nreset/consume/capture semantics, symbolic liveness, canonical CRC/UART,\nand marker-only timing. Verify both matching sources, x0, younger MEM\npriority, retained WB across long dmem holds, ordinary bubbles and\nflushes, trapped loads, load-to-MUL interlocks and a dependent consumer\nimmediately after DIV. Keep full existing RVFI and side-effect checks.\nRequire unchanged formal, units and stalled cosim, canonical CoreMark\nvalidation and all Gowin placement options. At unchanged 3,829,487\ncycles, acceptance requires fitness above 140.78114 and median Fmax\nabove approximately 53.914 MHz. Local timing probes are not a completed\ncorrectness or fitness evaluation.\n'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':7,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Register four nonzero source/destination matches on the existing ID/EX\npayload enable, using current ID/EX and EX/MEM destinations for future\nMEM and WB identities. Replace live integer/MUL comparator instances\nwith priority selection from those matches and the unchanged live\nproducer eligibility, alignment checks and held-WB provenance. Leave\nall ports, arithmetic, data muxes and pipeline control unchanged.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Add directed register-match transition checks and independent RVFI\nprograms for simultaneous source matches, x0, repeated destination\nwriters, trapped/misaligned loads, stale invalid payloads, write-first\nWB reads, long dmem holds, redirects, load-to-MUL bubbles and immediate\nDIV-result consumers. Assert match stability only while the ID/EX\npayload holds. Retain all existing arithmetic, retirement, side-effect,\nlatency, liveness and stall assertions without weakening them.\n'''}\n]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypoth