{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r8s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261004-001-r8s0\ntitle: Two arithmetic levels per five-bit divider group using radix-8 and radix-4\n  trials\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: 'LESSONS.md is absent. The champion scores 134.59 iter/sec at 51.540\n  MHz\n\n  and 3,829,487 bracketed cycles. Its reported worst path is entirely\n\n  inside the five-cell restoring divider, at 24.838 ns across 152 cells.\n\n  Earlier radix-4 groups reduced arithmetic depth but left three or four\n\n  dependent levels; segmented borrow lookahead regressed severely, and\n\n  the launch-prefix and forwarding-predecode attempts also regressed.\n\n  A wider parallel-trial digit offers a different local arithmetic trade:\n\n  replace the five serial subtract/select cells with only two levels,\n\n  while preserving the proven instruction and divider schedules.\n\n  '\nhypothesis: 'Rewrite only div_unit''s real RUN arithmetic as a radix-4 digit followed\n\n  by a radix-8 digit for each of the six normal five-bit groups. The last\n\n  group consumes exactly the remaining two bits with an independent copy\n\n  of the current two radix-2 cells and fused sign restoration. Preserve accepted\n  launch, seven RUN edges,\n\n  held DONE, consume, operand capture and all CPU pipeline boundaries.\n\n  This is one local parallel-trial divider optimization, with no new\n\n  execution stage or instruction-latency change.\n\n\n  Capture unsigned divisor magnitude D and explicitly widened unsigned\n\n  35-bit odd multiples 3D, 5D and 7D at launch. Form 3D=(D<<1)+D,\n\n  5D=(D<<2)+D and 7D=(D<<3)-D in parallel, using 35-bit D before every\n\n  shift or arithmetic operation. Derive 2D and 4D by wiring shifts of D\n\n  and 6D by shifting registered 3D. No divisor-multiple generation may\n\n  remain in the recurring RUN chain. Avoid computing an odd multiple\n\n  by cascading the other odd multiples. Check the forwarded launch path\n\n  through magnitude and multiple generation in vendor timing.\n\n\n  The radix-8 cell follows the radix-4 cell and forms unsigned 35-bit\n\n  T={R[31:0],Q[31:29]} from its completed remainder and quotient. Compute\n…[3210 of 6282 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6a47377caa43b62c]…\n.6 percent acceptance margin.\n\n  '\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n- file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n  description: 'Replace the five-cell real restoring chain with one radix-4 cell\n\n    followed by one radix-8 cell, registered widened odd divisor multiples,\n\n    parallel borrow-derived trials and disjoint digit/remainder selection.\n\n    Retain a separate two-radix-2-cell terminal path and preserve the exact\n\n    seven-clock real/ALTOPS schedule, corner cases and handshake.\n\n    '\n- file: test/test_div_unit.py\n  description: 'Add independent exact-result cases for all radix-8 and radix-4\n\n    digits, five-bit boundaries, terminal two-bit patterns, and trial\n\n    values below/equal/above each divisor multiple. Cover maximum-width\n\n    odd multiples, all operand signs, signed extrema, zero divisors,\n\n    changing post-launch operands, reset in each phase and held DONE.\n\n    Preserve existing latency, consume/relaunch and arithmetic assertions\n\n    in both real and ALTOPS builds.\n\n    '\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
