{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261004-002-r9s1|early.launch|launch|operand-register|pipeline' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share a radix-4 combinational divider across RV32M divide and remainder\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline's worst timed path is 199.837 ns across 156 cells and passes\\nthrough forwarding and the combinational ALU. Its 5.442 MHz Fmax strongly\\nsuggests that the deeply unrolled divide/remainder arithmetic dominates\\nfitness. alu.sv currently expresses signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder separately. Improving this timed arithmetic cone can increase\\nCoreMark iterations/second without changing instruction throughput or\\nadding pipeline control under the approximately 22% memory stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline's worst timed path is 199.837 ns across 156 cells and passes\\nthrough forwarding and the combinational ALU. Its 5.442 MHz Fmax strongly\\nsuggests that the deeply unrolled divide/remainder arithmetic dominates\\nfitness. alu.sv currently expresses signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder separately. Improving this timed arithmetic cone can increase\\nCoreMark iterations/second without changing instruction throughput or\\nadding pipeline control under the approximately 22% memory stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU implementations with one\\nshared, fully combinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divmod network.\\nConvert operands to unsigned magnitudes for signed DIV/REM, run sixteen\\ndependent steps that consume two dividend bits and emit two quotient\\nbits each, then apply the quotient and remainder signs. Each step forms\\nT = {previous_remainder[31:0], next_dividend_pair}, computes T-D, T-2D,\\nand T-3D in parallel, and chooses the largest n