\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_1_s1\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -10.807,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 21.101,\n      \"logic_cells\": 27,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_of/reg_q.ctrl.is_auipc_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_uu_63_s0\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -10.807,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 20.912,\n      \"logic_cells\": 11,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex\",\n        \"cpu/u_of\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/narrow_d3_q_0_s0\",\n      \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_7_s0\",\n      \"slack_ns\": -10.797,\n      \"arrival_ns\": 21.091,\n      \"logic_cells\": 29,\n      \"modules\": [\n        \"clock_ibuf\",\n        \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_77", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r10s1.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261004-002-r10s1\ntitle: \\\"EX-only divider launch with a six-clock asymmetric engine\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 161.60 iter/sec at 65.036 MHz and 4,024,573\n  marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst Gowin path crosses EX\n  arithmetic, OF forwarding and early-divider launch preprocessing,\n  ending at remainder_q after 20.938 ns. The successful r8s1 operand\n  register isolates normal execution, but division still bypasses that\n  boundary. LESSONS.md is absent. Structural history shows that divider\n  retiming succeeds when preparation and terminal arithmetic are kept\n  physically separate; r7s1's fused terminal/sign path regressed.\n  Eliminating early OF launch can remove the remaining arithmetic-to-\n  forwarding-to-divider chain if one internal divider clock is recovered.\nhypothesis: |\n  Launch DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU exclusively from registered OF/EX operands\n  and reduce the engine from seven RUN clocks to six. Recover that\n  clock by repartitioning prefix work: four bits at launch, six narrow\n  bits at the first RUN edge, five four-bit body clocks and the existing\n  independent terminal two-bit publication. Exactly 4+6+5*4+2=32 bits\n  are processed. This is one structural launch/stage-boundary change;\n  retain six CPU stages, single issue, nret=1 and all memory interfaces.\n\n  Remove early OF launch and its independent early forwarding datapath.\n  EX's divider op/a/b ports connect directly to registered in.ctrl.alu_op,\n  in.rs1_val and in.rs2_val, without early/fallback data selection. Start\n  once for an accepted valid legal divide when the engine is idle and\n  the older MEM request can advance. Capture exact RVFI sources and\n  instruction metadata together at this launch. Retain divider ownership,\n  older-stage draining, frontend holds, load-use handling, dmem priority,\n  held completions and single publication. Ordinary OF capture must\n  still forward normal EX and completed-divide results correctly.\n\n  At engine launch L, form the four-bit dividend-magnitude prefix P\n  directly: for a negative signed dividend, P=(~a[31:28]+\n  (a[27:0]==0)) modulo sixteen; otherwise P=a[31:28]. Compute the low\n  twenty-eight magnitude bits and full divisor magnitude independently.\n  Detect magnitude D<=15 directly from raw b, without waiting for its\n  full-width negate: negative signed b qualifies iff b[31:4] is all ones\n  and b[3:0]\"'!=0; otherwise b[31:4] must be zero. The small magnitude is\n  (0-b[3:0]) modulo sixteen for negative b, otherwise b[3:0]. Process\n  P with a two-bit divmod lookup followed by one narrow radix-4 cell.\n  The lookup covers D=0,1,2,3 exactly; D>3 yields zero quotient and its\n  unchanged two-bit prefix remainder. The second cell uses widened\n  parallel T-D/T-2D/T-3D trials and disjoint masks. Larger D yields\n  prefix quotient zero and remainder P. Register Q={magnitude_low28,\n  prefix_Q}, zero-extended prefix R, divisor, signs and result selection.\n\n  Also capture the narrow bootstrap'\"'s expensive divisor multiples at L,\n  independently of prefix arithmetic. Compute m=abs(b)[9:0] directly\n  from raw b: negative signed b uses (0-b[9:0]) modulo 1024, otherwise\n  b[9:0]. Register unsigned 13-bit 3m,5m,7m using widened shifts/adds.\n  For D>1023 the bootstrap ignores these truncated-divisor multiples.\n  Never compute full-width 3D or let a forwarded operand enter these\n  adders; their inputs come exclusively from the OF/EX operand flops.\n\n  At RUN group zero, L+1, consume six additional dividend bits with two\n  narrow radix-8 cells and prepare registered unsigned 34-bit 3D in\n  parallel from divisor_q. The completed prefix has only ten bits.\n  If D[31:10]\"'!=0, append six quotient zeros and concatenate the old\n  four-bit remainder with Q[31:26]. Otherwise each cell takes three\n  bits, trials jD for j=1..7 and chooses the largest successful digit\n  with disjoint masks. Build D,2D,4D by wiring, use the captured 3m,5m,\n  7m and derive 6m by shifting captured 3m. Keep all thirteen multiple\n  bits. Since each window is at most 1023, an eligible trial requires\n  multiple[12:10]==0 plus no borrow in the eleven-bit zero-extended\n  window[9:0]-multiple[9:0] subtraction. Preserve this high-bit guard;\n  truncating a large multiple without it is incorrect. Select ten-bit\n  restored remainders and three-bit quotient digits with masked ORs.\n  D=0 produces digit seven and reconstructs the original prefix.\n  Register Q={old_Q[25:0],six_new_bits} and zero-extended ten-bit R.\n  Full-width 3D preparation has no connection to these narrow cells.\n\n  On groups one through five, L+2..L+6, reuse the champion'\"'s two\n  full-width radix-4 cells, widened parallel trials and masked selection.\n  Enter READY after L+6 with thirty bits processed. Preserve the\n  independent held-state terminal two-bit/sign candidate bank and\n  consume into EX/MEM at L+7. There is no selected-result register,\n  extra padding step or sign arithmetic after the final digit mux.\n  Retain reset cancellation, rejected starts, simultaneous standalone\n  consume/relaunch and stable READY results. Real and ALTOPS builds\n  must have the identical six-RUN schedule and exact existing formulas.\n  Preserve divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1 and every signed remainder rule.\n\n  If a divide enters OF/EX at P, engine launch is P+1 and publication\n  is P+8, matching the champion's early-launch publication edge.\n  Consecutive divides improve from nine to eight retirement clocks;\n  unpredicted redirect-to-divide remains at most ten. Strengthen the\n  exact standalone latency and consecutive-divide checks to six and\n  eight respectively; retain the unchanged ten-cycle liveness bound\n  and all correctness assertions. Rework tests specific to early launch\n  to verify that an OF-only request cannot launch before OF/EX capture,\n  including wrong-path cancellation and acceptance under memory stalls.\n\n  Scratch EX-only launch without registered narrow multiples passed\n  real/ALTOPS divider arithmetic, and its canonical stalled CoreMark\n  produced all required CRCs, validation text, no out-of-bounds accesses\n  and exactly 4,024,573 bracketed cycles. Its median vendor clock was\n  only 63.827 MHz: divisor-multiple preparation before bootstrap trials\n  became the new limit. Capturing those narrow multiples at launch is\n  therefore essential to this final proposal. Do not infer acceptance\n  from the scratch checks. Require the final implementation's unchanged\n  unit/formal/cosim gates and median Gowin fitness above 169.0336 iter/sec,\n  approximately 68.029 MHz at unchanged cycles. Bootstrap depth, launch\n  multiple preparation and completed-DIV forwarding remain timing risks.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Implement four-bit launch, registered thirteen-bit narrow 3D/5D/7D,\n      a six-bit radix-8 first RUN beside full-width 3D preparation, five\n      existing two-digit radix-4 RUN groups, and unchanged independent\n      terminal publication. Use exactly six RUN clocks in real/ALTOPS.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove early-divider launch and early/fallback operand muxes. Launch\n      exclusively from registered OF/EX sources and capture metadata at\n      that edge. Preserve ownership, stalls, draining and single transfer.\n  - file: rtl/operand_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove the unused independent early-divider forwarding/payload path.\n      Retain ordinary RF/MEM/WB/normal-EX/completed-DIV selection and\n      actual-source load interlocks without new dependency bubbles.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Remove early-divider payload/acceptance wiring while preserving\n      ordinary operand acceptance, all top-level ports, RVFI provenance,\n      hazard arbitration and the existing single retirement boundary.\n  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n    description: |\n      Assert exact six-clock completion in real/ALTOPS and retain every\n      arithmetic, capture, reset, rejected-start, held-result and relaunch\n      check. Add exhaustive four-bit launch prefixes, ten-bit bootstrap\n      boundaries, widened multiple guards and D=15/16/1023/1024 cases.\n  - file: test/test_ex_divider.py\n    description: |\n      Verify EX-only launch and operand/metadata capture, no launch from\n      younger OF payloads, exact six-RUN/seventh-edge publication, stalls,\n      reset and duplicate suppression. Replace early-launch-specific\n      expectations with registered-boundary checks retaining their\n      architectural and side-effect coverage.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Strengthen consecutive-divide assertions to eight clocks and adjust\n      exact predicted-control-to-divide schedules to their shorter gaps.\n      Retain the ten-clock redirect/liveness bound and every source,\n      result, trap, order and memory assertion. Exercise dependent ALU,\n      multiply and load producers, wrong-path divides and random stalls.\n''')\nprint('Updated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
