{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"CoreMark passes all required CRCs, with a cycle cost of just 0.13%. The first timing result regressed, though: the scratch design duplicated partial-product state in the divider payload. I’m testing a dedicated EX/MEM product register bank to remove that extra state and its control paths."}}
