iate PC update and accepted training\nendpoints. A broader local prototype with a registered target and\nfetch-address mux matched 3,829,487 canonical cycles and passed stalled\nselftest plus all three random-program cosims, but its timing regressed.\nThat evidence motivates this narrower one-bit control split and\nvalidity-only kill; it does not establish a fitness improvement.\nAcceptance still requires fitness above 140.78114, or approximately\n53.914 MHz median Fmax at unchanged cycles. The unchanged divider and\ninteger datapath may prevent that gain; confidence is low. Evaluate\nall placement options and unchanged correctness gates.\nhyp-20261004-001-r10s0 Select OF forwarding sources directly with disjoint one-hot masks\nKeep the separate normal and early masks for both architectural sources, existing raw RVFI operands,\n…[10995 of 14067 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9bfad44e4f920ffb]…\nse.value) == 0\n    dut.ex_rd.value = 2\n    dut[\"in\"].value = decoded()\n    dut.stall.value = dut.flush.value = 1\n    dut.accept.value = 0\n    await tick(dut)\n    assert unpack(ID_EX, int(dut.out.value))[\"valid\"] == 0\n    # The older load moves once to MEM; its aligned/extended value is captured.\n    dut.ex_load.value = 0\n    dut.mem_rd.value = 2\n    dut.mem_w_en.value = 1\n    dut.mem_result.value = 0xffffff80\n    dut.stall.value = dut.flush.value = 0\n    dut.accept.value = 1\n    await tick(dut)\n    out = unpack(ID_EX, int(dut.out.value))\n    assert out[\"valid\"] == 1 and out[\"rs2_val\"] == 0xffffff80\n    # Trapping/invalid producers are suppressed by their writer qualification.\n    dut.mem_w_en.value = 0\n    dut.rs2_data.value = 7\n    await tick(dut)\n    assert unpack(ID_EX, int(dut.out.value))[\"rs2_val\"] == 7\n\n\ndef test_operand_stage_runner():\n    run_cocotb(toplevel=\"operand_stage\",\n               sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"forward_unit.sv\", \"operand_stage.sv\"],\n               test_module=\"test_operand_stage\")\n"