val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_ss_63_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -11.268, \"arrival_ns\": 21.374, \"logic_cells\": 39, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_of\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_of/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_ss_63_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -11.264, \"arrival_ns\": 21.369, \"logic_cells\": 39, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_of\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_of/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_uu_63_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -11.25, \"arrival_ns\": 21.324, \"logic_cells\": 39, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_of\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_of/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mul_ss_63_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -11.246, \"arrival_ns\": 21.32, \"logic_cells\": 39, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_of\"]}, {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_1_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_8_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -11.244, \"arrival_ns\": 21.538, \"logic_cells\": 21, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'] in ('hyp-20261004-002-r8s1','hyp-20261004-001-r3s0'):\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{}); s=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n  print(r['id']);print(s[:6500])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n r=json.loads(l)\n if r['id'] in ('hyp-20261004-002-r8s1','hyp-20261004-001-r3s0'):\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{}); s=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n  print(r['id']);print(s[:6500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-001-r3s0\nAdd one local MEM-to-EX forwarding path for completed loads, preserving the pipeline stages and retirement schedule for all other instructions. Expose the existing mem_stage sign/zero-extended load_data as part of a forwarding value: select load_data for mem_to_reg, otherwise the existing EX/MEM alu_result. Route this value into EX's existing highest-priority EX/MEM forwarding input. The forwarding producer must be valid, have a nonzero matching destination, and retain reg_write after memory-alignment trap correction. Never forward the effective address as a load result or make a trapped/misaligned load a producer.\n\nRemove the unconditional ID/EX-load versus fetched-source bubble once the new bypass is connected. A load enters MEM while its immediately following consumer enters EX. When io_dmemReady is high, the formatted load result feeds the consumer before the same accepting edge that moves the load to MEM/WB and the consumer to EX/MEM. When it is low, the existing dStall mechanism holds PC, ID/EX and EX/MEM, clears only MEM/WB.valid, preserves WB forwarding provenance, and suppresses redirect and divider launch. The consumer must never advance or launch a divide from unaccepted data. Thus one producer can serve ALU, branch/JALR, store-address/store-data and divide consumers without a new stage, queue, speculative state or architectural latency change. Preserve younger EX/MEM priority over held WB, source x0, simultaneous rs1/rs2 matches and all RVFI source values.\n\nRetain the seven-clock real/ALTOPS divider, captured forwarded operands, held DONE behavior, all decoder legality rules, trap behavior, nret=1 IO, strictly increasing retirement order, and redirect-over-fetch-stall priority. No evaluation or formal configuration changes are permitted. The improvement must come from fewer genuine load-use and conservative source-index bubbles. The longer dmem-to-EX-to-branch/multiplier path is the principal risk: validate the final design with median vendor Fmax times marker-bracketed CoreMark \n…[5657 of 8729 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a683cf7e83cd2b26]…\nprefix. Enter READY after L+7, hold all arithmetic state and expose\nthe last two steps plus parallel sign restoration combinationally.\nEX/MEM registers that final result at consume edge L+8; remove the\nintervening divider completed-result register. Exactly 2+7*4+2=32 bits\nare processed. READY result and valid remain stable for any delayed\nconsume, rejected starts or changing live inputs. Preserve reset and\nstandalone simultaneous consume/relaunch. The final path reads the\nheld thirty-bit state, never the four-step feedback output.\n\nReal arithmetic and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS have identical launch-to-valid\nand publication schedules. Retain every exact ALTOPS expression,\nRV32M signed/unsigned result, zero-divisor result, quotient-negation\nsuppression on zero, dividend-only remainder sign, and INT_MIN/-1\nbehavior. Capture divide metadata at whichever launch edge actually\naccepts its operands, without allowing a changing forward source to\ncorrupt held RVFI state.\n\nPreserve all top-level memory and nret=1 RVFI ports,\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"The deeper queues saved less than 0.3% of CoreMark cycles and reduced frequency. I’m refining the final hypothesis around issuing loads one stage earlier, using an address registered in OF. That could remove load-use bubbles while keeping ALU, branch, multiply and divide execution behind operand registers."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r12s1.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-002-r12s1',\n'title':'Early load execution behind a registered effective-address boundary',\n'category':'structural',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.88 iterations/second at median 70.381 MHz and\n4,024,573 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The\nstructural history shows that registering resolved operands and launching\ndivision exclusively from EX improved frequency substantially. The recent\npartial-product multiplier lost frequency and exposed divider timing.\nEarlier MEM-to-executing-EX load forwarding saved cycles but connected\nlive memory data to arithmetic and recovery paths, limiting its benefit.\n\nThe current six-stage pipeline still inserts one bubble whenever an EX\nload produces an actual source of the OF instruction. This remains true\nwith a ready memory bus. Moving the load request one stage earlier,\nbehind a registered effective address, can deliver its result to the\nexisting OF operand flops on that same accepting edge. The consumer's\nexecution remains isolated from the live bus. Scratch timing probes of\nbranch-comparison retiming, wider fetch buffering and removal of the ID\nregister did not beat this champion; an additional register or a deeper\nqueue alone is not a sufficient structural improvement.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Retiming only load execution should reduce dependent-load bubbles while\npreserving the resolved operand boundary: compute a legal load's effective\naddress during OF, register it atomically with the OF/EX instruction and\noperands, issue that load from EX, and capture both the memory response\nand the consuming OF instruction's resolved operands at the successful\nhandshake edge. Keep IF -> ID -> OF -> EX -> MEM -> WB, single issue,\nnret=1, the existing predictor and fetch queue, and the exact multiplier\nand six-RUN-clock divider. This is one structural change in load stage\nplacement and result availability, with the existing external memory bus.\n\nAdd a registered early_load_addr to OF/EX. Its value is the final\nx0-corrected, age-prioritized rs1 operand plus the decoded immediate,\nmodulo 32 bits. Compute the sum only on the load path; ordinary integer,\nbranch, store and multiply execution keep their present operands and\nstage placement. Preserve the accepting-edge payload enable and holds.\nEX loads use this address register directly, including its low bits for\nalignment and byte extraction; they do not recompute the address through\nthe EX ALU. The new address path must never run through a current EX\narithmetic result, completed divider result, or live early-load response\nbefore another wide addition in the same clock.\n\nEnforce that last constraint with a selective address dependency\ninterlock: when a valid legal OF load actually uses a nonzero rs1 that\nmatches the youngest accepted EX register writer, hold ID/OF and decode\nconsumption and insert an OF/EX bubble while that writer advances once.\nOn the next accepting edge form the load address from its registered MEM\nresult, then WB/RF as appropriate. Include completed division and accepted\nearly loads in this producer classification. An older matching MEM/WB\nwriter must not satisfy the dependency while the youngest EX writer is\nunavailable. This interlock is limited to load address generation; other\nconsumers may capture the accepted early-load result without a bubble.\nExisting decoded source-use flags, legality, writer qualification and x0\nrules remain mandatory. Keep division launch exclusively from OF/EX.\n\nUse the single dmem port in program order. An outstanding legal aligned\nMEM store owns it ahead of an EX load, including on the store's successful\nhandshake clock: never perform two memory operations on one edge. While\nthat store stalls, preserve its complete address/data/mask request. On\nits accepting edge retire/drain it normally, insert an EX/MEM bubble and\nhold the younger EX load; issue the load on the following cycle. Stores\nretain their MEM stage. Consecutive accepted EX loads may issue every\nclock because a load entering MEM already owns a captured response and\nmust not request the bus again. FENCE behavior remains ordered by this\nin-order execution and completion protocol.\n\nAn eligible EX load asserts read enable using its registered address only\nwhen no older store owns the bus. Gate illegal and misaligned requests\noff. If io_dmemReady is low, hold the EX load, its address and both younger\npayload stages; keep the read request stable. Older non-memory MEM/WB\ninstructions drain once rather than being replayed. Distinguish holding\nan outstanding MEM store from holding the executing early load: do not\nfreeze a drainable EX/MEM instruction just because the younger EX load is\nwaiting, and do not overwrite a stalled store with a bubble. These are\nindependent ownership/advance conditions, not a global hold of every\nbackend register. Reset cancels ownership and pending valid state.\n\nOn an accepted aligned EX load, format the live bus word with that load's\nregistered width, signedness and address offset. Expose the resulting\narchitectural value as a youngest EX forwarding producer only while\nrequest-valid and io_dmemReady are true. Capture it in OF/EX for an\nimmediate ALU, branch/JALR, store-data/store-address, multiply or divide\nconsumer; none of those execution units may consume live dmem directly.\nA load that generates the next load's address uses the selective bubble\ndescribed above. Qualify every consumer transfer with successful older\nmemory acceptance; bus stalls never authorize speculative captures,\nbranch training, redirect or divider launch.\n\nCapture the early load's raw memory word, formatted value, effective\naddress and exact instruction/RVFI payload into EX/MEM at that same edge.\nMEM uses the captured response for WB and for its registered-result bypass;\nit must not resample io_dmemRData or emit a second read. Keep rd_wdata equal\nto the captured sign/zero-extended value; RVFI mem_rdata reports the raw\naccepted word, mem_addr is word-aligned and mem_rmask describes the byte\nlanes. A misaligned load retires once with a trap, no memory request and\nno RF/forwarding write, without waiting for an irrelevant bus-ready bit.\nWB remains the architectural RF write and single-channel retirement\nboundary. Preserve retained WB forwarding provenance while other stages\nare held, exact source metadata and strict +1 retirement order.\n\nPreserve all decoder default-illegal and EBREAK-only SYSTEM checks,\nbranch/jump alignment and recovery behavior, memory bounds and MMIO\nordering, all real and ALTOPS arithmetic formulas, outstanding-request\nstability, wrong-path suppression and the unchanged ten-cycle symbolic\nprogress bound. No early request may come from an OF instruction that an\naccepted older EX redirect is killing. A request begins only from the\nregistered valid EX load. No contract files or nret changes are included.\n\nThe forecast is an eight-percent fitness improvement, with low confidence;\nthis early-load circuit has not been implemented or measured. The new\nOF address adder, dmem ownership mux and store-to-load serialization are\nmaterial costs, and the unchanged divider can still limit Fmax. The\nselective load-address interlock trades some cycle savings for keeping\ncurrent EX arithmetic and live load data out of the address adder. Do not\nassume that every current load-use bubble disappears or infer a gain from\nan IPC result alone. Acceptance requires fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec.\nFor a five-percent reduction from the champion's bracketed cycle count,\nmedian Gowin Fmax must exceed approximately 69.94 MHz; at unchanged cycles\nit must exceed approximately 73.62 MHz. Measure canonical CoreMark cycles\nbetween the MMIO markers, validate all five CRCs and the UART literal,\nand run every unchanged formal/cosim gate and scored placement option.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add the registered early-load effective address to OF/EX and accepted load-response/raw-word metadata to EX/MEM. Preserve all architectural/RVFI payloads and external interfaces.'},\n {'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'Form and register early load addresses from the final resolved rs1 and immediate. Interlock only OF load-address dependencies on the youngest accepted EX writer; allow other consumers to capture accepted early-load data with existing priority, x0, hold and kill rules.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Execute aligned legal loads using the registered effective address and an explicit request/accept handshake. Capture accepted responses and exact metadata, expose formatted data only on accepted EX-load forwarding, and hold a waiting load while older backend work drains once. Preserve ordinary arithmetic, branch recovery and EX-only divider launch.'},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Keep stores in MEM and export their outstanding request/ownership. Route already accepted load responses to WB and MEM forwarding without replaying reads or resampling the bus. Preserve aligned RVFI raw words, masks, load formatting and trap suppression.'},\n {'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'Separate outstanding-MEM-store holds, early-EX-load waits, store/load port collisions and selective address dependency bubbles. Preserve one-time older-stage draining, redirect priority, fetch acceptance and validity kills.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Arbitrate the existing dmem port between older MEM stores and registered EX loads, wire response acceptance and new producer availability, and distinguish MEM payload holds from executing-load holds. Preserve the exact nret=1 top-level ports, WB retirement and forwarding provenance.'},\n {'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'Check captured effective addresses against an independent modular-addition oracle, every forwarding age, x0, signed immediates and wraps; check selective EX-to-load address bubbles and successful early-load capture by other consumers. Retain all existing operand correctness assertions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'Update packed bundles for added metadata and load handshake ports. Verify load acceptance, raw/formatted capture, stable blocked requests, traps and reset while retaining exact real/ALTOPS divider arithmetic, latency, held completion and operand-isolation assertions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add load-to-ALU/branch/store/multiply/divide and load-to-load address cases, consecutive loads, store/load collisions, repeated destination writers, all load widths, misalignment, independent long bus stalls, resets and wrong-path loads. Check every architectural/RVFI field, accepted transaction count, request stability, age priority and unchanged progress bound; update stage-specific observations to the declared early-load availability.'}\n]}\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90,allow_unicode=True))\nprint('Wrote and validated:',p)\nprint('Single structural hypothesis:',h['title'])\nprint('Changed paths:', [c['file'] for c in h['changes']])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
