{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' tools/eval/gowin.py; sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/test/test_operand_stage.py; sed -n '1,180p' Makefile\"", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\n\nV2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\nroute and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\nmodel for this part misses whole classes of paths. The vendor flow is also\ndeterministic and insensitive to circuit-neutral netlist changes.\n\nFmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\na full build of the same RTL; results are deterministic for a given input.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport statistics\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import remove_path\n\nGOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\nGOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\nPART = \"GW2AR-LV18QN88C8/I7\"      # Tang Nano 20K\nDEVICE_VERSION = \"C\"\nPLACE_OPTIONS = (0, 1, 2)\nCST = \"fpga/constraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\"\nSDC = \"fpga/constraints/clock.sdc\"\nSTALL_GEN = \"fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\"\nBUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC = 2700\n\n\ndef gowin_env(base: dict | None, workdir: Path) -> dict:\n    env = dict(os.environ if base is None else base)\n    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n    env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = \":\".join(map(str, libs))\n    env[\"QT_QPA_PLATFORM\"] = \"offscreen\"\n    xdg = workdir / \".xdg\"\n    xdg.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    os.chmod(xdg, 0o700)\n    env[\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"] = str(xdg)\n    return env\n\n\ndef rtl_sources(rtl_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:\n    srcs = sorted(rtl_dir.glob(\"*.sv\"))\n    pkg = rtl_dir / \"core_pkg.sv\"\n    return ([pkg] if pkg in srcs else []) + [p for p in srcs if p != pkg]\n\n\ndef project_tcl(worktree: Path, rtl_dir: Path, bench_sv: str, place_option: int) -> str:\n    files = [*rtl_sources(rtl_dir), worktree / STALL_GEN, worktree / bench_sv,\n             worktree / CST, worktree / SDC]\n    return \"\\n\".join([\n        f\"set_device {PART} -device_version {DEVICE_VERSION}\",\n        *(f\"add_file {f}\" for f in fi\n…[19741 of 22813 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a2bcc291361cc309]…\ns $(N),--iterations 1,$(ORCH_FLAGS)) $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\n\nloop:\nifneq ($(strip $(WORKTREE)),)\n\t@if [ ! -d \"$(WT_PATH)\" ]; then \\\n\t  echo \"[wt] creating branch $(WT_BRANCH) and worktree $(WT_PATH)\"; \\\n\t  if git rev-parse --verify $(WT_BRANCH) >/dev/null 2>&1; then \\\n\t    git worktree add \"$(WT_PATH)\" $(WT_BRANCH); \\\n\t  else \\\n\t    git worktree add -b $(WT_BRANCH) \"$(WT_PATH)\"; \\\n\t  fi; \\\n\t  [ -e \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\" ] || ln -s \"$(CURDIR)/formal/riscv-formal\" \"$(WT_PATH)/formal/riscv-formal\"; \\\n\tfi\n\t@$(MAKE) -C \"$(WT_PATH)\" loop \\\n\t  WORKTREE= \\\n\t  TARGET=$(TARGET) N=$(N) K=$(K) AGENT=$(AGENT) \\\n\t  $(if $(strip $(BASE)),BASE=$(BASE),) \\\n\t  $(if $(strip $(COREMARK)),COREMARK=$(COREMARK),) \\\n\t  $(if $(strip $(LUT)),LUT=$(LUT),)\nelse\n\tAGENT_PROVIDER=$(AGENT) python3 -m tools.orchestrator $(ORCH_FLAGS) $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\nendif\n\nreport:\n\tpython3 -m tools.orchestrator --report $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\n\nclean:\n\trm -rf test/cosim/sim_build sim_build out\n\trm -rf experiments/worktrees\n\trm -f bench/programs/*.elf\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids={'hyp-20261004-002-r10s1','hyp-20261004-002-r11s1','hyp-20261004-003-r6s2','hyp-20261004-003-r10s2','hyp-20261004-002-r8s1','hyp-20261004-002-r12s1'}\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ids:\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'])\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis'); print('HYPOTHESIS:',h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids={'hyp-20261004-002-r10s1','hyp-20261004-002-r11s1','hyp-20261004-003-r6s2','hyp-20261004-003-r10s2','hyp-20261004-002-r8s1','hyp-20261004-002-r12s1'}\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ids:\n  print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'])\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis'); print('HYPOTHESIS:',h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261004-003-r6s2 One-bit registered predictor squash preserves immediate PC recovery\nNOTES: # One-bit registered predictor squash\n\nImplemented the proposed control split. Correctness gates pass, but the\nmeasured implementation does not meet the fitness acceptance threshold.\n\n## RTL changes\n\n- `cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv`: retained the existing accepted immediate\n  redirect and preselected target. Added exactly one registered squash bit,\n  assigned from that accepted redirect each edge and cleared on reset and\n  every following no-event edge. Squash excludes the younger EX instruction\n  from recovery, predictor training, divider launch/wait and next EX/MEM\n  validity. Its ordinary wide payload still captures through the existing\n  pipeline path, including ordinary trap adjustments.\n- `cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv`: immediate redirect controls only the ordinary\n  full 32-bit PC register. Reset wins, then redirect, then accepted fetch.\n  The registered squash bypasses obsolete queue entries with the word at the\n  corrected PC. An available consumed target leaves zero occupancy; an\n  available unconsumed target becomes the sole head; an unavailable target\n  clears occupancy and retries the same PC. PC advances exactly once per\n  accepted target fetch. `imem_addr` remains directly assigned from PC.\n- `cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv`: replaced immediate redirect arbitration\n  with squash qualification. Fresh target decode ignores the killed younger\n  load-to-MUL interlock and divider wait while retaining older-memory holds\n  and the ordinary load-to-MUL bubble.\n- `cores/bench/rtl/core.sv`: wired immediate redirect/target to IF PC recovery\n  and the registered event to IF queue handling and hazard arbitration.\n  Retirement, forwarding provenance and top-level ports were preserved.\n\nThe 64x2 folded-PC bimodal table, weakly-taken reset, Boolean saturation,\naligned legal BRANCH/JAL predecode and EX training boundary are unchanged.\nThere is no extra target register, fetch-address mux, training pipeline,\ntarget table,\n…[36653 of 39725 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a14d6d2671c3ab93]…\n the\nregistered valid EX load. No contract files or nret changes are included.\n\nThe forecast is an eight-percent fitness improvement, with low confidence;\nthis early-load circuit has not been implemented or measured. The new\nOF address adder, dmem ownership mux and store-to-load serialization are\nmaterial costs, and the unchanged divider can still limit Fmax. The\nselective load-address interlock trades some cycle savings for keeping\ncurrent EX arithmetic and live load data out of the address adder. Do not\nassume that every current load-use bubble disappears or infer a gain from\nan IPC result alone. Acceptance requires fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec.\nFor a five-percent reduction from the champion's bracketed cycle count,\nmedian Gowin Fmax must exceed approximately 69.94 MHz; at unchanged cycles\nit must exceed approximately 73.62 MHz. Measure canonical CoreMark cycles\nbetween the MMIO markers, validate all five CRCs and the UART literal,\nand run every unchanged formal/cosim gate and scored placement option.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
