{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261004-002-r4s1':\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Restructure only the shared multicycle divider into one preparation\nclock, five clocks that each process three radix-4 digits (six dividend\nbits), and one terminal clock that processes a single radix-4 digit\n(two bits) and restores the result sign. This consumes exactly 32 bits\nin seven RUN clocks, preserving the existing completion schedule and\nall pipeline boundaries. The recurring datapath has three dependent\nsubtract/select stages instead of five; the terminal path has one\ndigit stage followed by sign restoration.\n\nAt the accepted launch edge L, capture the dividend magnitude, divisor\nmagnitude D, operation and sign flags exactly as today. Do not compute\n3D on the launch path: it already includes forwarding and potentially\nlive load data. At edge L+1, use the captured D to register the unsigned\n34-bit value 3D = zero_extend(D) + (zero_extend(D) << 1), while retaining\nquotient and remainder unchanged. D and 2D are explicitly widened to\n34 bits from the captured divisor; 2D is a wiring shift. All RUN digit\narithmetic uses these registered sources, never live operands.\n\nReuse one physical chain of three radix-4 digit cells on edges L+2\nthrough L+6. Each cell forms the 34-bit unsigned trial\nT = {remainder[31:0], quotient[31:30]} and computes T-D, T-2D and T-3D\nin parallel as explicitly zero-extended 35-bit subtractions. Bit 34\nindicates borrow; do not implement a comparison followed by a second\nsubtraction. Let ok1, ok2 and ok3 be the three no-borrow predicates.\nAppend quotient digit {ok2, ok3 | (ok1 & !ok2)}. Select the low 32 bits\nof the next remainder using disjoint masks !ok1, ok1 & !ok2,\nok2 & !ok3 and ok3 on T and the respective differences, expressed as\na parallel masked OR rather than cascaded priority muxes. Shift the\nquotient by two per cell and register the third cell's outputs after\neach full group. For nonzero D the restored remainder is below D,\nso 32-bit remainder storage is sufficient even for large divisors.\nPreserve the high bits of 2D, 3D and T until borrow detection.\n\nOn edge L+7, use only the\n…[1370 of 4442 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a4329c8bd8668fbb]…\ndecoder legality and nret=1 remain as implemented.\nConsecutive divides must retain their nine-cycle zero-wait retirement\ngap and redirects immediately to a divide their ten-cycle gap. Preserve\nevery existing latency, arithmetic, RVFI and side-effect assertion.\nNo predictor, cache, additional CPU stage or retirement-width change\nis part of this structural divider folding and retiming hypothesis.\n\nExpect a 12 percent fitness gain from shortening the measured recurring\ndivider path with unchanged CoreMark cycles. Confidence is medium:\nparallel trials increase area and divisor fanout, and integer/load\nforwarding or the launch path may become the next frequency limit.\nValidate both arithmetic modes and the unchanged formal/cosim gates,\ncanonical CoreMark CRCs and UART literal, bounded accesses and marker\ntiming. Judge the result by median Gowin Fmax times iterations/cycle;\nthe candidate must exceed 119.16032 iter/sec to clear the champion's\n4.6 percent acceptance margin. RTL-only timing estimates do not suffice.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_36", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r13s1.yaml')\nd=dict(\n id='hyp-20261004-002-r13s1',\n title='Spatial divider stages remove shared feedback and narrow each quotient window',\n category='structural',\n motivation='''The champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz in 4,024,573 timed\nCoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The structural history repeatedly\nimproves by shortening division; r4s1 still reused one physical digit\nchain, whereas this proposal removes that reuse. Recent multiplier\npipelining and early load execution regressed. The latest neighboring\nattempts also expose the shared divider as the limiting path. Local\nscratch separation of operand-payload enables did not establish a gain;\nremoving launch qualification from divider payload capture measured only\n64.099 MHz median. The remaining opportunity is to remove the feedback\nand bootstrap/body selection network, rather than further tune it.\n''',\n hypothesis='''Replace only the reused full-width divider body with five physically\ndistinct registered prefix stages. Preserve the accepted EX-only launch,\nexisting four-bit launch computation, six-bit narrow bootstrap, six RUN\nclocks, terminal two-bit publication and start/busy/result-valid/consume\ninterface. This is a spatial unrolling and width specialization of the\nexisting divider, not an additional CPU instruction stage or a faster\nformal-only implementation.\n\nAt launch L retain the magnitude suffix, four-bit quotient/remainder,\nfull unsigned divisor, signedness flags and captured narrow multiples.\nAt L+1 run the existing six-bit bootstrap once, register the resulting\nten-bit remainder and quotient state, and prepare full-width 3D from\nregistered D as today. Hold those bootstrap registers afterward; they\nmust no longer be overwritten by the recurring body.\n\nAt L+2, L+3, L+4, L+5 and L+6 advance into separate body registers after\n14, 18, 22, 26 and 30 processed dividend bits respectively. Each stage\ncontains two radix-4 trial/subtract/select cells. Its first cell has an\nN-2-bit window and its second an N-bit window, where N is that stage's\nprocessed-bit count. Inputs come only from the preceding stage's flops,\nnever a mux over feedback and bootstrap results. Use statically sized\nremainder fields: 10 bits after bootstrap, then 14/18/22/26/30 bits.\nQuotient storage may remain 32 bits initially; explicitly size arithmetic\nand trim dead quotient storage where synthesis does not already do so.\nNo stage may recompute the preceding stage combinationally.\n\nA prefix after p dividend bits is below 2\"'^p, including when D=0, so its\ntrial window and restored remainder need only p bits. For a p-bit trial\nwindow T, trial multiple M in {D,2D,3D} is eligible only when all full\n34-bit multiple bits above p-1 are zero. Compute diff as the p+1-bit\nzero-extended subtraction of T and M[p-1:0]; ok is eligibility AND no\nborrow. Preserve the exact full multiples and explicit upper-bit check:\ntruncating a large divisor or multiple without this check is incorrect.\nUse the current quotient-digit equations and disjoint masked-OR remainder\nselection. Keep native subtraction/carry inference; do not substitute\ncustom carry-lookahead arithmetic or a priority comparator/subtractor.\n\nUse one shared held D and 3D per operation: only one division is active,\nand stage consumers never overlap the next launch. Capture each stage\nonce on its matching RUN phase, keep earlier intermediate registers\nstable afterward, and hold the final thirty-bit state throughout READY.\nDo not select a completed state through a phase-indexed wide mux. The\nexisting independent terminal bank reads the final stage directly,\nprocesses the last two dividend bits, applies signed quotient/remainder\ncandidate correction and publishes the result without another clock.\nEnter READY immediately after L+6 and consume at L+7 when EX/MEM accepts,\nexactly as the champion. On consume/relaunch, the old final state is\nobserved by the consumer before the new launch updates shared operands.\n\nReset cancels every valid phase. Reject starts while busy and retain\nREADY output until consume. Preserve divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, signed\nremainder rules and the exact ALTOPS formulas with the identical six-RUN\nschedule. Keep EX operands, RVFI metadata, division ownership, branch\nrecovery, forwarding, load-use bubbles, held-WB provenance, memory\nhandshakes and nret=1 top-level IO unchanged. Consecutive divides retain\nthe eight-cycle retirement gap; redirect-to-divide retains the unchanged\nten-cycle progress bound. No evaluation file or correctness check changes.\n\nThis trades duplicated arithmetic and intermediate flops for eliminating\nthe shared feedback mux and narrowing the two dependent trial banks.\nAn eight-percent fitness improvement is a low-confidence forecast; extra\nrouting, stationary-divisor fanout and the unchanged EX-to-OF path may\nlimit the benefit. Require the final median Gowin Fmax times canonical\nmarker-bracketed iterations/cycle above 182.92448 iter/sec, approximately\n73.62 MHz at unchanged cycles. Validate all real/ALTOPS divider tests,\npipeline tests, unchanged formal/cosim gates, every CRC, UART literal,\nmemory bounds and all scored placement options.\n'\"''',\n expected_impact={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n changes=[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'Replace the shared two-digit body and bootstrap/body feedback mux with five distinct registered prefix stages after 14/18/22/26/30 bits. Hold shared operands, bootstrap and final READY state. Preserve launch, bootstrap, terminal/sign publication, arithmetic semantics, reset and exact six-RUN real/ALTOPS schedule.'},\n {'file':'rtl/div_prefix_digit.sv','description':'Add a statically parameterized radix-4 prefix cell with p-bit window, p+1-bit native trial subtractions, explicit full-multiple upper-bit eligibility, current quotient digit equations and disjoint masked-OR restoration. Instantiate two cells per spatial body stage without a feedback connection.'},\n {'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'Test every prefix-width boundary, large D/2D/3D values that truncate to deceptively small lows, zero divisor, all signed corner cases, random exact quotient/remainder, rejected starts, consume/relaunch, reset in each phase and READY retention. Keep exact six-clock completion assertions in real and ALTOPS modes; include the new module in standalone build sources.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'Include the new divider cell in standalone EX builds and retain every captured-operand, exact-result, busy/held-result, launch-isolation and completion-latency assertion. Exercise memory stalls across intermediate and READY phases without changing EX producer availability.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add large-divisor and prefix-boundary divide/consumer chains under directed/random bus stalls and redirects. Preserve all existing full RVFI checks, eight-cycle consecutive-divide and ten-cycle progress checks, wrong-path suppression, retirement ordering and memory side-effect assertions.'}\n ])\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Refined hypothesis written and schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
