publishes the result without another clock.\nEnter READY immediately after L+6 and consume at L+7 when EX/MEM accepts,\nexactly as the champion. On consume/relaunch, the old final state is\nobserved by the consumer before the new launch updates shared operands.\n\nReset cancels every valid phase. Reject starts while busy and retain\nREADY output until consume. Preserve divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, signed\nremainder rules and the exact ALTOPS formulas with the identical six-RUN\nschedule. Keep EX operands, RVFI metadata, division ownership, branch\nrecovery, forwarding, load-use bubbles, held-WB provenance, memory\nhandshakes and nret=1 top-level IO unchanged. Consecutive divides retain\nthe eight-cycle retirement gap; redirect-to-divide retains the unchanged\nten-cycle progress bound. No evaluation file or correctness check changes.\n\nThis trades duplicated arithmetic and intermediate flops for eliminating\nthe shared feedback mux and narrowing the two dependent trial banks.\nAn eight-percent fitness improvement is a low-confidence forecast; extra\nrouting, stationary-divisor fanout and the unchanged EX-to-OF path may\nlimit the benefit. Require the final median Gowin Fmax times canonical\nmarker-bracketed iterations/cycle above 182.92448 iter/sec, approximately\n73.62 MHz at unchanged cycles. Validate all real/ALTOPS divider tests,\npipeline tests, unchanged formal/cosim gates, every CRC, UART literal,\nmemory bounds and all scored placement options.\n'\"''',\n expected_impact={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n changes=[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'Replace the shared two-digit body and bootstrap/body feedback mux with five distinct registered prefix stages after 14/18/22/26/30 bits. Hold shared operands, bootstrap and final READY state. Preserve launch, bootstrap, terminal/sign publication, arithmetic semantics, reset and exact six-RUN real/ALTOPS schedule.'},\n {'file':'rtl/div_prefix_digit.sv','description':'Add a statically parameterize