{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r13s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Feedforward divider stages and independent operand capture break execution feedback'\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('Replace only the reused full-width divider body with five physically\\\\ndistinct registered prefix stages.','Replace the reused full-width divider body with five physically\\\\ndistinct registered prefix stages, and separate OF/EX wide payload\\\\ncapture from the narrow instruction-valid token.')\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('Keep EX operands, RVFI metadata, division ownership, branch\\\\nrecovery, forwarding, load-use bubbles, held-WB provenance, memory\\\\nhandshakes and nret=1 top-level IO unchanged.','Preserve EX operand correctness, RVFI metadata, division ownership,\\\\nbranch recovery latency, forwarding priority, load-use bubbles, held-WB\\\\nprovenance, memory handshakes and nret=1 top-level IO.')\nkey='This trades duplicated arithmetic and intermediate flops for eliminating\\\\nthe shared feedback mux and narrowing the two dependent trial banks.'\nreplacement='''At OF/EX, separate payload_hold = dmem_stall OR div_wait from the\nexisting validity controls. Capture the operand/control/PC/instruction\npayload whenever payload_hold is low, including invalid, redirect and\nload-use-bubble cycles. The wide enable must not depend on redirect,\nflush, accept, in.valid or load_use. Flush still kills reg_q.valid with\nits current priority; a load-use event still holds ID/OF and inserts\nexactly one invalid EX token. Recapture the held consumer with correct\nMEM forwarding on its existing next accepting edge. Genuine backend\nholds retain the complete payload. predicted_taken travels with its\npayload and is inert when valid is zero. Keep accepted EX writer,\nbranch-training, redirect, divide-launch and memory side-effect\nqualification unchanged. Invalid speculative payloads must never act.\n\nThis is one structural treatment of execution feedback: spatial stages\nreplace the divider's data feedback mux, while independently captured\noperands remove late squash/dependency signals from wide register\ncontrol. It trades duplicated arithmetic and intermediate flops for\nshorter registered paths. Keep the original forwarding selection logic\nand instruction schedule; do not add predictor, memory, arithmetic or\nlatency optimizations. Standalone spatial unrolling measured 71.000 MHz\nmedian and exact canonical cycles/CRCs, but that 0.88% gain is below the\nacceptance margin. Independent operand capture alone also failed to\nestablish a gain. The proposed combination must therefore be evaluated\nas a new complete circuit, not inferred from either isolated result.'''\nassert key in d['hypothesis']\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace(key,replacement)\nd['changes'][2:2]=[\n {'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'Add payload_hold independent of valid-token arbitration; capture every wide payload field whenever there is no genuine backend hold. Retain reset, true holds and exact valid/flush/load-bubble behavior. Remove accept, in.valid and flush from wide payload enables while preserving all forwarding and x0 rules.'},\n {'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'Export operand_payload_hold = dmem_stall || div_wait, independently of the existing load-use/redirect validity controls. Preserve all architectural stall, flush, bus and retirement behavior.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire independent operand_payload_hold to OF and include the spatial divider module through normal RTL discovery. Preserve every external nret=1 port, WB forwarding provenance and retirement boundary.'},\n {'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'Exercise valid-only squash and harmless invalid payload capture, exact operands and metadata when validity is set, x0 and producer age priority. Retain complete payload-stability assertions for true backend holds; explicitly distinguish those from load-use bubbles and squash cycles.'}\n]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Complete combined structural hypothesis is schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_55", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r13s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Feedforward divider stages and independent operand capture break execution feedback'\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('Replace only the reused full-width divider body with five physically\\\\ndistinct registered prefix stages.','Replace the reused full-width divider body with five physically\\\\ndistinct registered prefix stages, and separate OF/EX wide payload\\\\ncapture from the narrow instruction-valid token.')\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('Keep EX operands, RVFI metadata, division ownership, branch\\\\nrecovery, forwarding, load-use bubbles, held-WB provenance, memory\\\\nhandshakes and nret=1 top-level IO unchanged.','Preserve EX operand correctness, RVFI metadata, division ownership,\\\\nbranch recovery latency, forwarding priority, load-use bubbles, held-WB\\\\nprovenance, memory handshakes and nret=1 top-level IO.')\nkey='This trades duplicated arithmetic and intermediate flops for eliminating\\\\nthe shared feedback mux and narrowing the two dependent trial banks.'\nreplacement='''At OF/EX, separate payload_hold = dmem_stall OR div_wait from the\nexisting validity controls. Capture the operand/control/PC/instruction\npayload whenever payload_hold is low, including invalid, redirect and\nload-use-bubble cycles. The wide enable must not depend on redirect,\nflush, accept, in.valid or load_use. Flush still kills reg_q.valid with\nits current priority; a load-use event still holds ID/OF and inserts\nexactly one invalid EX token. Recapture the held consumer with correct\nMEM forwarding on its existing next accepting edge. Genuine backend\nholds retain the complete payload. predicted_taken travels with its\npayload and is inert when valid is zero. Keep accepted EX writer,\nbranch-training, redirect, divide-launch and memory side-effect\nqualification unchanged. Invalid speculative payloads must never act.\n\nThis is one structural treatment of execution feedback: spatial stages\nreplace the divider's data feedback mux, while independently captured\noperands remove late squash/dependency signals from wide register\ncontrol. It trades duplicated arithmetic and intermediate flops for\nshorter registered paths. Keep the original forwarding selection logic\nand instruction schedule; do not add predictor, memory, arithmetic or\nlatency optimizations. Standalone spatial unrolling measured 71.000 MHz\nmedian and exact canonical cycles/CRCs, but that 0.88% gain is below the\nacceptance margin. Independent operand capture alone also failed to\nestablish a gain. The proposed combination must therefore be evaluated\nas a new complete circuit, not inferred from either isolated result.'''\nassert key in d['hypothesis']\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace(key,replacement)\nd['changes'][2:2]=[\n {'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'Add payload_hold independent of valid-token arbitration; capture every wide payload field whenever there is no genuine backend hold. Retain reset, true holds and exact valid/flush/load-bubble behavior. Remove accept, in.valid and flush from wide payload enables while preserving all forwarding and x0 rules.'},\n {'file':'rtl/hazard_unit.sv','description':'Export operand_payload_hold = dmem_stall || div_wait, independently of the existing load-use/redirect validity controls. Preserve all architectural stall, flush, bus and retirement behavior.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire independent operand_payload_hold to OF and include the spatial divider module through normal RTL discovery. Preserve every external nret=1 port, WB forwarding provenance and retirement boundary.'},\n {'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'Exercise valid-only squash and harmless invalid payload capture, exact operands and metadata when validity is set, x0 and producer age priority. Retain complete payload-stability assertions for true backend holds; explicitly distinguish those from load-use bubbles and squash cycles.'}\n]\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Complete combined structural hypothesis is schema valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Complete combined structural hypothesis is schema valid\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
