{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r13s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Spatial divider stages with local divisor banks remove shared feedback and fanout'\nh=d['hypothesis']\nh=h.replace('Replace the reused full-width divider body with five physically\\\\ndistinct registered prefix stages, and separate OF/EX wide payload\\\\ncapture from the narrow instruction-valid token.','Replace only the reused full-width divider body with five physically\\\\ndistinct registered prefix stages and local registered divisor banks.')\na=h.index('Use one shared held D and 3D per operation:')\nb=h.index('Reset cancels every valid phase.',a)\nh=h[:a]+'''Retain full D and 3D as the operation's setup state, but do not drive\nall body trial banks directly from these stationary high-fanout flops.\nFor each p=N stage capture local low-N-bit D/2D/3D banks and the six\nfull-multiple eligibility flags needed by its N-2 and N-bit cells on the\npreceding phase's edge. Thus the 14-bit bank captures at bootstrap L+1;\nthe 18/22/26/30-bit banks capture at L+2/L+3/L+4/L+5 respectively, before\ntheir consumers run. Each bank has a different phase enable and holds\nits operands throughout its consuming stage. This temporal distinction\nmust survive synthesis; do not use identical same-edge copies that the\ntool can merge. Body trial subtraction and digit selection read only\nthe matching local multiple flops and registered eligibility flags.\nThe arithmetic borrow must still be combined with its saved eligibility.\n\nFor the first body bank at L+1, form full 3D from registered D and use\nthat same exact widened expression to capture its truncated local 3D\nand both eligibility flags; do not read the old global 3D flop on that\nedge. Later local banks capture the already registered full 3D. Keep\nsetup capture independent of preceding body arithmetic and digit\nselection. Earlier local banks may hold values from a previous operation\nuntil their scheduled capture, but no valid stage may use those stale\nvalues. Reset clears bank state; each accepted operation overwrites\nevery bank before use. Only one division is active, so captured setup\nstate cannot be replaced until consume or consume/relaunch.\n\nCapture each remainder/quotient stage once on its matching RUN phase,\nand hold the final thirty-bit state throughout READY. No completed-state\nphase-indexed wide mux is permitted. The existing terminal bank reads\nthe final stage directly and retains full D/2D/3D for the last two-bit\ntrials and parallel signed-result candidates, without another clock.\nEnter READY after L+6 and consume at L+7 when EX/MEM accepts, exactly\nas the champion. On consume/relaunch the consumer observes the old\ncompleted result before new launch state takes effect.\n\n'''+h[b:]\na=h.index('At OF/EX, separate payload_hold')\nb=h.index('An eight-percent fitness improvement',a)\nh=h[:a]+'''This is one structural divider change: a feedforward chain of distinct\nprefix stages with local registered arithmetic operands replaces shared\nrecurring state, feedback selection and stationary divisor fanout.\nLeave OF capture, accepted EX producer qualification, branch recovery,\nprediction, memory execution and multiplication exactly as in the parent.\n\nA scratch spatial prototype using stationary shared multiples measured\n67.274/71.000/71.000 MHz, 5,298 LUT4s and 1,245 FFs. It passed all 31\npipeline tests, eight EX tests and the real-divider arithmetic suite;\ncanonical stalled CoreMark retained exactly 4,024,573 marker-bracketed\ncycles, all five CRCs, the validation literal and no out-of-bounds access.\nIts approximately 0.88% fitness gain is below acceptance. Local operand\nand eligibility banks are therefore essential to this final proposal;\nthe final banked circuit is unmeasured, and no acceptance is claimed.\nA separate capture-control variant regressed and is excluded.\n\n'''+h[b:]\nh=h.replace('extra\\\\nrouting, stationary-divisor fanout and the unchanged EX-to-OF path may\\\\nlimit the benefit.','extra\\\\nrouting, local-bank setup paths and the unchanged EX-to-OF path may\\\\nlimit the benefit.')\nd['hypothesis']=h\nd['changes']=[c for c in d['changes'] if c['file'] not in ('rtl/operand_stage.sv','rtl/hazard_unit.sv','rtl/core.sv','test/test_operand_stage.py')]\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Replace shared body feedback with separate 14/18/22/26/30-bit register stages and phase-staggered local D/2D/3D banks plus exact full-multiple eligibility flags. Capture each bank before use, prepare first-bank 3D from registered D at bootstrap, and hold setup/final state. Preserve launch, bootstrap, terminal publication, real/ALTOPS schedule, arithmetic and handshake semantics.'\nd['changes'][1]['description']='Add a statically parameterized radix-4 prefix cell consuming local truncated multiple flops and registered full-width eligibility flags. Use p+1-bit native trial subtraction, exact borrow qualification, existing digit equations and masked-OR restoration. Two independent cells feed each spatial stage; no live global-multiple reduction or feedback mux enters their selection cone.'\nd['changes'][2]['description'] += ' Check local bank preparation before use, first-bank same-edge 3D preparation, stale-bank isolation across consecutive different divisors and exact eligibility boundaries for both cells in every stage.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert d['category']=='structural' and type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Final hypothesis written and schema valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
