261004-003-r1s2', 'category': 'predictor', 'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 12.59, 'delta_pct': 3.88, 'fmax_mhz': 5.292, 'cycles': 4201766, 'lut4': 13072, 'ff': 620, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -195.565, 'arrival_ns': 205.859, 'logic_cells': 153, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261004-001-r2s0', 'category': 'micro_opt', 'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 94.28, 'delta_pct': 31.77, 'fmax_mhz': 42.346, 'cycles': 4491485, 'lut4': 3297, 'ff': 675, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_31_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_4_s0', 'slack_ns': -20.012, 'arrival_ns': 30.307, 'logic_cells': 132, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}}\n{'id': 'hyp-20261004\n…[15180 of 18252 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f70c9116be067b6a]…\n\ndivision operand capture and DONE retention, real/ALTOPS completion\nlatency, nine-cycle consecutive-divide and ten-cycle redirect-to-divide\nretirement bounds, strict RVFI order, decoder default-illegal behavior,\nEBREAK-only SYSTEM legality, and every nret=1 top-level port.\nNo fetch queue, predictor, cache, arithmetic algorithm change, or extra\npipeline stage is part of this hypothesis.\n\nThe predicted fitness gain is 8 percent with medium confidence. The\nfull-bypass experiment saved about 4.5 percent of cycles; selective\ninterlocking sacrifices some of those savings to remove its worst\ntimed memory-to-multiplier path. Combined with the measured opportunity\nto shorten branch feedback, this may clear the 4.6 percent acceptance\nmargin. The unchanged divider remains a competing clock limit.\nValidate the final implementation with unchanged formal/cosim gates,\ncanonical CoreMark CRCs, bounded memory accesses, marker-bracketed\ncycles, and median Gowin Fmax; exploratory timing is not a formal proof.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
