{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='structural' and d.get('round_id',0)>1:\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(d['id'], '\\\\n',h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-002-r2s1 \n Restructure only the shared divider's sequential datapath from four\ngroups of eight restoring bit steps to six groups of five steps and\none final group of two steps. Reuse one physical chain of five 33-bit\nsubtract/restore cells and register quotient and remainder after each\nfull five-bit group. Widen the group counter to three bits. Keep\noperand-magnitude and sign capture at the accepted launch edge. This\ncuts the recurring arithmetic depth from eight cells to five and\nreduces divisor fanout and replicated divider logic.\n\nRemove the separate SIGN state. On the seventh RUN edge, form the\nregistered result directly from quotient_step[2] and remainder_step[2],\napplying the captured quotient or remainder sign and operation selection\nbefore entering DONE. Use the final combinational step outputs, not the\nold quotient_q/remainder_q values, and do not execute three padding\nsteps after processing all 32 dividend bits. Compute quotient and\nremainder sign corrections in parallel, then select the requested\nresult. The terminal path contains only two restoring steps plus sign\ncorrection, keeping it shorter than the five-step recurring path.\nAn accepted launch at edge L must assert result_valid immediately after\nedge L+7; DONE retains the registered result until consume. With the\nexisting EX launch/transfer protocol, consecutive divides have a\nnine-cycle zero-wait RVFI retirement gap; the extra recovery cycle for\na taken branch followed by a divide still fits the ten-cycle limit.\nPreserve that bound and the existing formal liveness configuration.\n\nGive real arithmetic and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS precisely the same seven-RUN\nschedule. ALTOPS still captures the exact existing subtraction/XOR\nformula and publishes it only on the seventh RUN edge. Preserve all\nsigned/unsigned quotient and remainder results, including zero divisors\nand INT_MIN/-1. Retain the existing rule that quotient sign inversion\nis disabled for divisor zero, and that signed remainder follows only\nthe dividend sign. Keep start/busy/result_\n…[8448 of 11520 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ba41d1a550558ce1]…\ndecoder legality and nret=1 remain as implemented.\nConsecutive divides must retain their nine-cycle zero-wait retirement\ngap and redirects immediately to a divide their ten-cycle gap. Preserve\nevery existing latency, arithmetic, RVFI and side-effect assertion.\nNo predictor, cache, additional CPU stage or retirement-width change\nis part of this structural divider folding and retiming hypothesis.\n\nExpect a 12 percent fitness gain from shortening the measured recurring\ndivider path with unchanged CoreMark cycles. Confidence is medium:\nparallel trials increase area and divisor fanout, and integer/load\nforwarding or the launch path may become the next frequency limit.\nValidate both arithmetic modes and the unchanged formal/cosim gates,\ncanonical CoreMark CRCs and UART literal, bounded accesses and marker\ntiming. Judge the result by median Gowin Fmax times iterations/cycle;\nthe candidate must exceed 119.16032 iter/sec to clear the champion's\n4.6 percent acceptance margin. RTL-only timing estimates do not suffice.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
