ind a faster formal-only completion path.\n\nLaunch exactly once for a valid legal divide in ID/EX when the older MEM\ninstruction can advance. Capture the forwarded operands and their RVFI\nvalues before holding the instruction, since forwarding sources can\ndisappear while older instructions drain. Hold PC and ID/EX during the\noperation; allow older EX/MEM and MEM/WB instructions to drain once,\ninserting EX/MEM bubbles instead of repeatedly issuing the old instruction.\nExisting dmem backpressure must still hold an outstanding memory request.\nRetain a completed division result until EX/MEM accepts it, then publish\nit exactly once through the normal forwarding, writeback, and single\nchannel RVFI paths. Qualify redirects and side effects with valid and\nactual stage advance so stalls ca\n…[22176 of 25248 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:47e8346f7a73ad4c]…\nt=1 ports, decoder default-illegal behavior, EBREAK-only\nSYSTEM legality, traps, operand forwarding, arithmetic, seven-clock\nreal/ALTOPS division schedule, held completions, strict RVFI order,\nand the unchanged formal liveness window. This single structural change\ntargets overlap of independent bus and backend stalls. The projected\nseven percent fitness gain is an estimate, not a measured cycle result;\nthe extra head mux and queue control are material FPGA timing risks.\nRequire fitness above 132.15164 iterations/second, using median Gowin\nFmax times canonical marker-bracketed CoreMark iterations/cycle, with\nevery existing formal, cosim, CRC, UART, and memory-bound gate passing.\n\nPATH: {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_4_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -14.544, 'arrival_ns': 24.838, 'logic_cells': 152, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}\nNOTES: \nhyp-20261004-003-r5s2 predictor regression 122.03 48.634 3985515 Pipeline predictor training to isolate branch-comparator fanout\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
