{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"The six-bit launch prefix also created a long path, even with registered-only operands. I’m moving the prefix work behind the existing operand register: a dedicated first RUN stage will process ten bits, followed by five four-bit groups and the existing two-bit final group. This keeps the seven-clock schedule."}}
