stages instead of five; the terminal path has one\ndigit stage followed by sign restoration.\n\nAt the accepted launch edge L, capture the dividend magnitude, divisor\nmagnitude D, operation and sign flags exactly as today. Do not compute\n3D on the launch path: it already includes forwarding and potentially\nlive load data. At edge L+1, use the captured D to register the unsigned\n34-bit value 3D = zero_extend(D) + (zero_extend(D) << 1), while retaining\nquotient and remainder unchanged. D and 2D are explicitly widened to\n34 bits from the captured divisor; 2D is a wiring shift. All RUN digit\narithmetic uses these registered sources, never live oper\n…[12164 of 15236 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c8c2a9d4dc7671d9]…\n(INT_MIN,-1)=INT_MIN and REM(INT_MIN,-1)=0.\nKeep exact ALTOPS subtraction/XOR formulas and identical seven-RUN\ncompletion timing in real and formal builds. Preserve EX forwarded\noperand/RVFI capture, single publication, pipeline draining and dmem\nholds, nine-cycle consecutive-divide and ten-cycle redirect-to-divide\nretirement gaps, nret=1 ports, strict RVFI order, decoder legality,\nmultiplier isolation, fetch queue, predictor and all correctness gates.\n\nExpect eight percent fitness improvement at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\nConfidence is medium pending vendor timing: prefix selection, the final\nfour-bit/sign path, or existing integer/multiplier paths may cap Fmax.\nSpatial probe timings are evidence against full duplication, not\nmeasurements of the final asymmetric circuit. Require fitness above\n140.78114 iter/sec; unchanged-cycle median Gowin Fmax must exceed\n53.91084 MHz. Preserve canonical CRCs, UART validation, bounded accesses\nand MMIO timing brackets, and evaluate the final median vendor timing.\n\nnotes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
