{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_41", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r9s1.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='Retimed two-digit radix-4 divider with parallel terminal publication'\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'].replace('''Keep the existing final\ntwo-bit lookahead and parallel sign restoration physically independent\nof the feedback cells. They read held quotient_q/remainder_q and the\nregistered divisor/triple, and publish directly into EX/MEM at L+8.''','''Keep final two-bit lookahead physically independent of the feedback\ncells. It reads held quotient_q/remainder_q and the registered D/3D,\nand publishes directly into EX/MEM at L+8. Prepare all four possible\nsigned architectural results in parallel before selecting the final\ndigit, so late borrow decisions do not feed sign or operation muxes.''')\nanchor='''arithmetic, introduce padding bits, add a result register or extend\nlatency. READY state, data and valid remain stable during delayed consume,\nchanging live inputs and rejected starts.\n'''\naddition='''\nFor terminal T={held_R,held_Q[31:30]}, retain widened parallel\nT-D, T-2D and T-3D differences and their borrow-derived success bits.\nUse disjoint terminal masks \"'!ok1, ok1 & !ok2, ok2 & !ok3, and ok3.\nFor each constant final digit k=0..3, prepare positive remainder\n(T-kD)[31:0] and negative remainder (kD-T)[31:0] in parallel, with\nk=0 using T and -T. Prepare quotient {held_Q[29:0],2'\"'(k)} and its\nnegative: for k=0 use {(30'd0-held_Q[29:0]),2'b00}; for k>0 use\n{~held_Q[29:0],(2'd0-2'(k))}. These are exact constant-digit negations,\nincluding the upper carry when k=0. Captured remainder/quotient sign\nand select_rem flags choose one architectural result per candidate\nbefore the final masks. Publish the masked OR of those four candidates.\nThis replaces the terminal priority mux followed by sign/op selection\nwith a parallel result bank at the same publication boundary; no\nselected digit drives a new wide negate or post-selection sign mux.\n'''\nassert anchor in h['hypothesis']\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'].replace(anchor,anchor+addition)\na=h['hypothesis'].index('A scratch implementation of this exact partition')\nb=h['hypothesis'].index('\\\\nAcceptance requires',a)\nh['hypothesis']=h['hypothesis'][:a]+'''A scratch implementation of this exact partition and parallel terminal\npublication passed existing real/ALTOPS divider tests, EX-divider tests\nand the full pipeline test runner. Gowin placement options 0/1/2 measured\n62.203/62.337/62.337 MHz, median 62.337 MHz, using 4,438 LUTs and\n963 FFs, versus the champion's 4,292 LUTs and 963 FFs. At unchanged\nCoreMark cycles, this projects approximately 154.89 iter/sec, a 5.53\npercent gain. The feedback-only version reached 62.021 MHz; preparing\nsigned terminal candidates before digit selection improved publication\nmargin without altering completion timing. These are scratch timing\nand simulation results; the final implemented circuit must still pass\nall evaluator gates. Confidence is medium because the measured margin\nabove the 4.6 percent acceptance threshold is less than one percentage\npoint and other execution/control paths now limit frequency.\n'''+h['hypothesis'][b:]\nh['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'medium'}\nh['changes'][0]['description']='''Retain the two-bit launch and seven-RUN/held-READY protocol. Specialize\ngroup zero as four seven-bit prefix steps alongside registered 34-bit\n3D preparation; reuse two full-width radix-4 parallel-trial cells on\ngroups one through six. Keep terminal arithmetic physically independent,\nand prepare each constant-digit signed quotient/remainder and requested\noperation before disjoint final-digit selection. Publish their masked\nOR directly to EX/MEM. Preserve exact real/ALTOPS latency, all corner\ncases, held-state stability and existing handshake ports.\n'''\nclass LiteralDumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_string(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nLiteralDumper.add_representer(str,represent_string)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=LiteralDumper,sort_keys=False,width=95))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('VALID',p)\nprint('Projected fitness:',62.337e6*10/4024573)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
