{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|r8s2|r9s2|return|history|branch prediction' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share a radix-4 combinational divider across RV32M divide and remainder\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline's worst timed path is 199.837 ns across 156 cells and passes\\nthrough forwarding and the combinational ALU. Its 5.442 MHz Fmax strongly\\nsuggests that the deeply unrolled divide/remainder arithmetic dominates\\nfitness. alu.sv currently expresses signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder separately. Improving this timed arithmetic cone can increase\\nCoreMark iterations/second without changing instruction throughput or\\nadding pipeline control under the approximately 22% memory stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline's worst timed path is 199.837 ns across 156 cells and passes\\nthrough forwarding and the combinational ALU. Its 5.442 MHz Fmax strongly\\nsuggests that the deeply unrolled divide/remainder arithmetic dominates\\nfitness. alu.sv currently expresses signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder separately. Improving this timed arithmetic cone can increase\\nCoreMark iterations/second without changing instruction throughput or\\nadding pipeline control under the approximately 22% memory stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU implementations with one\\nshared, fully combinational unsigned radix-4 restoring divmod network.\\nConvert operands to unsigned magnitudes for signed DIV/REM, run sixteen\\ndependent steps that consume two dividend bits and emit two quotient\\nbits each, then apply the quotient and remainder signs. Each step forms\\nT = {previous_remainder[31:0], next_dividend_pair}, computes T-D, T-2D,\\nand T-3D in parallel, and chooses the largest nonnegative trial. Derive\\nboth each trial's borrow and its candidate remainder from the same\\nsubtraction; avoid a serial comparator followed by a second subtractor.\\nPrecompute the 34-bit D, 2D, and 3D once. Use 35-bit zero-extended trial\\nsubtractions so bit 34 indicates borrow, and retain only the selected\\nlow 32 remainder bits between steps:\n…[250831 of 253903 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4faa701bf7f9eb0a]…\nction and new training outputs;\\nretain all real/ALTOPS arithmetic, launch, stall and latency checks.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_operand_stage.py\", \"description\": \"Update bundle packing and assert context capture/hold/flush alongside\\nthe existing independent operand-forwarding and interlock checks.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 137.2, \"delta_pct\": -6.52, \"vs_baseline\": 1032.01, \"fmax_mhz\": 54.954, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4005415, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4746, \"ff\": 1239, \"seeds\": [56.93, 54.954, 54.954], \"perturbations\": [[0, 56.93, 27], [1, 54.954, 27], [2, 54.954, 27]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_0_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_1_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -12.565, \"arrival_ns\": 22.86, \"logic_cells\": 132, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 27, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T19:13:09.677532Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
