{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor' and d.get('round_id') in (4,5,6):\n  print(d['id'], d['title'], d.get('fitness'), d.get('fmax_mhz'), d.get('cycles'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-003-r4s2 Folded-PC bimodal prediction with one-bit recovery 126.34 50.352 3985515\nAdd one compact direct-control-flow predictor to the current champion:\na fixed 64-entry bimodal table of two-bit saturating counters, reset to\nweakly taken (10), indexed by fetch PC[7:2] XOR PC[13:8]. This is a generic\naddress hash with no benchmark-PC constants, software annotations or\naddress-range assumption. Predecode legal RV32I BRANCH funct3 values and\nJAL from raw imem_data. Predict a conditional branch taken from the\nselected counter's MSB; predict JAL taken unconditionally. Form exact\nsign-extended B/J targets, and predict only word-aligned targets. All\nother instructions, including JALR and reserved branch encodings,\npredict PC+4. No BTB, return stack, global/local history, instruction\nbuffer, memory change, arithmetic change or new stage is proposed.\n\nCarry only predicted_taken through if_id_t and id_ex_t, captured with\nthe accepted instruction and held with it during backend stalls. The\nhash depends solely on instruction PC, so EX recomputes the identical\ntraining index from registered in.pc; no stored prediction index or\n32-bit predicted_next_pc is needed. Lookup sees old registered counter\nstate, with no combinational training bypass. Use per-entry decoded\nwrite enables and local Boolean saturation logic, as in the successful\nprior implementation refinement, rather than reading the indexed\ncounter through a second mux for training. Only the MSB needs a fetch\nread mux. Keep raw predecode separate from the full legality decoder.\n\nIn EX recover conditional branches only when effective_taken XOR the\ncaptured predicted_taken bit is one. Effective taken includes legal\ninstruction validation and absence of a target-alignment trap. Select\nthe conditional recovery address from the registered prediction bit:\nPC+4 after an incorrect taken guess, direct branch target after an\nincorrect not-taken guess. Keep the late operand comparator out of this\ntarget-selection mux and avoid a wide actual-versus-predicted-PC test.\nC\n…[8870 of 11942 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:28b36764583b249a]…\nrement stage. Preserve all decoder\nlegality and alignment traps, actual RVFI operands/targets/links,\nnret=1 IO, +1 retirement order, symbolic liveness, bus handshakes,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART and bounds checks.\n\nThe intended timing gain comes from removing the live load comparator\nfrom queue-head decode, queue payload enables and younger-ID control,\nwhile retaining only its immediate PC update and accepted training\nendpoints. A broader local prototype with a registered target and\nfetch-address mux matched 3,829,487 canonical cycles and passed stalled\nselftest plus all three random-program cosims, but its timing regressed.\nThat evidence motivates this narrower one-bit control split and\nvalidity-only kill; it does not establish a fitness improvement.\nAcceptance still requires fitness above 140.78114, or approximately\n53.914 MHz median Fmax at unchanged cycles. The unchanged divider and\ninteger datapath may prevent that gain; confidence is low. Evaluate\nall placement options and unchanged correctness gates.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
