{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema,shutil\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r11s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-003-r11s2',\n 'title':'Predecode branch prediction verification polarity at the operand boundary',\n 'category':'predictor',\n 'motivation':'''The champion achieves 174.88 iter/sec at median 70.381 MHz and 4,024,573 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior target, loop, return-shadow and tagged-history supplements saved few cycles and lost frequency; delayed training and registered squash also regressed. A fresh unchanged-parent Gowin option-0 run reproduces 69.480 MHz and the reported 19.498 ns worst path: OF/EX operand flop, ordering comparator, train_taken selection, recovery control, OF operand mux, multiplier input register. Comparator output has fanout 194. Divider feedback paths are almost tied, so increasing predictor complexity is particularly risky.\n\nLocal scratch checks of narrower operand kills, payload-enable splits, deferred training/squash and smaller predictor tables did not beat the champion. This motivates retaining its exact predictor behavior and immediate recovery while shortening verification itself. Current direction verification selects and possibly complements the actual branch condition, then XORs the captured prediction. The condition's true/complement polarity and predicted direction are both known before EX and need not be combined after operand comparison.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Add one branch_recovery_invert bit to OF/EX, computed at the existing accepting operand edge as in.ctrl.branch_op[0] XOR in.predicted_taken. All six legal branch encodings use funct3 bit zero for relation inversion: BEQ/BLT/BLTU use the base comparison, while BNE/BGE/BGEU use its complement. Thus a direction mismatch can be computed in EX by applying the already registered combined polarity directly to the base operand comparison.\n\nRetain the existing actual branch_cond computation for architectural branch_taken, RVFI pc_next and counter training. Compute branch_pred_wrong separately: BEQ/BNE use (rs1 == rs2) XOR branch_recovery_invert; BLT/BGE use signed (rs1 < rs2) XOR that bit; BLTU/BGEU use unsigned (rs1 < rs2) XOR that bit; default remains zero. Express the inversion inside each relation arm so the late comparison does not first pass through the actual-condition output and its branch-operation polarity selection. The synthesis tool may share base comparators, but recovery must consume this direct verification result rather than branch_cond XOR predicted_taken. Do not rewrite the existing comparators into a different arithmetic engine.\n\nPreserve the exact misalignment convention. Conditional mismatch is misalign_fault ? in.predicted_taken : branch_pred_wrong, inside the existing accepted, legal conditional-branch qualification. This is algebraically equivalent to effective_taken XOR predicted_taken, including a taken branch whose target traps. Keep the current valid/nonstalled/nondivide EX acceptance gate and aligned JALR redirect. The original predicted_taken bit still selects the conditional recovery address: predicted taken selects PC+4, predicted not taken selects the branch target. Retain exact JAL prediction, JALR target calculation and bit-zero clearing, actual RVFI next PCs, link-write suppression on traps, and unchanged recovery latency.\n\nCapture the new polarity atomically with operands, PC, controls and prediction under the existing OF acceptance condition. Preserve it on OF/EX holds; reset clears it with the bundle. A flush kills validity exactly as today, and an invalid payload's polarity cannot authorize recovery or any other side effect. Add no new field to fetch entries, IF/ID or ID/OF: their existing decoded branch_op and captured predicted_taken already provide the inputs. EX/MEM and MEM/WB need no polarity field because recovery completes in EX. No stage, prediction table, speculative history, training delay, target cache or deferred squash is introduced.\n\nKeep the folded-PC 64x2 table, local Boolean saturation, weakly-taken initialization, raw legal/aligned predecode, old-state updates and exact accepted training events unchanged. Preserve the EX-only divider, integer/multiply forwarding, load-use interlock, queue behavior, bus handshakes, held-WB provenance, decoder legality, alignment traps, nret=1 ports, strict retirement order, symbolic progress and every eval invariant.\n\nThe intended gain is higher frequency at exactly unchanged dynamic instruction and cycle counts; six percent is a low-confidence projection, not an observed result. Divider feedback and placement may prevent a gain even if verification loses a logic level. At unchanged 4,024,573 cycles, acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 73.62 MHz and fitness above 182.92448. Validate both directions of every branch type under arbitrary predictions, signed/unsigned extreme operands, misalignment, loads and divisions, plus reset and independent bus stalls. Keep all formal/cosim checks, canonical CRC/UART validation, memory bounds and marker-bracketed scoring unchanged. Evaluate every scored placement option; do not claim acceptance from an option-0 result alone.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add branch_recovery_invert only to id_ex_t, immediately before instr so the existing instr/predicted_taken/valid tail layout remains unchanged. Preserve all external IO, retirement width and other bundles.'},\n {'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'At the existing accepted OF/EX payload capture edge, register ctrl.branch_op[0] XOR predicted_taken into the new polarity bit. Keep reset, stall holds, immediate flush validity, operand forwarding and every existing payload enable unchanged.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Compute direct prediction mismatch from each base relation and the saved combined polarity, independently of the actual-condition selection. Retain actual branch condition/training, use the exact misalignment fallback to captured predicted_taken, and preserve all acceptance, target, divider, forwarding and architectural gates.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'Extend ID_EX packing with the new bit at its declared location. Add directed EX verification cases covering all six branch relations, both predictions, equality, signed/unsigned extremes, target traps and held instructions. Preserve every existing divider arithmetic, exact-latency, reset and held-result assertion.'},\n {'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'Check atomic capture of combined polarity with branch controls and prediction, preservation under stalls, reset clearing and validity kills. Retain existing forwarding age, x0, load-use and operand-isolation checks.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Keep the independent old-state predictor and immediate-recovery model unchanged. Extend relation coverage and inspect the saved polarity at accepted OF/EX transfers and holds. Check both mismatch directions, load/divide dependencies, queue occupancies, target iStalls, older dStalls, illegal/misaligned instructions, exact RVFI order/results/PCs and absence of wrong-path side effects.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Validated final hypothesis:',p)\np=Path('cores/bench/generated/r11_polarity')\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/test',p/'test',dirs_exist_ok=True)\nf=p/'test/test_ex_divider.py'; s=f.read_text().replace('(\\\"rd\\\", 5), (\\\"rs1_addr\\\", 5), (\\\"rs2_addr\\\", 5), (\\\"ctrl\\\", 22),','(\\\"rd\\\", 5), (\\\"rs1_addr\\\", 5), (\\\"rs2_addr\\\", 5), (\\\"ctrl\\\", 22), (\\\"branch_recovery_invert\\\", 1),',1); f.write_text(s)\nPY\npytest -q cores/bench/generated/r11_polarity/test/test_operand_stage.py cores/bench/generated/r11_polarity/test/test_ex_divider.py cores/bench/generated/r11_polarity/test/test_pipeline.py > cores/bench/generated/r11_polarity/tests.log 2>&1\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
