{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_74", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r13s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261004-003-r13s2',\n'title':'ID predecode registers one-hot conditions for prediction recovery',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz with 4,024,573 timed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior tagged-target, loop, return-shadow and history supplements saved less than one percent of cycles and lost Fmax; delayed training/squash, scalar recovery polarity and static target prevalidation also regressed. An unchanged-parent scratch Gowin run reproduces 69.480 MHz on option zero and its 19.498 ns comparator-to-OF path. Local payload-enable separation, counter re-encoding and operand-comparison summaries also lost frequency.\n\nA scratch prototype that registers complete one-hot prediction-failure conditions at OF/EX measures options 0/1/2 = 69.118/70.190/70.190 MHz, versus the champion's 70.381 MHz median. It retains exactly 4,024,573 cycles and passes warning-free lint, selftest and all three random-program RVFI cosims with and without stalls, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART validation and memory bounds. This is close to the parent but does not clear acceptance. Moving the same predecode into ID removes its class/polarity/alignment logic from the OF register input and acceptance cone, while retaining immediate EX recovery. It is a distinct complete one-hot verification predecode, rather than another scalar polarity or alignment-only change.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add a seven-bit recovery_mode to id_of_t and id_ex_t, before instr in each bundle so the existing instr/predicted_taken/valid tail stays intact. Compute recovery_mode in ID from the validated decoded branch_op, fetched prediction and exact PC-plus-B-immediate alignment; do not compare operands in ID or OF. Let aligned mean the low-two-bit PC-plus-immediate sum is zero, and invert = branch_op[0] XOR predicted_taken. For an aligned target select exactly one condition: BEQ/BNE select bit 0 for equal if invert=0 or bit 1 for unequal if invert=1; BLT/BGE select bit 2 for signed-less or bit 3 for signed-greater-or-equal; BLTU/BGEU select bit 4 for unsigned-less or bit 5 for unsigned-greater-or-equal. Other comparison arms are zero. Bit 6 is \"'!aligned && predicted_taken. Reserved comparison classes select no relation. This seventh bit preserves verification even for inconsistent prediction metadata: an unaligned direct target has effective direction zero.\n\nRegister this mode with its instruction in ID/OF under the existing payload !stall rule. OF only copies the matching mode into OF/EX at its existing accepted operand edge. Reset clears it with each bundle; holds preserve it, and flush kills validity exactly as today. Retain the original prediction bit for choosing the conditional recovery address. No IF/ID or queue metadata, stage, speculative history or deferred squash is added. The final extra state is fourteen bits, seven at each existing register boundary.\n\nIn EX form recovery_wrong as a balanced OR of the six masked ordinary full-width operand relations and bit 6. Consume these registered masks directly, bypassing actual branch_cond selection, branch-operation inversion, predicted-direction XOR and misalign_fault in conditional verification. Keep the existing outer ex_accept && !is_illegal && is_branch qualification and unchanged aligned JALR recovery arm. Do not move acceptance, qualify producer eligibility differently or alter wide payload enables. For aligned legal branches this equals branch_cond XOR predicted_taken; for an unaligned direct target it equals predicted_taken. The actual branch_cond case remains unchanged for architectural taken status, trap checks, actual RVFI pc_next and accepted table training. JAL/JALR targets, bit-zero clearing, PC+4 links and trapping-link suppression remain exact.\n\nRetain immediate prediction-selected correction addresses, same-edge queue discard and both younger-stage validity kills. Keep the folded-PC 64x2 bimodal table, local Boolean saturation, weakly-taken reset, raw aligned/legal BRANCH/JAL predecode, old-state lookup and every existing training event. Preserve arithmetic, EX-only divider launch/consume, forwarding, load-use bubbles, all bus acceptance/hold rules, WB provenance, decoder legality, nret=1 ports, strict RVFI order, symbolic progress and every evaluation invariant. This is one predictor-verification retiming hypothesis.\n\nThe intended gain is frequency with identical predictions, recovery latency and benchmark cycles. Six percent is a low-confidence forecast for the final ID-predecoded design, not an observed improvement from the OF prototype. The unchanged divider and placement may prevent any gain. Acceptance at unchanged cycles requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 73.62 MHz and fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec. Require all scored placement options and unchanged lint, unit, formal, RVFI cosim, canonical five-CRC/UART, bounds and MMIO-bracket checks on the final implementation.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add seven-bit recovery_mode to ID/OF and OF/EX before instr, retaining all architectural/RVFI bundles, the existing low-order bundle tails and the exact nret=1 external interface.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Predecode complete one-hot prediction-failure conditions from decoded branch class, exact PC-relative alignment and fetched prediction. Register them atomically with the ID/OF instruction under existing reset, hold and validity-kill rules. Preserve default-illegal decoding.'},\n {'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'Copy recovery_mode from the matching ID/OF word into OF/EX at the existing accepted payload edge, with no comparator or additional mode-generation logic here. Preserve operand selection, x0, load-use, acceptance, reset, holds and kills.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Use the balanced masked-relation OR for conditional prediction verification under unchanged accepted/legal/branch qualification. Preserve actual condition and training, immediate correction, recovery targets, traps, JALR, links, producer gates, arithmetic and actual RVFI PCs.'},\n {'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'Update ID/OF and OF/EX packing. Check mode capture for back-to-back instructions, invalid words, resets, holds and flushes, retaining all operand, age-priority and x0 assertions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'Update packed OF/EX inputs with independently derived recovery_mode. Check all six branch types, both predictions, all target low-bit combinations, signed/unsigned extremes, illegal/bubble inputs and EX stalls. Preserve every real/ALTOPS arithmetic and divider protocol assertion.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Update packed-bundle observations for both added fields and independently check ID mode generation. Preserve exact predictor/training/correction schedules, RVFI PCs/results/order, alignment traps and wrong-path memory/divider suppression under queue occupancy, load/divide dependencies, reset and independent bus stalls.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Final ID-predecode hypothesis written and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
