\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the combinational EX result path into one\\nregistered, unsigned-magnitude quotient/remainder engine. Use a restoring\\nshift/subtract recurrence with eight quotient bits computed per clock:\\neight bit steps are unrolled combinationally and reused for four clocks,\\nrather than cascading all 32 steps in one clock. Register operand\\nmagnitudes and sign flags at launch, then restore\n…[24124 of 27196 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f5690b8f5c820432]…\n // ID/EX register:\n    //   - dmem_stall  -> hold        (preserve in-flight pipeline state)\n    //   - load_use    -> bubble      (1-cycle stall between LOAD + use)\n    //   - redirect    -> bubble      (kill wrong-path)\n    //   - otherwise   -> capture\n    // dmem_stall takes precedence over load_use's bubble: re-evaluate\n    // load_use next cycle when the bus unblocks. flush_id is 1 only when\n    // we want bubble (not hold).\n    stall_id      = dmem_stall || load_use_hazard || div_wait;\n    flush_id      = (load_use_hazard || redirect) && !dmem_stall && !div_wait;\n    // EX/MEM register: holds on dmem_stall (LOAD waits in MEM until the\n    // bus delivers).\n    stall_ex_mem  = dmem_stall;\n    // MEM/WB register: on dmem_stall the previously-retired instruction's\n    // data fields stay alive for forwarding (e.g. a held BNE needs the\n    // LOAD's load_data via fwd_mem_wb), but valid is cleared so we don't\n    // double-retire / double-write the regfile.\n    hold_mem_wb   = dmem_stall;\n  end\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
