{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"if test -f cores/bench/LESSONS.md; then cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md; fi\nrg -n 'predictor|hyp-20261004-003-r[12]s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Fetch-time bimodal prediction removes taken-branch bubbles\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current core always fetches PC+4 and flushes the younger instruction\\non every taken conditional branch or jump, even for stable CoreMark loop\\nbranches. IF/ID is combinational, so steering the PC when an instruction\\nis accepted into ID/EX can supply its predicted successor without adding\\na pipeline stage. A small direction-only predictor avoids a tagged target\\narray and should reduce benchmark cycles while leaving the dominant\\ncombinational M-extension timing path structurally unchanged. The local\\nhistory has only the baseline and no prior predictor attempts or lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current core always fetches PC+4 and flushes the younger instruction\\non every taken conditional branch or jump, even for stable CoreMark loop\\nbranches. IF/ID is combinational, so steering the PC when an instruction\\nis accepted into ID/EX can supply its predicted successor without adding\\na pipeline stage. A small direction-only predictor avoids a tagged target\\narray and should reduce benchmark cycles while leaving the dominant\\ncombinational M-extension timing path structurally unchanged. The local\\nhistory has only the baseline and no prior predictor attempts or lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one compact fetch-time control-flow predictor: a 64-entry bimodal\\nbranch-history table of two-bit saturating counters, indexed by PC[7:2]\\nand reset to weakly not taken (01). Predecode only legal RV32I conditional\\nbranches and JAL from the raw fetched instruction. For a conditional\\nbranch, use the counter MSB as the direction; predict JAL taken without\\nconsulting the table. Form direct targets from PC plus the B/J immediate,\\nand predict only word-aligned targets. All other instructions, including\\nJALR, predict PC+4. Keep direction state only: no BTB, global history,\\nreturn stack, target cache, or instruction buffering.\\n\\nCarry the exact predicted next PC w\n…[19862 of 22934 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d2199e845cf6557b]…\nr busy/result consumption,\\nand directed/random imem/dmem stalls. Assert exact retired PC chains,\\nRVFI order and source/link values, no wrong-path stores, and one\\ntraining/recovery event per accepted instruction. Retain all existing\\nassertions and run unchanged formal/cosim and CoreMark CRC gates.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 75.18, \"delta_pct\": 5.07, \"vs_baseline\": 520.3, \"fmax_mhz\": 31.556, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4197517, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4475, \"ff\": 960, \"seeds\": [31.781, 31.556, 31.556], \"perturbations\": [[0, 31.781, 47], [1, 31.556, 47], [2, 31.556, 47]], \"lutram\": 96, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/divisor_q_1_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_0_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -26.465, \"arrival_ns\": 36.759, \"logic_cells\": 242, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 47, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T14:46:30.605621Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"Both prior predictors passed correctness checks and cut CoreMark cycles by about 6.5%, but their Fmax gains were insufficient. The champion’s worst path now crosses branch recovery logic. I’ll propose a direction-only predictor with one-bit mismatch detection to remove taken-branch bubbles without adding a wide next-PC comparison."}}
