{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|hyp-20261004-003-r[123]' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Fetch-time bimodal prediction removes taken-branch bubbles\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current core always fetches PC+4 and flushes the younger instruction\\non every taken conditional branch or jump, even for stable CoreMark loop\\nbranches. IF/ID is combinational, so steering the PC when an instruction\\nis accepted into ID/EX can supply its predicted successor without adding\\na pipeline stage. A small direction-only predictor avoids a tagged target\\narray and should reduce benchmark cycles while leaving the dominant\\ncombinational M-extension timing path structurally unchanged. The local\\nhistory has only the baseline and no prior predictor attempts or lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current core always fetches PC+4 and flushes the younger instruction\\non every taken conditional branch or jump, even for stable CoreMark loop\\nbranches. IF/ID is combinational, so steering the PC when an instruction\\nis accepted into ID/EX can supply its predicted successor without adding\\na pipeline stage. A small direction-only predictor avoids a tagged target\\narray and should reduce benchmark cycles while leaving the dominant\\ncombinational M-extension timing path structurally unchanged. The local\\nhistory has only the baseline and no prior predictor attempts or lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one compact fetch-time control-flow predictor: a 64-entry bimodal\\nbranch-history table of two-bit saturating counters, indexed by PC[7:2]\\nand reset to weakly not taken (01). Predecode only legal RV32I conditional\\nbranches and JAL from the raw fetched instruction. For a conditional\\nbranch, use the counter MSB as the direction; predict JAL taken without\\nconsulting the table. Form direct targets from PC plus the B/J immediate,\\nand predict only word-aligned targets. All other instructions, including\\nJALR, predict PC+4. Keep direction state only: no BTB, global history,\\nreturn stack, target cache, or instruction buffering.\\n\\nCarry the exact predicted next PC w\n…[50474 of 53546 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3fe74b0e29baf1aa]…\n crcstate=8e3a, crcfinal=fcaf and \\\"Correct operation validated.\\\" with\\n  the unchanged 2K, -O3, ITERATIONS=10 benchmark and random bus stalls.\\n\\nMeasured final Gowin/fitness result (NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench):\\n- Placement Fmax: option 0 = 48.264 MHz; options 1 and 2 = 47.603 MHz.\\n- Median Fmax = 47.603 MHz.\\n- Marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles = 4,201,709, iterations = 10.\\n- Fitness = 113.29 iterations/second, versus champion 108.26 (+4.65%).\\n- Area: 3123 LUT4/logic, 772 FF, 8 LUTRAM, 6 BSRAM, 6 DSP.\\n\\nConcern: fitness clears the required 113.24 margin by only 0.05. The\\ncycle savings are present, but median Fmax is below the champion's\\n48.625 MHz. Final acceptance still depends on the orchestrator's unchanged\\ncorrectness and vendor timing gates. The first indexed-update table\\nimplementation measured 47.199 MHz / fitness 112.33; local counter updates\\nimproved that result without changing instruction timing or prediction.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T15:08:02.062892Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
