{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"The earlier direction predictor saved about 290,000 CoreMark cycles, but its timing cost left it near the acceptance margin. The tagged target predictor saved only about 4,000 more cycles and used much more storage. I’m focusing on conditional-branch accuracy with a compact gshare predictor, retaining the earlier one-bit recovery logic."}}
