{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_58", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r6s2.yaml');h=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='One-bit registered predictor squash preserves immediate PC recovery'\nh['hypothesis']='''Split predictor recovery into immediate fetch-PC correction and a\none-bit registered squash event. Keep the existing accepted EX\nconditional direction-mismatch decision and preselected target.\nDrive only IF's fetch-PC update from that immediate decision: reset\nwins, an accepted PC redirect installs its target even if imem stalls,\notherwise an accepted fetch installs its predicted successor. Register\nthe accepted recovery pulse for one clock before it controls queue\noccupancy, head selection, decode arbitration and younger-EX killing.\nDo not add a second target register or a mux on io_imemAddr: the\nordinary PC register already contains the corrected target during\nthe registered squash cycle. Preserve its current full 32-bit address.\n\nDuring that following cycle, ignore all old queue entries and offer\nthe instruction at the corrected PC directly to ID. Its old younger\nEX instruction is invalidated on the same edge. If the target word\nis available and decoded, clear queue occupancy and advance PC to that\nword's predicted successor. If available but unconsumed, retain it as\nthe sole new head and advance PC once. If imem is stalled, clear the\nold queue and keep the corrected PC for retry. Permit the target word\ninto ID/EX instead of flushing it. Thus target acceptance and every\nbranch/JALR-to-DIV retirement gap match the immediate-recovery parent;\nthe registered squash introduces no extra recovery bubble.\n\nKill the younger EX instruction by gating next EX/MEM validity, not\nby clearing or holding its entire wide payload. Continue capturing\ndummy invalid payload fields through the ordinary pipeline path, as\nallowed by the existing validity contract. Also suppress its divider\nlaunch/wait, branch training and recovery generation. A wrong-path\nload must not create a load-to-MUL hold for the fresh target word.\nNever let a killed instruction issue a memory request, become a\nforwarding producer, write a register, train the table or retire.\nThe older resolving control transfer already in EX/MEM continues\nnormally, including its link write and actual RVFI next PC. Preserve\nolder MEM/WB writes and held-WB forwarding. Capture a squash event\nonly on actual EX advance after older memory backpressure clears;\nclear pending validity on reset and on the following no-event cycle\nso it cannot repeat. An active squash suppresses a younger event.\n\nKeep the existing 64x2 folded-PC bimodal predictor, weakly-taken reset,\nlocal Boolean saturation, exact aligned BRANCH/JAL predecode and\npredicted_taken capture. Train at the existing EX boundary, with only\nthe extra qualification excluding the killed younger EX instruction.\nDo not pipeline training or add a target table, return stack, history,\ncache, arithmetic change or retirement stage. Preserve all decoder\nlegality and alignment traps, actual RVFI operands/targets/links,\nnret=1 IO, +1 retirement order, symbolic liveness, bus handshakes,\ncanonical CoreMark CRC/UART and bounds checks.\n\nThe intended timing gain comes from removing the live load comparator\nfrom queue-head decode, queue payload enables and younger-ID control,\nwhile retaining only its immediate PC update and accepted training\nendpoints. A broader local prototype with a registered target and\nfetch-address mux matched 3,829,487 canonical cycles and passed stalled\nselftest plus all three random-program cosims, but its timing regressed.\nThat evidence motivates this narrower one-bit control split and\nvalidity-only kill; it does not establish a fitness improvement.\nAcceptance still requires fitness above 140.78114, or approximately\n53.914 MHz median Fmax at unchanged cycles. The unchanged divider and\ninteger datapath may prevent that gain; confidence is low. Evaluate\nall placement options and unchanged correctness gates.'''\nh['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'}\nh['changes'][0]['description']='''Export the existing immediate accepted PC redirect separately from\na one-clock registered squash pulse. Suppress younger EX recovery,\ntraining and divide launch/wait during squash. Kill only EX/MEM\nvalidity through the ordinary payload-capture path. Preserve branch\ncomparison, preselected target, arithmetic, RVFI and forwarding.'''\nh['changes'][1]['description']='''Use immediate EX recovery only for the existing PC-register update.\nUse registered squash to bypass the old queue head with the word at\nthe corrected PC and clear obsolete occupancy on the next edge.\nConsume or retain exactly the available recovery-target word, and\nadvance its predicted successor only on acceptance. Preserve the\nbimodal table and direct io_imemAddr connection to registered PC.'''\nh['changes'][2]['description']='''Use registered squash to admit the fresh target word, excluding\nholds from the killed younger load or divide. Preserve genuine\nolder-memory backpressure and ordinary load-to-MUL arbitration.\nKeep immediate PC correction independent of decode/queue controls.'''\nh['changes'][3]['description']='''Wire immediate PC redirect/target only to IF PC correction and the\nregistered squash pulse to IF queue recovery and decode arbitration.\nKeep top-level ports, single-channel retirement and WB provenance.'''\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=80))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261004-003-r6s2'\nprint('Final one-bit-squash hypothesis written and schema-validated.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
