{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'predictor|return.address|\\\\bras\\\\b|\\\\bbtb\\\\b|gshare|history' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Fetch-time bimodal prediction removes taken-branch bubbles\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current core always fetches PC+4 and flushes the younger instruction\\non every taken conditional branch or jump, even for stable CoreMark loop\\nbranches. IF/ID is combinational, so steering the PC when an instruction\\nis accepted into ID/EX can supply its predicted successor without adding\\na pipeline stage. A small direction-only predictor avoids a tagged target\\narray and should reduce benchmark cycles while leaving the dominant\\ncombinational M-extension timing path structurally unchanged. The local\\nhistory has only the baseline and no prior predictor attempts or lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current core always fetches PC+4 and flushes the younger instruction\\non every taken conditional branch or jump, even for stable CoreMark loop\\nbranches. IF/ID is combinational, so steering the PC when an instruction\\nis accepted into ID/EX can supply its predicted successor without adding\\na pipeline stage. A small direction-only predictor avoids a tagged target\\narray and should reduce benchmark cycles while leaving the dominant\\ncombinational M-extension timing path structurally unchanged. The local\\nhistory has only the baseline and no prior predictor attempts or lessons.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add one compact fetch-time control-flow predictor: a 64-entry bimodal\\nbranch-history table of two-bit saturating counters, indexed by PC[7:2]\\nand reset to weakly not taken (01). Predecode only legal RV32I conditional\\nbranches and JAL from the raw fetched instruction. For a conditional\\nbranch, use the counter MSB as the direction; predict JAL taken without\\nconsulting the table. Form direct targets from PC plus the B/J immediate,\\nand predict only word-aligned targets. All other instructions, including\\nJALR, predict PC+4. Keep direction state only: no BTB, global history,\\nreturn stack, target cache, or instruction buffering.\\n\\nCarry the exact predicted next PC w\n…[176832 of 179904 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6dcca0fb5722a617]…\n fetch lookahead, source dependencies, traps, changed instructions at a learned PC and independent bus stalls. Verify accepted training provenance, both recovery directions, absence of wrong-path side effects, exact RVFI operands/targets/links/order and unchanged liveness requirements.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 129.99, \"delta_pct\": -3.42, \"vs_baseline\": 972.52, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.614, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3816810, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4037, \"ff\": 1114, \"seeds\": [46.115, 49.614, 49.614], \"perturbations\": [[0, 46.115, 18], [1, 49.614, 18], [2, 49.614, 18]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.685, \"arrival_ns\": 26.98, \"logic_cells\": 18, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_mem\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 18, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T17:50:45.872234Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
