benchmark address constants or target truncation.\n  For legal aligned conditional branches, an exception valid/tag hit\n  overrides the base only when confidence is at least two. Otherwise use\n  the base direction. Keep existing raw legality/alignment predecode,\n  exact direct targets, unconditional JAL prediction and EX-only JALR\n \n…[4728 of 7800 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a6271e1e38eccf69]…\ncontext independently across all queue occupancies,\n      enqueue/dequeue/bypass combinations, holds, recovery and later history\n      or tag replacements. Preserve existing acceptance assertions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise correlated branches, competing contexts and both override\n      recovery directions with independent bus stalls and wrong-path stores\n      or divides. Verify exact RVFI PCs, source/results/order and one update\n      per accepted nontrapping branch. Update bundle parsing and the model\n      while preserving correctness and retirement-latency bounds.\n  - file: test/test_ex_divider.py\n    description: |\n      Update standalone packed-bundle construction and new training outputs;\n      retain all real/ALTOPS arithmetic, launch, stall and latency checks.\n  - file: test/test_operand_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Update bundle packing and assert context capture/hold/flush alongside\n      the existing independent operand-forwarding and interlock checks.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
