{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The history shows competing limits in the multiplier and divider; recent branch-control changes have regressed. I’m focusing on a single-cycle multiplier rewrite that shares the signed and unsigned arithmetic while preserving instruction latency."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses; python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r14s0',\n 'title':'Shared single-cycle limb multiplier with carry-save sign correction',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz with 4,024,573 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The champion and several recent regressions have worst paths from OF operand registers through the signed or unsigned multiplier toward EX/OF capture. alu.sv currently expresses three separate full-width products for signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned and signed-unsigned results, using six DSP resources. Prior branch-comparator and capture-enable rewrites regressed, and the two-stage multiplier attempt regressed with an extra dependent-multiply bubble. A local combinational multiplier rewrite can reduce duplication and arithmetic depth while preserving the champion's producer schedule.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace only the real multiplication network in alu.sv with four shared unsigned 16x16 limb products and a carry-save reduction that incorporates high-half sign corrections before its single final carry-propagate addition. Keep multiplication combinational and retain the exact existing normal EX forwarding, instruction latency and all pipeline boundaries. MUL reads the low half, MULHU reads the uncorrected high half, MULH subtracts b from the unsigned high half when a[31] is set and subtracts a when b[31] is set, and MULHSU subtracts only b when a[31] is set. These identities hold modulo 2\"'^32 for the high half. Infer portable native DSP multiplication; do not instantiate vendor primitives or change the flow.\n\nLet p00=a_lo*b_lo, p01=a_lo*b_hi, p10=a_hi*b_lo, p11=a_hi*b_hi, each explicitly unsigned 32 bits from 16-bit inputs. The low sixteen product bits equal p00[15:0] and bypass reduction. In the remaining 48-bit coordinate system, the unsigned terms are zero_extend(p00[31:16]), zero_extend(p01), zero_extend(p10), and {p11,16'\"'b0}. Use explicit carry-save XOR/majority compressors, with carry shifted left by one modulo 2\"'^48. Add the necessary sign-correction terms in this same compressor tree, not with serial subtractors after the product. For MULH/MULHSU with negative a add {~b,16'\"'b0} and the correction carry at coordinate bit 16; for MULH with negative b likewise add {~a,16'b0} and a carry at coordinate bit 16. Mask each correction term and its carry by its matching operation/sign condition. The sum of the two correction carries is representable as a two-bit count at coordinate bits 17:16. Balance the fixed compressor tree to minimize dependent levels; finish with one explicitly sized 48-bit addition. Assemble the product as {reduced48,p00[15:0]} and select the architectural half. Corrections have zero low sixteen coordinate bits, hence cannot alter the original low thirty-two product bits. Ensure every term is widened before shifting.\n\nPreserve SEPARATE_MUL_OPERANDS so no live MEM/RF bypass enters the multiplier. Keep the original standalone ALU interface and COMBINATIONAL_DIV behavior, all exact RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas and constants, RV32I arithmetic, the six-RUN divider, forwarding priority, load-use bubble, WB provenance, reset/hold/redirect semantics, illegal/trap discipline, nret=1 IO, RVFI order and symbolic-progress bounds. Do not change any correctness or evaluation file. This is one combinational arithmetic sharing/reduction optimization, without a new multicycle unit, stage or interlock.\n\nThe gain forecast is low confidence: Gowin DSP inference, compressor routing and the unchanged divider may limit Fmax. At unchanged cycles, acceptance requires median vendor Fmax above approximately 73.62 MHz and fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec. Require exact multiplication tests, real and ALTOPS builds, unchanged formal and stalled RVFI cosim gates, canonical five CRCs and UART literal, memory bounds and MMIO timing. A proposed gain is not an observed fitness measurement.''',\n 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n  {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Replace three real full-width products with four shared unsigned 16x16 limb products, a balanced explicitly sized 48-bit carry-save tree including masked high-half sign corrections, and one final carry-propagate sum. Bypass product bits 15:0 and preserve every interface, ALTOPS expression and nonmultiply operation.'},\n  {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Extend independent exact-result MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU checks across all operand sign pairs, 16-bit limb carries, all-ones and INT_MIN patterns, zero and power-of-two operands, and randomized full-width values. Check original and SEPARATE_MUL_OPERANDS modes with differing live a/b versus captured mul_a/mul_b and retain all existing arithmetic assertions.'},\n  {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add dependent and back-to-back mixed multiply-high/low chains, both-source matches, x0 and younger-writer priority under independent bus stalls and redirects. Verify unchanged single-cycle EX producer availability, exact RVFI source/result/order fields and wrong-path side-effect suppression without weakening existing checks.'}\n ]\n}\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r14s0.yaml')\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h, sort_keys=False, width=100))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote and schema-validated', p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
