{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_23", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r14s0.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nh['title']='One shared native signed multiplier with opcode-selected extension bits'\nh['motivation']='''The champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz with 4,024,573 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The champion and several recent regressions report timing paths through the multiplier toward OF capture. alu.sv expresses three separate full-width signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned and signed-unsigned products using six DSP resources. Branch-comparator and capture-enable rewrites regressed, while the earlier two-stage multiplier added a dependency bubble and also regressed. A scratch four-limb multiplier with carry-save sign correction passed arithmetic and pipeline tests but lost frequency: median 59.570 MHz despite reducing DSP use to three. This proposal instead removes the duplicated native multiplier networks without adding a LUT compressor tree or a new pipeline boundary.'''\nh['hypothesis']='''Replace the three real MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU product expressions in alu.sv with one native 33x33 signed multiplication. Give each source one explicit extension bit: A33 = {signA,product_a}, B33 = {signB,product_b}; signA = product_a[31] && (op == ALU_MULH || op == ALU_MULHSU), signB = product_b[31] && op == ALU_MULH. Declare both operands signed [32:0] and their common product signed [65:0]. MUL and MULHU thus multiply two zero-extended nonnegative operands; MULH sign-extends both, and MULHSU sign-extends only A. Select common_product[31:0] for MUL and common_product[63:32] for the other three operations; bits 65:64 are redundant extension bits. Explicit casts and widths must preserve those signed interpretations. Multiplication stays combinational; infer the vendor's native DSP multiplier from portable SystemVerilog rather than constructing a LUT partial-product tree or requiring vendor primitives.\n\nThe extra source bit allows all four architectural results to share one multiply operator. Only the two extension bits depend on opcode, with all 32 original source bits wired directly to the shared arithmetic. Avoid an opcode-controlled 32-bit magnitude mux or a serial post-product sign-correction adder. This reduces the number of large DSP cones and their input/result routing. It preserves the exact normal EX producer schedule and aims to improve Fmax at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n\nKeep SEPARATE_MUL_OPERANDS so the core's multiply inputs remain the registered OF/EX values and standalone instances retain their original a/b interface. Leave every RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS multiply expression and constant exact; the real shared product must be eliminated from that verification elaboration if unused. Preserve COMBINATIONAL_DIV and every nonmultiply ALU operation, all six CPU stages, single issue, nret=1 ports, the six-RUN real/ALTOPS divider and handshake, operand forwarding and age priority, load-use behavior, memory backpressure, WB provenance, branch recovery and training, legality/alignment traps, exact RVFI operands/results/order and symbolic progress. No stage, interlock, completion register, bus behavior or evaluation/check relaxation is included.\n\nAn eight-percent gain is a low-confidence forecast. The native 33-bit extension may map less efficiently than 32-bit modes, and the unchanged divider remains a competing limit. Acceptance at unchanged cycles requires median vendor Fmax above approximately 73.62 MHz and fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec. Require exact multiplication tests, real and ALTOPS builds, unchanged formal and stalled RVFI cosim gates, canonical five CRCs and validation literal, bounds and MMIO timing. The failed limb prototype is evidence for rejecting that implementation, not a fitness measurement for this native design.'''\nh['changes'][0]['description']='Replace three separate real 64-bit multiplication expressions with one explicitly signed 33x33 native product, opcode-selected extension bits, and exact low/high-half selection. Preserve the standalone and isolated-operand interfaces, all ALTOPS constants/formulas and every nonmultiply operation; infer native DSP arithmetic without extra stages or correction adders.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated native multiplier hypothesis')\nPY\ncat /srv/hwebench/tmp/e4e97874/b737a704/native33-tests.log; tail -12 cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/gw.log\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
