{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"The signedness-register variant reached 68.804 MHz, still below the champion. The reports also exposed another path: load alignment is checked through the general ALU result, which brings multiply-high arithmetic into load-use control. I’m testing a two-bit load-address calculation to remove that dependency."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r14s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r14s0',\n 'title':'Compute load alignment directly before load-use hazard qualification',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz with 4,024,573 timed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Recent branch-comparator, operand-capture-enable and divider-bank changes regressed. ex_stage computes load_misalign from the general alu_result low bits even though valid legal loads always use rs1+immediate. Consequently the timed producer_load/load_use/frontend-hold cone structurally includes every ALU output, including multiply-high bits, despite loads never selecting those operations. Scratch shared-multiplier variants passed arithmetic/pipeline checks but regressed; their detailed vendor paths explicitly traverse multiplier output into frontend control. Removing the irrelevant arithmetic from load alignment is a smaller local change with no extra stage or cycle cost.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Change only EX's alignment predicate used to qualify producer_load. Independently compute load_addr_low = in.rs1_val[1:0] + in.imm[1:0] as an explicitly two-bit modulo-four sum. For a word load, load_misalign is load_addr_low \"'!= 0; for a halfword load it is load_addr_low[0]; a byte load is always aligned. Use the existing mem_width encoding and keep producer_load'\"'s ex_accept, valid/legal, and mem_read qualification exactly as today. The actual effective address remains the existing 32-bit ALU ADD result in EX/MEM. A valid legal load is decoded to ALU_ADD with rs1 and immediate operands, so this low-two-bit sum is exactly the alignment of that address, including carries and 32-bit wraparound. The halfword predicate can simplify to XOR of rs1[0] and imm[0]. Never use an OR or compare the operands independently: carries across bit zero matter for word alignment.\n\nThis replaces only an unnecessary dependence on the general result mux with an independent tiny address calculation. In particular MULH/MULHU/MULHSU high-half bits, shifter results, comparison outputs and normal result selection can no longer feed load-use stalls through load_misalign. Preserve the actual load bubble, trap suppression and dmem request semantics. The MEM stage remains the authority for alignment traps and RVFI; do not alter its full-address checks, memory masks, trap control or data extraction. Aligned EX loads still block their dependent OF consumer for one cycle, and misaligned/trapped loads never become valid forwarding producers. Preserve use_rs1/use_rs2, source x0, younger-writer priority and simultaneous matches.\n\nKeep all pipeline stages and payload/valid enables, branch prediction/recovery/training, multiplier and six-RUN divider arithmetic, real/ALTOPS formulas and schedules, accepted producer timing, EX-only divide launch, independent bus stalls, retained WB provenance, reset/redirect priority, default-illegal decoding, EBREAK-only SYSTEM behavior, nret=1 top-level IO, strict RVFI order, exact operands/results and symbolic progress. Do not add a new stage, precomputed architectural address, forwarding route, register bank or correctness/evaluation relaxation. This is one combinational dependency removal in the existing load-use qualification, not early load execution.\n\nA six-percent gain is a low-confidence forecast rather than an observed fitness improvement. Unchanged branch and divider paths may become the limit. At identical cycles acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 73.62 MHz and fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec. Validate every scored placement option, existing formal and stalled RVFI cosim gates, exact alignment/source/producer tests, canonical five CRCs and UART validation literal, memory bounds and MMIO timing.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Replace alu_result-dependent load_misalign used by producer_load with the independent explicitly sized modulo-four sum of registered rs1 and immediate low bits. Preserve all acceptance/legality/producer gates, actual ALU and effective-address logic, traps, redirect, division and forwarding interfaces.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'Add direct EX load-alignment and producer_load checks for all sixteen low-bit operand pairs, byte/halfword/word widths, signed/wrapping immediates, legal aligned/misaligned loads, rd=x0, invalid/illegal inputs and EX stalls. Retain exact arithmetic, divider protocol and branch assertions; use load payloads with independently decoded ADD/immediate controls.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Exercise aligned and misaligned loads with nonzero low bits in both rs1 and immediate, dependent ALU/branch/store/divide consumers, both-source matches, older WB matches and arbitrary independent bus stalls. Preserve full RVFI address/mask/trap/source/result/order checks, wrong-path suppression, one-cycle load bubbles and all existing correctness assertions.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote and schema-validated load-alignment hypothesis')\nPY\ncat /srv/hwebench/tmp/e4e97874/b737a704/alignment-tests.log; tail -6 cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/gw.log\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
