{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"The alignment bypass measured 69.372 MHz, so it did not clear the acceptance threshold. I’m now checking a local divider optimization: its two reused body cells process at most 28 and 30 dividend bits, but currently use 35-bit trial subtractors. Narrower trials can preserve exact results if oversized divisor multiples are rejected explicitly."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r14s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r14s0',\n 'title':'Bound shared divider body trials to their maximum dividend-prefix widths',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz with 4,024,573 timed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. The divider body remains a competing critical path in recent vendor timing reports. The engine processes ten bits before its five four-bit body clocks and thirty bits before terminal publication. Nevertheless both reused body cells use the full 34-bit window and 35-bit subtractors required only by the terminal cell. Earlier borrow-lookahead/carry-select and fifteen-trial radix-16 changes regressed; spatial width-specific divider banks also regressed and introduced additional launch/control timing. This proposal retains the two shared native-carry cells and removes only provably unnecessary high arithmetic bits, without adding phases or operand banks.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Specialize only the two combinational radix-4 body cells in div_unit.sv to static maximum window widths W=28 for the first cell and W=30 for the second. Before the final body clock the divider has processed twenty-six dividend-magnitude bits; its first and second cells therefore produce twenty-eight and thirty processed bits respectively. Earlier body clocks have smaller prefixes. Starting from zero remainder, the restoring remainder never exceeds the processed dividend prefix, including division by zero, so no body window can exceed these bounds. Preserve the full 32-bit Q/R registers and existing bootstrap/body state mux and enables. This is width reduction inside the existing reused recurrence, not spatial stage unrolling.\n\nFor each body cell form the unsigned W-bit window T={R[W-3:0],Q[31:30]}. For each full 34-bit multiple M in D,2D,3D, subtract {1'b0,M[W-1:0]} from {1'b0,T} using one native W+1-bit unsigned subtraction. Its bit W is the local borrow. A trial is successful iff every M[33:W] bit is zero AND that borrow is zero. This high-multiple eligibility check is mandatory: a large full multiple whose low W bits look small must never become an accepted subtraction. Keep D,2D and registered 3D at their present full widths and preparation edge. Do not generate truncated multiples with narrow arithmetic. Derive digit bits and the existing four mutually exclusive masks from these exact success predicates. Restore the W-bit remainder with the same masked-OR selection of T and low-W trial differences, zero-extend it into the existing 32-bit state and append the unchanged two quotient bits. Explicitly separate the W=28 and W=30 elaborations, e.g. constant-width generate blocks, so synthesis sees 29-bit and 31-bit native trial carry chains instead of 35-bit chains. No custom carry-select network or serial comparator/subtractor is added.\n\nLeave launch, six-bit bootstrap, group count and five body clocks exact. Leave the independent terminal two-bit trials full width: their window can contain all thirty-two dividend bits, and D/2D/3D must retain all high bits. Preserve terminal signed-result candidates and held READY publication. Real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS builds retain the identical six-RUN schedule, formulas and constants. The launch-time four-bit prefix and registered bootstrap multiples stay unchanged. Maintain division-by-zero results, signed remainder sign, INT_MIN/-1, rejected starts, consume/relaunch and reset cancellation. At each boundary verify the remainder bound with independent arithmetic checks; never weaken a latency or arithmetic assertion.\n\nKeep the rest of the parent circuit unchanged: EX-only launch from OF/EX operands, all producer and payload enables, normal/divide forwarding, branch prediction/recovery/training, load-use bubbles, arbitrary bus stalls, WB provenance, multiplier and ordinary ALU, legality/alignment traps, nret=1 IO, exact RVFI operands/results/order and symbolic progress. Do not add state, pipeline stages, phase-indexed data selection or change any evaluation contract.\n\nThe expected gain is shorter native borrow propagation in both dependent body cells at identical instruction and CoreMark cycles. Six percent is a low-confidence forecast; the high-bit eligibility reduction, terminal publication and unchanged EX-to-OF path may prevent acceptance. At unchanged cycles acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 73.62 MHz and fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec. Validate every scored placement option, exact real/ALTOPS divider tests, unchanged formal and stalled RVFI cosim, canonical five CRCs and UART validation literal, bounds and MMIO timing.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'Replace only the two full-width shared body digit calls with statically elaborated W=28/W=30 trial subtractors, mandatory full-multiple high-bit eligibility checks, existing digit/mask equations and zero-extended restored remainders. Preserve full-width divisor multiples, state registers, launch/bootstrap/terminal logic and exact real/ALTOPS schedules.'},\n {'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'Add independent integer-reference vectors around 2\"'^28 and 2''^30 trial-eligibility boundaries for D,2D,3D, including oversized multiples with misleading low bits, all radix-4 digits, every body phase, all-ones dividend, zero divisor and signed extrema. Check body window/remainder bounds independently and retain all arithmetic, exact six-clock latency, held READY, rejected-start, reset and consume/relaunch assertions.'\"'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Add divide/rem-to-consumer chains with boundary and large divisors, signed cases and zero divisors under independent memory stalls and redirects. Retain exact RVFI fields/order, eight-cycle consecutive-divide retirement, ten-cycle progress, forwarding age priority and wrong-path divider/side-effect checks.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Wrote and schema-validated bounded body hypothesis')\nPY\ncat /srv/hwebench/tmp/e4e97874/b737a704/bounded-tests.log; tail -8 cores/bench/generated/timing/gowin_p0/gw.log\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
