{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"agent_message","text":"Removing the duplicate RF bypass saved 130 LUT4s but measured 68.517 MHz. I’ll make the final hypothesis an unmeasured ALU decode change: register one-hot result-selection masks in the existing ID/OF and OF/EX bundles, then use them directly in EX. This targets late opcode decoding without changing arithmetic units or instruction timing."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_51", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r14s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r14s0',\n 'title':'Register one-hot ALU result selection before the execute boundary',\n 'category':'micro_opt',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz with 4,024,573 marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Prior micro_opt forwarding-select, branch-comparison, capture-enable and arithmetic rewrites regressed. Local scratch shared multipliers, narrowed divider trials and redundant RF-bypass removal also failed to clear the threshold; even saving four DSPs or 130 LUT4s did not improve clock frequency. Detailed timing repeatedly exposes EX-result/control-to-OF paths, including paths starting at the registered five-bit ALU opcode. The current scalar opcode is decoded in the live EX result-selection cone before forwarding and load alignment. Moving that decode into an earlier existing register boundary targets a concrete logic dependency, while retaining the parent's arithmetic networks, forwarding topology and clock schedule.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Predecode the ALU result selector once in ID and carry nineteen one-hot operation masks through the existing ID/OF and OF/EX bundles. Define mask bit k to select ALU operation value k, for the existing ALU_ADD=0 through ALU_REMU=18 constants. ID computes this mask from the already validated decoder's dec_alu_op and registers it with the same instruction under the existing payload \"'!stall rule. Invalid or illegal words may carry the decoder'\"'s default ADD mask but retain their original validity and default-illegal control; a mask never authorizes retirement, a producer or a side effect. Preserve the scalar alu_op field for divider operation/sign decoding, ALTOPS operation discrimination and every existing control gate. Do not recode the architectural decoder or replace its default-illegal rules.\n\nAdd the mask before the existing ctrl/instr/prediction/valid tail in id_of_t and id_ex_t, so those established low-order fields keep their bit offsets. OF only copies the matching ID/OF mask at its unchanged accepted operand-capture edge; no opcode decode or comparator is added to OF. Reset clears mask state with each existing bundle, holds retain it and validity kills retain their existing priority. Exactly thirty-eight extra selector bits are carried across two existing boundaries; no new stage, skid entry, architectural latency or additional interlock is introduced.\n\nExtend alu.sv with a default-false USE_PREDECODED_SELECT parameter and a nineteen-bit select input. Default standalone instances derive equivalent masks locally from scalar op, retaining their current public combinational behavior. In the core set USE_PREDECODED_SELECT=true and connect the registered OF/EX masks from ex_stage. For this mode use each mask directly as the enable of its existing 32-bit arithmetic result and combine terms with an explicitly balanced masked-OR tree. Do not feed the scalar opcode back into the final result mux. ADD/SUB, logic, signed/unsigned comparisons, three shifts, LUI, the three existing native products and the divide-result path retain their current arithmetic and signedness; do not consolidate products, add partial-product compressors, alter barrel-shifter structure or change division. MUL reads the existing unsigned low product, and MULH/MULHU/MULHSU select the existing exact high products. For each of the four divide/rem selectors use the existing div_result. In ALTOPS builds keep every existing formula and constant exact, and gate its result with the corresponding mask. A zero mask produces zero, and all legal decoded instructions carry exactly one mask. Keep COMBINATIONAL_DIV and SEPARATE_MUL_OPERANDS behavior unchanged.\n\nThis is one local decode-retiming optimization: operation-result qualification is registered before EX instead of decoding the five-bit opcode after OF/EX. The final reduction must be balanced, not a procedural priority chain, and no broad one-hot rewrite of forwarding, branch recovery, producer acceptance or payload enables is included. Keep the parent pipeline's EX-only divider launch, six-RUN real/ALTOPS schedule, normal/divide producer timing, load bubbles, retained WB provenance, all memory handshakes, prediction/training/recovery and alignment traps. Preserve nret=1 top-level IO, strictly increasing RVFI order, exact source/result/PC/memory fields, EBREAK-only SYSTEM legality, symbolic progress and every evaluation/correctness gate.\n\nAn eight-percent fitness gain is a low-confidence forecast for this final, unmeasured circuit. The earlier scratch circuits are rejected alternatives and provide no validation or fitness claim for these masks. Additional selector flops/routing and the unchanged divider or branch comparator may prevent acceptance. At identical cycles acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 73.62 MHz and fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec. Require every scored placement option plus unchanged real/ALTOPS unit, formal and stalled RVFI cosim gates, exact canonical five CRCs and UART validation literal, memory bounds and MMIO timing. Decode-mask tests must compare against an independently computed scalar ALU reference and exercise instruction/mask association across stalls, reset and redirects.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add nineteen-bit alu_select fields to ID/OF and OF/EX before the existing ctrl/instr/prediction/valid tails. Keep scalar alu_op, every architectural field and all top-level/RVFI interface types intact.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Compute one-hot ALU result selection from the validated decoded operation and register it with the ID/OF instruction under existing reset, payload hold and validity-kill rules. Preserve the default-illegal decoder and every existing control signal.'},\n {'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'Copy the matching registered alu_select into OF/EX at the unchanged accepted payload edge. Retain all source resolution, forwarding masks, producer gates, x0, load-use logic, acceptance, holds and flush behavior.'},\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Add optional predecoded nineteen-bit selector interface with default scalar-op behavior. Replace final result qualification with directly enabled existing arithmetic terms and an explicitly balanced masked-OR reduction. Preserve native multiplier expressions, all ALTOPS formulas/constants, nonmultiply arithmetic, division parameters and isolated operand semantics.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Enable the ALU predecoded-selector mode and wire registered in.alu_select. Preserve scalar-op divider decoding, actual arithmetic, EX/MEM payload, producer qualification, alignment traps, redirect/training and all divider ownership/handshake logic.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain existing scalar-interface arithmetic tests and add parameterized predecoded-mode tests with independent exact scalar reference results for all nineteen operations, signed extrema, random operands, zero masks and captured multiplication operands. Assert legal selector one-hotness and ALTOPS formula equivalence without weakening real arithmetic checks.'},\n {'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'Update packed ID/OF and OF/EX layouts and independently verify selector propagation alongside operands and instruction identity across accepted edges, invalid words, reset, stalls and flushes. Retain all forwarding age-priority, x0, exact operand and load-use assertions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'Update packed OF/EX payloads with independently derived selectors and preserve every exact arithmetic/divider/branch assertion. Exercise all ALU operations and matching selector/op association, stalls, reset and captured operands in real and ALTOPS builds.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Check decoded selector one-hotness and operation correspondence across back-to-back instruction classes, independent bus stalls, load/divide dependencies and redirects. Preserve full RVFI source/result/PC/memory/order checks, wrong-path suppression, exact division latency and all existing correctness assertions.'}\n ]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261005-001-r14s0'\nassert h['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Wrote and schema-validated final one-hot ALU hypothesis')\nbackup=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/e4e97874/b737a704')\nfor name in ['core_pkg.sv','operand_stage.sv','ex_stage.sv','reg_file.sv','core.sv','div_unit.sv']:\n Path('cores/bench/rtl',name).write_text((backup/(name+'.original')).read_text())\nPath('cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv').write_text((backup/'alu.original.sv').read_text())\nPath('cores/bench/test/test_alu.py').write_text((backup/'test_alu.original.py').read_text())\nPath('cores/bench/test/test_ex_divider.py').write_text((backup/'test_ex_divider.py.original').read_text())\nprint('Restored all scratch RTL and test edits')\nPY\ngit status --short --untracked-files=all\ngit diff --exit-code -- cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/test\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
