n under existing reset, payload hold and validity-kill rules. Preserve the default-illegal decoder and every existing control signal.'},\n {'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'Copy the matching registered alu_select into OF/EX at the unchanged accepted payload edge. Retain all source resolution, forwarding masks, producer gates, x0, load-use logic, acceptance, holds and flush behavior.'},\n {'file':'rtl/alu.sv','description':'Add optional predecoded nineteen-bit selector interface with default scalar-op behavior. Replace final result qualification with directly enabled existing arithmetic terms and an explicitly balanced masked-OR reduction. Preserve native multiplier expressions, all ALTOPS formulas/constants, nonmultiply arithmetic, division parameters and isolated operand semantics.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Enable the ALU predecoded-selector mode and wire registered in.alu_select. Preserve scalar-op divider decoding, actual arithmetic, EX/MEM payload, producer qualification, alignment traps, redirect/training and all divider ownership/handshake logic.'},\n {'file':'test/test_alu.py','description':'Retain existing scalar-interface arithmetic tests and add parameterized predecoded-mode tests with independent exact scalar reference results for all nineteen operations, signed extrema, random operands, zero masks and captured multiplication operands. Assert legal selector one-hotness and ALTOPS formula equivalence without weakening real arithmetic checks.'},\n {'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'Update packed ID/OF and OF/EX layouts and independently verify selector propagation alongside operands and instruction identity across accepted edges, invalid words, reset, stalls and flushes. Retain all forwarding age-priority, x0, exact operand and load-use assertions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'Update packed OF/EX payloads with independently derived selectors and preserve every exact arithmetic/divider