{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nids=['hyp-20261004-001-r6s0','hyp-20261004-001-r9s0','hyp-20261004-002-r10s1','hyp-20261004-001-r11s0','hyp-20261004-002-r13s1']\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d['id'] in ids:\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-001-r6s0 Borrow-lookahead carry-select subtraction in the restoring divider\nReplace the monolithic subtraction in each of div_unit's five\nrestoring bit cells with an explicitly segmented borrow-lookahead,\ncarry-select subtractor. Keep the unsigned restoring recurrence,\noperand registers, six five-bit groups, terminal two-bit group,\nfused sign restoration, and exactly seven RUN clocks unchanged.\nThis is one combinational arithmetic optimization; no CPU stage,\npredictor, forwarding path, instruction latency or memory policy\nchanges are included.\n\nIn each bit cell form X={R[31:0],Q[31]} and subtract {1'b0,D}.\nPartition X[31:0] and D into four eight-bit blocks, numbered from\nleast significant to most significant. For block k compute in\nparallel a nine-bit local subtraction t0[k]={1'b0,X_k}-{1'b0,D_k},\nits generate bit g[k]=t0[k][8], and propagate p[k]=(X_k==D_k).\nSet incoming borrow b[0]=0 and form b[1] through b[4] with explicit\nbalanced prefix generate/propagate equations, not a dependent chain\nof four general-purpose arithmetic operators. The final low-word\nborrow is b[4]. Because the subtrahend's bit 32 is zero, the true\n33-bit borrow is !X[32] && b[4]; this formula must also handle X[32]=1.\nDo not infer a signed comparison or silently drop X[32].\n\nFor upper blocks compute the eight-bit alternative difference\nt1[k]=X_k+(~D_k), modulo 256, alongside t0[k]. This is subtraction\nwith an incoming borrow of one. Select each block's low difference\nfrom t0[k][7:0] or t1[k] using its prefix-derived b[k]; block zero\nneeds only t0[0]. Build the accepted low 32-bit difference from\nthose four selected blocks. Restore R_next to X[31:0] on true\nborrow, otherwise use that low difference; append !borrow to the\nquotient. Expose independent per-block signals or an acyclic helper\nmodule so synthesis can retain short native carry chains and parallel\nprefix logic. No full-width subtraction may remain in a restoring\ncell, and do not serialize t1 after t0 with an increment/decrement.\n\nPreserve the existing signed-magnitude \n…[20565 of 23637 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f39d7d50b6fcb821]…\nMHz, 5,298 LUT4s and 1,245 FFs. It passed all 31\npipeline tests, eight EX tests and the real-divider arithmetic suite;\ncanonical stalled CoreMark retained exactly 4,024,573 marker-bracketed\ncycles, all five CRCs, the validation literal and no out-of-bounds access.\nIts approximately 0.88% fitness gain is below acceptance. Local operand\nand eligibility banks are therefore essential to this final proposal;\nthe final banked circuit is unmeasured, and no acceptance is claimed.\nA separate capture-control variant regressed and is excluded.\n\nAn eight-percent fitness improvement is a low-confidence forecast; extra\nrouting, local-bank setup paths and the unchanged EX-to-OF path may\nlimit the benefit. Require the final median Gowin Fmax times canonical\nmarker-bracketed iterations/cycle above 182.92448 iter/sec, approximately\n73.62 MHz at unchanged cycles. Validate all real/ALTOPS divider tests,\npipeline tests, unchanged formal/cosim gates, every CRC, UART literal,\nmemory bounds and all scored placement options.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
