{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor row in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(row)\n if r.get('category')=='structural':\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  h=h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n  print('\\\\nID:',r['id'],'OUTCOME:',r.get('outcome'),'FITNESS:',r.get('fitness'))\n  print(h)\n  print('PATH:',r.get('critical_path'))\n  print('NOTES:',r.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID: hyp-20261004-002-r1s1 OUTCOME: improvement FITNESS: 71.55\nMove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the combinational EX result path into one\nregistered, unsigned-magnitude quotient/remainder engine. Use a restoring\nshift/subtract recurrence with eight quotient bits computed per clock:\neight bit steps are unrolled combinationally and reused for four clocks,\nrather than cascading all 32 steps in one clock. Register operand\nmagnitudes and sign flags at launch, then restore quotient sign from\nrs1-sign XOR rs2-sign and remainder sign from rs1. Reserve at most seven\nclocks from accepted launch to result availability, including setup and\nsign restoration; keep the zero-wait retirement gap within the unchanged\nten-cycle liveness window, including pipeline transfer cycles. Use the\nsame bounded handshake latency in ALTOPS mode, substituting only the\narithmetic value with the exact existing formal formulas. Do not hide a\nslow real divider behind a faster formal-only completion path.\n\nLaunch exactly once for a valid legal divide in ID/EX when the older MEM\ninstruction can advance. Capture the forwarded operands and their RVFI\nvalues before holding the instruction, since forwarding sources can\ndisappear while older instructions drain. Hold PC and ID/EX during the\noperation; allow older EX/MEM and MEM/WB instructions to drain once,\ninserting EX/MEM bubbles instead of repeatedly issuing the old instruction.\nExisting dmem backpressure must still hold an outstanding memory request.\nRetain a completed division result until EX/MEM accepts it, then publish\nit exactly once through the normal forwarding, writeback, and single\nchannel RVFI paths. Qualify redirects and side effects with valid and\nactual stage advance so stalls cannot replay a branch or memory request.\n\nPreserve the existing alu unit-test interface with a constant elaboration\nparameter if needed: its default may retain combinational divide for\nstandalone tests, but the core must instantiate the no-combinational-divide\nvariant. No / or % hardware may remain reachable in the tim\n…[73377 of 76449 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ab93d31363d0070f]…\ntract file.\n\nForecast eight percent greater fitness with low confidence. Fewer\nglobal store-stall cycles must compensate for FIFO and arbitration\ntiming costs; loads after stores still serialize. The final store-queue\ncircuit is unimplemented and unmeasured. Alternative divider-lane and\nforwarding-topology scratch probes did not clear acceptance and are\nexcluded; no measured gain is claimed for this proposal. Require\nactual median Gowin Fmax times canonical bracketed iterations/cycle\nabove 182.92448 iter/sec. At unchanged Fmax that requires more than\n4.4 percent fewer cycles; with six percent fewer cycles the required\nFmax is approximately 69.20 MHz. Validate every unchanged formal/cosim\ngate, canonical CRCs, UART validation literal, memory bounds and marker\ndrain ordering before judging the scored placements.\n\nPATH: {'from': 'cpu/u_of/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu/mult_101_s1', 'slack_ns': -9.48, 'arrival_ns': 19.585, 'logic_cells': 40, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_of']}\nNOTES: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
