{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nids={'hyp-20261004-001-r5s0','hyp-20261004-002-r9s1','hyp-20261004-002-r10s1','hyp-20261004-001-r11s0'}\nfor row in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(row)\n if r['id'] in ids:\n  h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('\\\\nID',r['id'],'fitness',r['fitness'],'path',r.get('critical_path'))\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('NOTES',r.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID hyp-20261004-001-r5s0 fitness 124.31 path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -14.581, 'arrival_ns': 24.876, 'logic_cells': 17, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nReplace only div_unit's real restoring arithmetic with signed partial\nremainders and speculative pairs of non-restoring radix-2 steps.\nPreserve six five-bit groups, the final two-bit group, seven RUN clocks,\nall launch/consume semantics and the existing CPU pipeline. Each normal\ngroup uses two speculative two-bit cells followed by one ordinary\nnon-restoring bit cell; the terminal group uses the first pair alone.\nThis changes local combinational arithmetic and a few divider registers,\nwithout changing any instruction's latency or stall behavior.\n\nCapture unsigned divisor magnitude D and a 33-bit two's-complement\n-D at launch. Use a signed 33-bit partial remainder R initialized to\nzero, so all unsigned divisors through 0xffffffff are representable.\nOne non-restoring step with dividend bit b computes\nR1=2R+b+(R<0 ? D : -D), and emits quotient bit !(R1<0).\nKeep the recurrence in explicitly sized 33-bit modular arithmetic.\nFor D nonzero its selected result stays in [-D,D), so bit 32 is the\ncorrect sign even when an intermediate shifted value wraps.\n\nFor a pair with incoming bits b1,b0 let S=4R+2*b1+b0 modulo 2^33.\nIn parallel compute the ordinary first-step R1 and both possible\nsecond-step results:\n  N = S + (R<0 ? 3D : -D);\n  P = S + (R<0 ? D : -3D).\nSelect R2 = R1<0 ? N : P and append the two quotient bits\n{!(R1<0),!(R2<0)}. Derive both N and P directly from incoming R and\nthe two dividend bits, not by doubling the just-computed R1.\nThe first-step sign and two second-step candidates therefore traverse\nparallel carry chains. A pair has one dependent arithmetic depth plus\nselection, rather than two serial arithmetic depths. Use precomputed\n+/-D and +/-3D registers and two candidate adders per pair; avoid\nexpanding into four complete second-step adders, which increases\n\n…[18271 of 21343 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f23d55961040b9c3]…\ny ALTOPS formula and completion edge unchanged. Keep\ntop-level nret=1 IO, decoder default-illegal rules, alignment\ntraps, load interlocks, wrong-path suppression, held-WB provenance,\nexact eight-cycle divide spacing and ten-cycle progress bound.\n\nExtend independent divmod arithmetic checks with all sixteen body\ndigits, transitions around each kD, quotient nibbles spanning body\nboundaries, high unsigned divisors, all signs, zero divisors and\noverflow. Require existing real/ALTOPS divider, EX and pipeline\nsuites, unchanged formal gates and canonical stalled CoreMark\nCRCs, validation text, address bounds and marker timing. Inspect\nvendor timing for body, preparation, bootstrap and terminal paths\nand verify resource fit. Added trial/multiple routing and the\nunchanged terminal/OF paths are the main risks. At unchanged cycles,\nacceptance requires median Fmax above approximately 73.619 MHz\nand fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec. The ten-percent forecast\nis a hypothesis until final all-placement vendor timing.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
