{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_17", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor row in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(row)\n h=r.get('hypothesis',{})\n h=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n if re.search(r'shared.*multipl|multipl.*shar|33.bit.*product|partial.product multiplier',h,re.I|re.S):\n  print(r['id'],r.get('title'),r.get('fitness'),r.get('critical_path'))\n  for paragraph in h.split('\\\\n\\\\n'):\n   if re.search(r'multipl|product|DSP',paragraph,re.I): print(paragraph)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261004-001-r1s0 Share a radix-4 combinational divider across RV32M divide and remainder 13.32 {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -171.709, 'arrival_ns': 182.003, 'logic_cells': 483, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_rf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nKeep the alu module interface, zero-cycle combinational latency,\nmultiplication, RV32I operations, forwarding, stall handling, pipeline\nregisters, decoder legality, and nret=1 contract intact. Preserve every\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expression exactly. Explicitly return all ones for\ndivision by zero and the original dividend for remainder by zero;\npreserve DIV(INT_MIN,-1)=INT_MIN and REM(INT_MIN,-1)=0. Signed remainder\ntakes only the dividend's sign. Do not introduce FPGA-specific divider\nprimitives or change the evaluation flow. The expected gain comes from\nshortening the existing arithmetic path, with no extra CoreMark cycles.\n\nhyp-20261004-002-r2s1 Fold the divider to five bit steps per clock with a fused final partial group 108.26 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_0_s100', 'slack_ns': -17.02, 'arrival_ns': 27.314, 'logic_cells': 48, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id']}\nThis is one structural folding and retiming change. Its expected fitness\ngain comes from reducing the measured divider register-to-register path,\nwith two additional execution clocks only on divide/remainder\ninstructions. The final sign path or the existing multiplier may become\nthe next clock limit, so a twofold Fmax increase is not assumed. Validate\nexact arithmetic and identical real/ALTOPS completion schedules, all\nexisting formal/cosim checks, the unchanged ten-cycle retirement bound,\nand canonical CoreMark CRCs under random memory stalls. Score the final\ncircuit with median Gowin Fmax times marker-bracketed iterations/cycle.\n\nhyp-20261004-002-r3s1 Separate live load forwarding from registered multiplier operands 113.92 {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/quotie\n…[15967 of 19039 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b33c753cfaa181f4]…\n combined with its saved eligibility.\nThis is one structural divider change: a feedforward chain of distinct\nprefix stages with local registered arithmetic operands replaces shared\nrecurring state, feedback selection and stationary divisor fanout.\nLeave OF capture, accepted EX producer qualification, branch recovery,\nprediction, memory execution and multiplication exactly as in the parent.\nA scratch spatial prototype using stationary shared multiples measured\n67.274/71.000/71.000 MHz, 5,298 LUT4s and 1,245 FFs. It passed all 31\npipeline tests, eight EX tests and the real-divider arithmetic suite;\ncanonical stalled CoreMark retained exactly 4,024,573 marker-bracketed\ncycles, all five CRCs, the validation literal and no out-of-bounds access.\nIts approximately 0.88% fitness gain is below acceptance. Local operand\nand eligibility banks are therefore essential to this final proposal;\nthe final banked circuit is unmeasured, and no acceptance is claimed.\nA separate capture-control variant regressed and is excluded.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
