{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_84", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-002-r15s1',\n 'title':'Asymmetric divider with one radix-8 body digit per clock',\n 'category':'structural',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.88 iter/sec at 70.381 MHz and 4,024,573 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent vendor reports repeatedly identify divider feedback as a clock limit. Each body clock crosses two serial full-width radix-4 subtract/select cells. Extra execution clocks threaten the unchanged ten-cycle progress bound, so repartitioning existing work is preferable.\n\nRead the structural history: r10s1 successfully introduced the six-RUN EX-only asymmetric engine; r13s1 spatial divider banks regressed to 166.95; r11s1's staged multiplier regressed to 159.50. Relevant arithmetic attempts include r11s0's fifteen-trial radix-16 body (161.35) and r8s0's serial radix-4/radix-8 groups. Neither tried one radix-8 body digit with enough narrow bootstrap work to preserve the current completion edge. LESSONS.md does not exist. Scratch multiplier-sharing, narrowed-feedback and alternating-bank probes in this proposal turn also failed to clear the champion and are excluded. A seven-trial reused body removes one dependent full-width cell with much less parallel hardware than radix-16.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Restructure only div_unit into four bits at launch, ten additional narrow bootstrap bits on the first RUN edge, five single-digit radix-8 body clocks and independent terminal three-bit publication. Exactly 4+10+5*3+3=32 bits are processed. Preserve accepted EX launch L, RUN edges L+1..L+6, READY after L+6 and EX/MEM consumption at L+7. This is one structural folding and work-repartition hypothesis, retaining the six CPU stages and nret=1.\n\nAt L retain the existing four-bit prefix computation, low twenty-eight dividend-magnitude bits, full divisor magnitude and sign/op flags. Replace the bootstrap's captured ten-bit multiples with explicitly nineteen-bit odd multiples j*m, odd j=3..31. Here m is b[13:0] for unsigned/positive b, or (14'd0-b[13:0]) modulo 2\"'^14 for negative signed b. Capture these directly from OF/EX operand flops independently of prefix trials. Derive even multiples by shifts of captured odd multiples or m and powers of two by wiring. Size every shift/add before evaluation. Generate each odd multiple independently using shifts/adds/subtracts; compress three or more summands with carry-save logic before a final carry addition. Do not cascade newly computed multiples. These truncated-divisor multiples are ignored when full D exceeds fourteen bits.\n\nAt L+1 consume ten bits using two specialized radix-32 cells, each appending five quotient bits. The first window contains at most nine prefix bits, so use a nine-bit window and ten-bit differences; the second contains at most fourteen, so use a fourteen-bit window and fifteen-bit differences. For width w, trial j=1..31 succeeds only if every nineteen-bit multiple bit above w-1 is zero AND the zero-extended w+1-bit T-multiple subtraction has no borrow. Do not truncate large multiples into eligible trials. Set ok[0]=1, ok[32]=0 and mask[k]=ok[k]&&!ok[k+1]. Select the original window for k=0 or its matching difference for k>0 using disjoint masks and balanced OR trees, and encode the five quotient bits from masks without serial priority selection. The second cell reads only the first restored nine-bit remainder and the next five dividend bits. If divisor_q[31:14]!=0, instead append ten quotient zeros and concatenate old R4 with the next ten dividend bits. Otherwise use the two cells. Register Q={old_Q[21:0],ten_new_bits} and zero-extended R14. D=0 must emit two digits of 31 and reconstruct the prefix as remainder.\n\nIn parallel at L+1 register full unsigned thirty-five-bit 3D=D+(D<<1), 5D=D+(D<<2), and 7D=(D<<3)-D, with D widened before all operations. Prepare each independently from captured D; their arithmetic has no path into bootstrap trials. Derive 2D,4D,6D by wiring shifts of D or registered 3D. No full-width multiple preparation belongs in launch or recurring feedback.\n\nOn groups one through five, L+2..L+6, reuse exactly one radix-8 cell. Form unsigned thirty-five-bit T={R,Q[31:29]} and seven zero-extended thirty-six-bit T-jD differences. No-borrow bit 35 gives ok[j], with ok[0]=1 and ok[8]=0. Use eight masks ok[k]&&!ok[k+1], balanced masked OR remainder selection and three-bit quotient encoding; register Q={old_Q[28:0],digit} and the selected low thirty-two remainder bits. For D>0, R<D implies T<8D and restored R<D. Preserve full multiple high bits. For D=0 all trials succeed, digit seven is selected and R reconstructs the dividend. The body therefore has one dependent wide carry chain instead of two, with seven trials rather than radix-16'\"'s fifteen.\n\nAfter L+6 twenty-nine bits are processed. An independent terminal radix-8 bank reads held Q/R directly and processes the last three bits, without a body-output or phase-state mux. Prepare all eight signed architectural result candidates before the late trial masks. For constant k=0..7, positive remainder is (T-kD)[31:0], negative remainder is (kD-T)[31:0], and positive quotient is {held_Q[28:0],3'(k)}. For k>0, negative quotient is {~held_Q[28:0],(3'd0-3'(k))}; for k=0 use {(29'd0-held_Q[28:0]),3'b000}. Captured operation/sign flags select within each candidate before the balanced masked OR publication. No selected digit drives a subsequent wide negate or operation mux. Retain READY state and result through delayed consume and preserve simultaneous standalone consume/relaunch semantics.\n\nKeep the exact ALTOPS formulas and identical six-RUN schedule; never give formal a faster completion. Preserve divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, dividend-only remainder sign and zero-divisor suppression of quotient negation. Reset cancels ownership and initializes preparation registers; every accepted launch overwrites each bank before use. Reject starts while busy. Keep EX-only captured operands/RVFI metadata, single publication, older-stage draining, dmem stall priority, forwarding age, load-use bubbles, branch recovery, alignment traps, decoder default-illegal and EBREAK-only SYSTEM checks, nret=1 IO, strict retirement order and every invariant. No multiplier, predictor, memory-stage or evaluation-contract change is included.\n\nValidate actual real and ALTOPS engines against independent integer divmod, all body digits 0..7 and bootstrap digits 0..31, widths around 2\"'^9 and 2''^14, full-D bypass, overflowing multiple guards, every terminal digit/negation carry, all signs and corner cases. Retain exact six-RUN completion, eight-cycle consecutive-divide retirement, ten-cycle symbolic progress, reset/hold/relaunch assertions and all unchanged formal/RVFI cosim gates. Require canonical CoreMark CRCs, UART validation, memory bounds and marker bracketing. Inspect vendor paths through launch preparation, both narrow cells, body and terminal-to-OF publication.\n\nForecast eight percent fitness improvement with low confidence. This final radix-8 circuit is unimplemented and has no vendor timing measurement; the failed scratch circuits do not support an acceptance claim. The thirty-one-trial narrow bootstrap, nineteen-bit launch preparation, larger terminal bank and competing multiplier path are significant timing/area risks. At unchanged 4,024,573 CoreMark cycles, acceptance requires median Gowin Fmax above approximately 73.62 MHz and fitness above 182.92448 iter/sec. Score all placements and actual bracketed iterations/cycle without weakening any gate.'\"''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'Repartition launch/bootstrap/body/terminal work as 4/10/15/3 bits. Capture nineteen-bit bootstrap odd multiples at launch and full 3D/5D/7D at first RUN. Use specia